The meeting was held in order to further strengthen the relationship and cooperation between the two countries, especially to promote cooperation and investment in halal industry in Cambodia, one of the largest industries in the world.
Also at the meeting, Senior Minister Osman Hassan informed the Sri Lankan Minister of Industry that after the end of the civil war, Cambodia had rapidly developed its country, which had maintained economic growth for more than 20 years at around 7%. He also stressed that Cambodia encourages and promotes all forms of investment to further enhance the economy between the two countries.
Buddika Pathirana welcomed the visit of Senior Minister Osman Hassan and his delegation to the Socialist Democratic Republic of Sri Lanka and pledged to further strengthen and deepen cooperation between the two countries.
(Phnom Penh): The International Cycling Federation (UCI), a world-class cycling organization, has selected Cambodia to host the "World Cycling in Coastal Areas" event from January 4-6, 2020. Coming soon. This is according to Mr. Vath Chamroeun, Secretary General of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia.
Mr. Vath Chamroeun said this after the meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission to organize the World Cycling Event on the coast of Cambodia at the Ministry of Tourism on the morning of August 27, 2019, chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism.
Mr. Vath Chamroeun said that this world event is organized in collaboration with the Ministry of Tourism, the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia (NOCC), the Cambodian Cycling Federation, the World's Most Beautiful Beach Club and the International Cycling Federation (UCI).
He said that the three days of the world-class cycling event will pass through Koh Kong, Kampot, Kep and Sihanoukville, Cambodia's coastal provinces, which are divided into three stages, including:
* Phase 1: On January 4, 2020, the first departure from Darasakor Tourist Resort will pass through Say Phu Thong Roundabout (located in Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province) towards Khemarak Phoumin (Koh Kong Provincial Town) which is a long distance. A total of about 135 kilometers.
* Phase 2: On January 05, 2020, depart from Say Phou Thong roundabout, cross Sre Ambel junction to Veal Renh roundabout (located in Prey Nob district, Sihanoukville province) and continue to Thansur Bokor resort, Kampot province. There is a total distance of about 170 kilometers.
Mr. Vath Chamroeun said that the World Cycling Event in the coastal area of Cambodia is also a support for Cambodia in preparing for the 2023 SEA Games, which means that it will contribute to encourage more Cambodian athletes and people. Play a lot of sports training to increase their ability and reach any sport to be ready to participate in the upcoming 2023 SEA Games.
He added that this cycling event will also provide technical assistance to the Cycling Federation of Cambodia, which is actively training to prepare to participate in various racing events, especially the upcoming SEA Games.
According to Mr. Vath Chamroeun, for the Cambodian team, it is a new experience to participate in this world sports event, because in the past, Cambodia has only participated in national, regional events or championships in some countries, namely Never competed in the International Cycling Federation calendar program like this.
Please be informed that in the above meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission, the focus was on the issue of roads and races that are being damaged in some areas, such as the road from Khemarak Phoumin to the Sre Ambel roundabout, the road from Sihanoukville through Veal Renh. To Kampot, as well as congestion in Sihanoukville, however, Minister Thong Khon also urged to speed up repairs and resolve the event as soon as possible.
