Kampong Speu Provincial Civil Society and Administration Forum Meets with Civil Society Organizations in Kampong Speu Province
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Kem Rath Viseth, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Civil Society Forum, and Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, presided over a forum with civil society organizations in Kampong Speu province this morning. August 27, 2019 at Kampong Speu Provincial Hall.
The forum was held under the theme "Strengthening Cooperation between Civil Society Organizations and the Royal Government to Achieve the Sustainable Development Goals within Cambodia", including the participation of representatives of departments and units under the provincial hall, including representatives of trade unions. And communities in many provinces.
The Dialogue was organized by the Civil Society Alliance Forum (CSF) in collaboration with Kampong Speu Provincial Administration with the aim of promoting civil society organizations to better understand and understand the Sustainable Development Goals of Cambodia 2030 and establish A closer and more effective partnership with stakeholders and the Royal Government to contribute to the successful achievement of the 18 development goals by 2030.
The forum also provided an opportunity for civil society organizations to openly discuss with relevant authorities and provincial administrations some practical challenges and suggestions to find appropriate solutions together.
At the same time, he urged all civil society organizations to pay high attention to the performance of their duties, to adhere to political neutrality, and to fulfill their roles, duties and legal obligations in force. Registration at relevant ministries and institutions, including proper tax registration, so that civil society organizations can receive various tax incentives.
