The Royal Academy of Cambodia is holding a roundtable discussion on "Proceedings and Partnerships of Banking and Microfinance Institutions in Cambodia" tomorrow.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 28, 2019, tomorrow, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will hold a roundtable discussion on "Proceedings and Partnerships of Banking and Microfinance Institutions in Cambodia". The discussion will take place at the Confucius Institute auditorium of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The Round Table Discussion of the Royal Academy of Cambodia will be attended by: Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, National Bank of Cambodia Cambodia and representatives of the Cambodian Microfinance Association.
The reason for holding this roundtable discussion after the recent positive and negative views on the role and partnership of banking institutions and microfinance institutions in Cambodia in socio-economic development, in particular. Cases of human rights violations, such as forced sale of land, exploitation of child labor, and migration, are linked to the operations of banks and microfinance institutions.
