(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, praised the efforts of firefighters as well as all relevant authorities in their efforts to put out the fire in Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh.
On the afternoon of August 23, 2019, a large fire broke out in a large mattress production handicraft in Phnom Penh, Group 4, Chamroeun Phal 1 Village, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey. The blaze destroyed three craft buildings, including a warehouse and a four- and six-story office building, as well as other items such as sewing machines, mattress cutters and injection molding machines. More than 3 million US dollars.
The firefighting operation used a total of 45 water trucks from various units such as the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Command, the 70th Brigade Command and the OCIC fire truck. Angkor Beer Company and Borey Peng Huoth. The firefighting operation used up to 261 units of water.
In addition to the fire brigade, the armed forces and many other local authorities participated in the operation with great care. Senior Minister Kun Kim, Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, arrived at the scene to direct the firefighting operation.
The firefighting operation lasted more than 16 hours, from the time of the incident at about 1:20 pm on the 23rd until 5 am on the 24th of January 2019. Although the fire in the building could not be extinguished, firefighters tried to prevent the blaze from spreading to nearby homes.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, through Fresh News on the night of August 26, 2019, highly appreciated and appreciated the efforts of firefighters and all relevant authorities in the firefighting operation.
"We are very sorry for the fire. But we are amazed at the firefighters and our authorities who did their best to put out the fire. "Although we did not successfully extinguish the blaze, we prevented the flames from spreading to nearby homes." Senior Minister Kun Kim confirmed.
During the firefighting operation, there were also some comments that the capacity of firefighters is still limited, which led to the firefighting operation was not successful and had to sit and watch the flames of the building. The rest.
Senior Minister Kun Kim dismissed the allegations. Mr. Kun Kim claimed that the Cambodian firefighters were competent in the firefighting operation, but could not put out the flames that burned the mattress craft due to the geographical conditions, the fire trucks were difficult to enter and put out the fire. Mattress is a substance that burns, spraying water is not easy to extinguish.
Please note that until August 26, 2019, law enforcement forces are continuing to demolish the burning building. Another building has not yet been completely demolished, and the demolition operation will continue tomorrow. 200 Angkor students receive heritage education from APSARA Authority and partner organizations in 8 months
(Siem Reap): A total of 200 students at Srah Srang Primary School and Nokor Thom High School (located in Angkor area) received knowledge and training on heritage, which is conducted in collaboration with the Heritage Protection Organization and APSARA Authority. And philanthropists.
