He stated that for primary school students to teach the basics, what is heritage, what is heritage? By studying in class and studying at historical sites, museums and painting. High school students teach general introduction to history, archeology, anthropology and research methods that enable young people to conduct research and document themselves in their communities.
He added that in addition to target schools in heritage areas in the future, heritage education programs for children will expand to other areas.
She stated that the Heritage Support Organization will withdraw from Cambodia by establishing a new local organization led by Khmer children and maintaining the same vision, called the Khmer Cultural Heritage Organization.
Mr. Un Monita, Executive Director of Heritage Protection Organization, said that in 2018, Heritage Protection Organization cooperated with APSARA Authority regarding the heritage education program for children in Angkor area in order to train children in Angkor area who were born and raised here. Understand the cultural potential around you, there are many levels to understand, maintain, learn more and serve in this profession.
He stated that seeing the success of heritage education in Banteay Chhmar, therefore, the Angkor Heritage Protection Organization has initiated a heritage education program for children in the Angkor area, the training here is unique in Banteay Chhmar, Koh Ker, Sambo, Prey Kuk, etc.
