Authorities decided to completely close 2 gas stations in Russey Keo district at the request of the people
(Phnom Penh): The Joint Commission of Russey Keo District Administration has taken drastic measures to completely shut down the gas stations and install two car gas systems immediately without proper rules, that is, without a business license. .
The move comes shortly after local residents complained and asked the media to cover the high risk of radiation and negligence for fear of a fire.
The operation was led by Mr. Sorn Sophoan, Administrative Director of Russey Keo District, represented by Mr. Lin Nhok, Acting District Governor, and was attended by Khan Inter-sectoral Office, Khan Office of Industry and Handicraft, Khan Environment Office, Sangkat Chief, Village Chief and other relevant officials under the command of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sorn Sophoan, Administrative Director of Russey Keo District, confirmed that before reaching the decision to completely close the gas stations and install gas systems in two cars, according to the actual inspection from the relevant specialized offices, found See that apart from the location is not technically correct, there is no business license from the Ministry of Mines and Energy.
The administrative director of Russey Keo district also confirmed that in addition to the gas station and equipped with the gas system of the two cars, there is no business license and there is a high risk of radiation, which is extremely flammable. Icom and ID services are neglected for fear of fire, which could endanger people's property and lives.
