This was stated by Samdech Heng Samrin at the plenary session of the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) on the morning of August 26, 2019 in Thailand.
He told AIPA that parliamentary diplomacy and partnership are important factors in the current context to promote sustainable regional and global development. Samdech emphasized that no country is isolated without relations with other countries.
The National Assembly President said that AIPA must promote trade and investment, which is an important factor that AIPA should pay attention to, monitor and maintain its common position, support the multilateral system based on the principles of international law, respect Understanding and mutual benefit without interfering in internal affairs, sovereignty and territorial integrity are the foundations of lasting peace.
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) is the inter-parliamentary body representing the legislatures of the 10-member Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN): Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam and the Philippines. AIPA is a gathering of the voices of the people of the ASEAN Community to be an ASEAN partner in advancing the goals of a single ASEAN Community.
Samdech Heng Samrin continued that promoting sustainable development is a fundamental principle of the ASEAN Community and a key point of ASEAN to achieve a community with close integration in the future based on environmental principles.
The National Assembly President also asked AIPA to consider and pay attention to the issue of effective use of labor. He stressed that all countries in the region must pay attention to the implementation of social protection systems to ensure that all migrant workers, including their families, are protected by law and have access to public services without discrimination.
Please be informed that after the plenary session, the AIPA General Assembly will convene a series of meetings of its committees, including the Political Committee, which discusses terrorism, extremism, transnational crime, and the fight against corruption. The Women's Committee will discuss gender equality.
The Economic Committee will discuss many topics, such as promoting common economic development in ASEAN. Improving ASEAN cooperation in preparation for the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
The Cambodian parliamentary delegation led by Samdech Heng Samrin will join the committees. The presence of a high-level delegation of the Cambodian Parliament on the international stage is a fulfillment of the parliamentary diplomatic mission in contributing to the building of peace, social stability and sustainable development in the region and the world, as well as building the prestige of our parliament and our country. On the international stage as well.
