PRASAC Financial Institution creates a type of loan, providing loans without collateral
(Phnom Penh): PRASAC, the largest financial institution in Cambodia, has developed a type of loan that does not require collateral, with customers being able to borrow up to 6 million Riel or US $ 1,500 for up to 36 months to serve. To customer growth.
Say Sony, PRASAC's CEO, said the unsecured loans are available to small and group loans. This loan is very convenient because the customer does not need to have collateral, the interest rate is reasonable, the documents are not complicated and there is flexibility in repayment.
Mr. Sony also emphasized that PRASAC is an institution that adheres to the code of ethical lending and consumer protection principles. PRASAC is a private institution that contributes significantly to boosting the financial environment for Cambodians, especially in rural areas.
At the same time, Mr. Sony stated: "On behalf of the management and staff of PRASAC, we would like to express our deepest gratitude to the National Bank of Cambodia, all levels of authorities and stakeholders for their support and good advice. We would like to thank all the customers who have continued to use the services of PRASAC and wish all the customers success in all tasks and continue to grow together sustainably.
Vietnam's BIDC, through the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in early August, announced the sale of 26 properties of Keo Maly's company for about $ 7.2 million to seize the company's debt.
The company has appealed to the Court of Appeal to oppose the bank's sale of the bank. In a press release today, Ms. Keo Maly expressed regret over the bank's move and considered it an act of drowning customers.
"Every company always needs capital to expand its business, so the bank is an important partner," she said. For their own benefit, all banks in Cambodia have always been considerate of their customers. My company is willing to pay a principal of $ 7,850,744.73 and interest of $ 2,681,150.08, no fraudulent ideas. "Why Vietnam Bank BIDC has no understanding and drowns its customers."
