The President of the Civil Society Forum said that in the past few years, through the establishment of dialogue forums in the provinces, the capital has achieved remarkable positive results in the relationship between sub-national authorities, provincial authorities, districts, communes and Institutions involved with civil society organizations.
He added that in the past 25 capital-provincial dialogue forums, many challenges have been identified. So far, the atmosphere of dialogue has become more relaxed, resulting in closer friendships between sub-national authorities and civil society organizations, especially when operating in remote provinces. There are many communities involved.
Mr. Kem Rathviseth stated, "This is a result of pride and satisfaction with the positive results we have achieved, and this is what the government wants: a good working environment between civil society and the government." "This proves that the civil society sector in Cambodia is free, there is no pressure from any side."
