(Kampot): With only 4 months left, the 8th round of the 8th Sea Festival in Kampot Province is approaching, the Ministry of Tourism, Kampot Provincial Administration, representatives of relevant ministries, institutions, departments, units and the private sector met. See you again at Kampot Provincial Hall on the morning of August 26, 2019 under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot.
To prepare for this smooth tourism event, the Royal Government has decided to set up an inter-ministerial committee to prepare for the Sea Festival, with Minister Thong Khon as chairman, Mr. Chiao Tai as permanent vice chairman and relevant member institutions.
With the aim of making Kampot province more attractive, Minister Thong Khon introduced a number of recommendations to the subcommittee, including:
* To identify Kampot as a model province in the preparation of Food Street (Food Sreet), Mr. Thong Khon advised the team to speed up the preparation of the upcoming Sea Festival by organizing infrastructure in the area of Food Street. Arrange order, beautify the city, organize the area with sidewalks, beautify the porch, especially the area where there are houses from the French era, near the food street.
* While the construction of the Kampot tourist port is proceeding according to plan, the Minister urged the construction of a lighting road to the new tourist port to prepare for the transport of tourists.
* Regarding the plan to build a new Kampot beach, Minister Thong Khon advised to consider the preparation of a lot of sand, to provide some services, toilets, special security to ensure sustainability.
* To improve the quality of water transport tourism services, such as the need to set up a safe port on the Kampot canal, to have airbags for tourists to wear when cruising. Meanwhile, the water traffic police force must strengthen this work as well.
* He recommended that the authorities explain to the restaurant owners to list the food items and the price list of their services, to continue to improve food hygiene, to consider the provision of clean toilets. As for the problem of paper falling under the table, it must not be allowed to continue, the "No trash under the table in restaurants-canteen" campaign must continue.
* Increase the training of tour guides and further strengthen their capacity to meet the growing number of tourists who are turning to visit Kampot.
* Tourist resorts in Kampot must improve their services, have proper waste management, parking services. He said that any site that is related to history or historical site is requested by the province to redefine the geographical location to protect, preserve and develop well to request the Royal Government again through the competent ministry.
* Increase the construction of roads to some important resorts in the province, such as Phnom Kampong Trat, Phnom Chhnok, pepper plantation resort in the area of young animals.
* Prepare new tourist destinations on Koh Ses with an area of more than 500 hectares by arranging the transportation of tourists to protect the safety of tourists Must mobilize investment in this island to prepare a new tour package for the province Kampot. He praised the tourism potential of the island because it is close to Koh Tral, near the sea border with Vietnam.
