(Bangkok, Thailand): National Assembly President Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin informed the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) that parliamentary diplomacy and partnership are important factors in the current context to promote sustainable regional and global development.
This was stated by National Assembly President Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin at the plenary session of the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) on the morning of August 26, 2019 in Thailand. The Thai Parliament will host the 40th AIPA General Assembly from 25 to 30 August 2019 under the theme "Promoting Parliamentary Partnership for Sustainable Communities."
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) is the inter-parliamentary body representing the legislatures of the 10-nation Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN): Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam and the Philippines. AIPA is a gathering of the voices of the people of the ASEAN Community to be an ASEAN partner in advancing the goals of a single ASEAN Community.
