BANGKOK: As many as 200,000 Rohingya gathered in a refugee camp in Bangladesh on Sunday to mark the two-year anniversary of their escape from a violent crackdown. By the Myanmar military in Rakhine state. This is according to a quote from CNA on Sunday afternoon, August 25, 2019.
August 25, 2017 is the day that Rohingya militants attacked several Myanmar police outposts in Rakhine state bordering Bangladesh, killing 12 Myanmar security forces.
The Myanmar military has since launched a response campaign. Despite the Myanmar army claiming to target only Rohingya militants, the Rohingya people claim that the military and Buddhist groups in Rakhine state have carried out violent crackdowns on Rohingya Muslims. Overall.
Since that day, a total of about 740,000 Rohingya have left Rakhine State to join the estimated 200,000 Rohingya refugees who have fled earlier in the day. Refugee camp area in southeastern Bangladesh.
