Karate is a Japanese art that originated in Okinawa that focuses on hand and foot action techniques. Most of the styles of karate also include, for example, human activities, digging and hard work. Originally, there was a Chinese martial art, while Okinawa had a long history of relations with China in the past.
By 1930, karate had spread rapidly to Japan. After the end of World War II, karate became a global culture, with almost every karate film being made into a hugely popular Hollywood film, and in 1960 the word karate became a common word in the language. English and more languages.
