Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin Leads a High-Level Delegation of the Cambodian Parliament to Attend the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly in Thailand
AIPA is an inter-parliamentary body representing the legislatures of the 10 member countries of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN): Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam and the Philippines.
AIPA is a gathering of the voices of the people of the ASEAN Community as ASEAN partners in promoting the achievement of the ASEAN Community.
The General Assembly is held annually by the member countries in alphabetical order of the names of the countries in the Latin alphabet to organize. The Thai Parliament is hosting this year's AIPA General Assembly under the theme "Promoting Parliamentary Partnership for Sustainable Community Development."
During the General Assembly, there will be meetings of AIPA's specialized committees, such as the Executive Committee, the Women's Parliamentary Committee (WAIPA), the Political Committee, the Economic Committee, the Social Affairs Committee, the Organizing Committee, and meetings between AIPA and observer countries. .
The presence of a high-level delegation of the Cambodian Parliament on the international stage is a fulfillment of the Parliamentary diplomatic mission in contributing to the building of peace, social stability and sustainable development in the region and the world, and building the prestige of the Parliament and the nation in On the international stage as well. Preah Vihear Provincial Armed Forces cracked down on a drug case, arrested a suspect and confiscated 5 packages of drugs
