Please be informed that the case of the fire that broke out in the building of the 6-storey mattress factory in front of the Russian Hospital in Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh, the authorities can fully control, but until the night of August 24, 2019 Authorities are continuing to dismantle the collapsed building.
Major General Net Vantha, Director of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department of the National Police, told Fresh News that the fire was completely under control at 5 am, but so far the operation has not been completed. Still, continue to clean the premises, especially the piles where the building collapsed.
According to Major General Net Vantha, as of 4 pm on August 24, 2019, the police used 46 water trucks to come to the rescue using more than 300 water trucks. Of the authorities and private companies that have been working closely together since the first day of the incident.
The director of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department confirmed that the building affected by the fire had three locations and a large handicraft factory, of which two four-storey buildings, but one collapsed to the ground and the other cracked. Pieces. The six-story building did not collapse, and the handicraft factory was completely burnt down.
However, for on-site operations as of now, it is observed that the presence of Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management is directing with Mr. Pa Socheatvong, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor Phnom Penh, the leadership of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, the Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, as well as many other authorities and authorities.
