(Svay Rieng): Mr. Ros Pharith, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, instructed all district, commune / sangkat authorities in Svay Rieng Province to strive to provide better services to the people, both in terms of needs and requests, especially needs. Be fast and transparent.
Mr. ROS Pharith, Representative of Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, said so on the afternoon of August 23, 2019, when he chaired the closing ceremony of the refresher training course on how to record civil status and how to use birth record books. Marriage, death, and recent legal documents.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Yim Sam Ol, Deputy Director of the Civil Status Department of the General Department of Identification, Ministry of Interior, as well as a total of 169 registrar officers.
Mr. Ros Pharith instructed all participants to pay attention to complete and perform 6 important tasks when returning to work:
1: After gaining the knowledge of the registrar, you, the Deputy Governor of the District, keep the book in accordance with the civil registration procedures, such as having to sign the registrar before entering the commune to keep the book. The registrar used properly according to the instructions of the Ministry of Interior.
2. To pay attention to the registrar's work by urging the commune / sangkat through monthly meetings or supporting the commune / sangkat to provide the civil status certificate as required.
3: For you, the Commune / Sangkat Chief, please apply this knowledge to implement the registration of the census in accordance with the procedures and guidelines.
4: Before signing and stamping the registrar, fill in the data with the date of birth in Latin letters.
5. The used civil status book must be sent to the district by the beginning of January of the following year.
6: Do not commit any acts that are prohibited by the Civil Status Provisions.
Please note that this training course lasts for 4 days, divided into 2 sessions from 20 to 23 August 2019, the first session consists of Svay Rieng city, Romeas Hek district, Kampong Ror district and Chantrea district, and the second course consists of: Svay Chrum district, Svay Teap, Romduol district and Bavet city.
