The body of General Suy Keo was taken to be buried at Wat O Cheng, Kon Mom district
(Ratanakkiri): After keeping the traditional ceremony for 8 days, the body of General Suy Keo, a former senator, was buried at Wat Udom Ratanaream, also known as Wat O Cheng in Ta Ong village, Ta Ong commune, Kon Mom district, Ratanakkiri province. .
Senator Muong Poy read out a biography of His Excellency Seuy Keo, citing the heroic deeds of sacrificing fresh flesh and blood in the cause of national independence and the struggle for national liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
On behalf of the Senate, the National Assembly, the Provincial Council, the Provincial Board of Governors, the civil servants, the Armed Forces throughout Ratanakkiri Province, I would like to express my deepest condolences to the family of the late General Seuy Keo.
Mr. Muong Poy emphasized that the death of the General was the loss of her husband, father, father-in-law, grandfather, who was deeply loved and pious, and that in the past he always worked hard to build a family, nurture and take care of him. And educating children and grandchildren to follow the path of righteousness until they become intellectuals, good leaders in institutions, organizations and good citizens in the society.
