(Prey Veng): During the inspection mission of farmers this morning, August 24, 2019, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, requested the owner of a large rice mill in Prey Veng to collect Buy stockpiled rice during the next harvest to avoid the outflow of rice, which causes a lot of losses.
The request was made on the occasion of Minister Veng Sakhon and the provincial governor visiting the rice fields of farmers in Kok village, Ang Tret commune, Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province, where most farmers in this area use Romduol rice.
Every farm owner has praised the progress of the agricultural sector, now they stop using livestock as a traction to use machinery and take those cattle to feed the meat that the market is in high demand. Domestic and foreign. Leaving the rice fields, the Minister came to inspect the Chhun Thom rice mill not far from the rice production area.
Mr. Oknha Chhun Thom, the owner of the factory, informed him that the factory is able to collect more than 30,000 tons of paddy rice per year from farmers and from 16 communities who have signed a contract to produce both fragrant and seed rice at a price 1,200 riels per kilogram. Currently, the company has received export policy to China and some European markets.
