(Phnom Penh): AII Language Center (Aii) and American Intercontinental School (AIS) Chom Chao Branch will celebrate Environment Day at 6 locations in Phnom Penh to contribute to the dissemination of knowledge about the environment, living, hygiene, health, beauty of the capital and participate in the campaign. The height of the green environment to the public in particular provides a good example of environmental hygiene.
He said that this activity will be done to clean up the environment around where we live and advise people to take care of and dispose of garbage properly. Throwing rubbish in the open field during the rainy season causes the rubbish to flow into the sewers, causing clogged drains and affecting people's livelihoods.
Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly added that the celebration of Environment Day also wants to remind students to continue to remind their families to take care of the environment.
He said that this campaign is aimed at students, teachers to contribute to the dissemination of knowledge on the environment, hygiene, health, aesthetics of the capital better. What is special is to participate in maintaining a green environment for society or the general population living in Phnom Penh to reduce the use of plastic bags.
He also thanked Phnom Penh City Hall for allowing the event, and called on the people and authorities in the Chom Chao area to work together to improve the environment.
