Minister Vong Soth Inspected a Site for the Construction of the First Stop Center in Poipet City
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, representing Minister Vong Soth, led a team to inspect the construction site of the first stop to receive victims of human trafficking and vulnerable groups in Poipet City. Banteay Meanchey Province, a grant from Thailand.
After inspecting the location, he also met and discussed work related to the construction process of the stop center with the Governor of Banteay Meanchey.
It should be noted that Cambodia and Thailand have decided to build a shelter for victims of human trafficking in Poipet during the end of 2019.
The decision to build the first and first shelter for victims of human trafficking in Poipet today marks the positive start of Cambodia-Thailand on strengthening and managing repatriation and integration cases. Victims of Human Trafficking (SOP) in Thailand, which Cambodia and Thailand signed on April 22, 2019.
By signing the agreement, the two States Parties shall cooperate fully to ensure the safe and sustainable repatriation and systematic integration under the scope of cooperation, including:
* First: the exchange of information from victims of human trafficking for the purpose of repatriation and integration * Second: the facilitation of repatriation and integration * Third: Coordination in efforts to provide legal assistance to Victims of human trafficking * Fourth: Monitoring and estimating the results of repatriation and integration
Following the signing, the Cambodian and Thai sides also expressed their joint commitment to implementing the Agreement on the Elimination and Prevention of Trafficking in Persons to a Minimum, and the Victims of Trafficking in Persons to Be Raised and Equalized. Discrimination and to help improve the lives of victims.
