Outgoing Japanese Ambassador: The beauty of Cambodia has given me the dream of returning to this wonderful land again.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Horino Uchihi Hidehisa, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia at the end of his term, expressed his excitement to complete the mission in Cambodia, a beautiful land.
The following is the message of Mr. Hidehisa Horinouchi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia to the Cambodian people on the occasion of concluding his mission in Cambodia:
"I am a little saddened to hear that this is my last message as the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia.
Time is really moving fast. About three years have passed since my wife and I arrived in Phnom Penh in 2016. These three years have been a wonderful time for both of us. Cambodia maintains a strong economic growth rate of 7% annually, and bilateral relations between Japan and Cambodia are also gaining momentum.
Bilateral trade, direct investment and exchange of visits also increased significantly. At the same time, I also attended the inauguration of various development assistance projects of the Japanese government, which symbolize the friendship between our two countries, such as the repair of the Chroy Changvar bridge.
As for political relations, I am fortunate to have attended the Japan-Cambodia Summit between Prime Minister Abe and Prime Minister Hun Sen three times in the past three years.
My wife and I are leaving Phnom Penh next week, but the beauty of Cambodia has given us the dream of returning to this wonderful land again in the future. Phnom Penh will change its face in the coming years with a new airport, many high-rise buildings and a new public transport system. I may also have the opportunity to speak Khmer again.
Finally, I wish all Cambodians good health, happiness and the development of Japan-Cambodia relations.
Civil Servants of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport Volunteer to Donate Blood to 16 January Referral Hospital to Save Patients' Lives
(Preah Vihear): On the morning of August 23, 2019, many civil servants of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province volunteered to donate blood to the 16th January Referral Hospital to save the lives of patients.
Dr. Sok Veasna, director of the 16 January Referral Hospital, said that today the hospital needs a lot of blood to save patients' lives, and the blood that can be used to save patients effectively is blood from voluntary blood donation. The mind is better than the blood that comes from external trade, and voluntary blood donation is a good example of humanitarian promotion in society.
Mr. Sok Veasna thanked Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, for inspiring his subordinates to donate blood to the hospital at this time. At the same time, the director of the hospital called on government officials and the armed forces, our people, to donate blood voluntarily to save the lives of our victims.
In particular, Mr. Samleang Try said, "In order to participate in humanitarian work in society, leaders at all levels and all civil servants in the Department of Public Works have cooperated very well, sacrificing both budget, physical and mental energy and time, especially Now we have another sacrifice, voluntary blood donation to save the lives of patients.
