Major General Net Vantha stressed that all law enforcement forces at the scene were working closely together to intervene in this accident, which can be considered as a case that is almost unprecedented in Phnom Penh.
According to Mr. Net Vantha, so far, the police have used about 50 water trucks, while the cause has not been determined yet with the extent of the damage.
However, Fresh News, which has been covering the scene since the fire broke out, reported that authorities had decided to use Phnom Penh City Hall excavators to pave the way for easy spraying of water into the burning area.
It should be informed that the fire at the mattress factory building started at more than 1 noon and so far for more than 8 hours, the police are confronting the fire that is burning in the commune. Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. In this rescue operation, they observed the presence of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh to lead the intervention at the scene with the authorities and other authorities.
