Phnom Penh Department of Commerce continues to call on business and service owners to beware of scammers
(Phnom Penh): The Department of Commerce of Phnom Penh has continued to call on business and service owners in Phnom Penh to be extremely careful, to beware of fraudsters who pretend to be officials of the Department of Commerce to defraud for various reasons.
In the announcement received by Fresh News on August 23, 2019, the Department of Commerce of Phnom Penh emphasized that the officials of the Department of Commerce, when performing business-service activities, have the correct uniform, ID card. Civil servants, name tags and mission orders issued by the Phnom Penh Department of Commerce and valid.
The department also called on business and service owners to immediately report to the Department of Commerce when anyone goes to the business-service inspection base without a clear identification. Business and service owners can report by calling 016 855 666/077 333 286 if there is any suspicion on the person who went down.
The appeal of the Department of Commerce of Phnom Penh came after some crooks disguised as officials of the Department of Commerce to swindle fees from business owners and services for various reasons.
