Ministry of Interior trains more than 100 judicial police officers on criminal procedures and roles and responsibilities to strengthen capacity when cracking down on counterfeit products
(Phnom Penh): The Committee for Combating Counterfeit Products that pose a high risk to health and social safety (CPPCC) of the Ministry of Interior on the afternoon of August 23, 2019, opened a training course on the Code. Criminal Procedures and Duties and Responsibilities of Judicial Police Officers and Risks of Authorities During Crackdown on Counterfeit Products.
The above training on criminal procedure and duties of judicial police officers was organized under the chairmanship of General Miech Sophanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee (CPPCC). The training was held in the auditorium of Building S, Ministry of Interior.
General Miech Sophanna stated that the purpose of opening this training course is to strengthen the capacity of law enforcement officers in their functions so that there will be no misconduct, so officials must pay attention in this workshop. .
The chairman of the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee also emphasized that the committee will hold a series of training sessions in collaboration with the Court of Appeal.
Please be informed that this training course was attended by more than 100 judicial police officers and 2 speakers, including:
* First: Major General Professor Seng Satya, Director of the Research Institute, Police Institute of the Police Academy of Cambodia, as a lecturer on the roles and responsibilities of judicial police officers. * Second: Brigadier General Teng Bunthon, Deputy Director of the Secretariat of the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee, as a lecturer on the procedure for sending cases and evidence to the judiciary.
The purpose of this training is to provide additional knowledge to the law enforcement officers of the Committee (CPC) on the various law enforcement procedures set out in the Code of Criminal Procedure and the roles and responsibilities of judicial police officers to strengthen the officers. Implement the law to be more capable when cracking down on counterfeit products and the risk of the competent authorities when cracking down on counterfeit products.
