Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, co-chairs with Mr. Pham Binh Minh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, chairing the 17th Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission (17th JC) on Economic Cooperation. Culture, Science and Technology on August 21, 2019 in Phnom Penh.
The two sides agreed to boost cooperation in high value-added industries such as medicine, electrical products and automotive electronics, and agreed to boost agro-industrial investment along the two countries' borders. This is according to the same press release.
It should be noted that in the first five months of 2019, Cambodia-Vietnam achieved a trade volume of more than 2,300 million US dollars, while the first five months of 2018 was only about 2 billion US dollars, an increase of about 300 Million US dollars. This is according to the report of the Vietnamese Customs.
According to the report, in the first five months of 2019, from January to May, Cambodia's exports to Vietnam reached more than 560 million US dollars, an increase of more than 60 million US dollars compared to the same period last year. Same in 2018. At the same time, in the same five months, Vietnam also brought back to Cambodia more than 1.7 billion US dollars, which is higher than the first five months in 2018, more than 280 million US dollars.
The main products that Vietnam imports to Cambodia are iron and steel, gasoline, textiles and clothing, and other agricultural products such as fish, meat and vegetables, fruits, as well as many other consumer goods. The products that Cambodia exports to Vietnam include cashew nuts, rubber, wood and wood products, vegetables, fruits and many other products.
