Kampong Speu Governor: There is no African swine fever in the province
(Kampong Speu): Following the call of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to eat pork on August 23, 2019, the Kampong Speu Provincial Administration led by Mr. Vy Samnang, Provincial Governor of Kampong Speu and Mr. Yim Sokhom, Chairman of the Provincial Council. Together with government officials, the three armed forces, a group of traders ate solidarity pork, which was held in front of Kampong Speu Provincial Hall.
On that occasion, Mr. Vy Samnang confirmed that African swine fever could not be transmitted to humans, only to pigs. So let the people eat pork as usual, because it is not contagious to humans. In addition, the re-eating of pork is to encourage local farmers and pork traders.
