The 48th Meeting of the Monetary Policy Committee was attended by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia and Chairman of the Monetary Policy Committee. The meeting discussed the current state of the world economy, progress and challenges of macroeconomic and financial stability in Cambodia, as well as monetary policy to be implemented in the future.
The Monetary Policy Committee has decided to continue to implement five monetary policies, including:
1. Maintain a stable exchange rate by adopting a stable exchange rate regime through interventions based on market fluctuations.
2: Continue to maintain the supply of liquidity in riel to meet the needs of banking and financial institutions.
4: Continue to promote the widespread use of the riel by increasing public awareness of the importance and role of the riel in the economy and society.
The meeting was also attended by Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department, Lt. Gen. Hang Sophannara, Lt. Gen. Muong Sothea, Director of the Technical and Scientific Department, Lt. Gen. Mao Pov and Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning, Chief of the Criminal Police Office. Nationwide.
