The Traffic Police Department cooperates with partner organizations to train police officers on techniques to increase the efficiency of law enforcement on drunk driving and rescue victims.
(Siem Reap): The Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police, in collaboration with CamMS CaMSafe, under the financial support of APIWSA and its partner members, organized the opening ceremony of a technical training course to increase the efficiency of traffic law enforcement. Driving under the influence of alcohol and rescuing victims for two days, from 21 to 22 August 2019.
The training was held at the Siem Reap Provincial Police with the participation of Brigadier General Teng Channath, Deputy Commissioner for Public Order Planning, Lt. Col. Thi Visal, Director of the Land Traffic Police Office of the National Police, Mr. Keo Manit, Representative of CaMSafe and Ms. Olivier. A total of 60 APIWSA representatives and traffic police officers from around the province.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of the training, Brigadier General Teng Channath thanked for the good cooperation between the partners in road safety, especially the National Police, who organized the training in accordance with the actual needs of the province.
The two-day training aims to:
1: Increase knowledge about the general situation of traffic conditions and risk behaviors and the effects of driving under the influence of alcohol.
2: Increase knowledge of operational planning and rules to deal with the challenges of driving restrictions under the influence of alcohol.
3: Strengthen professional skills, set goals, restrict and use alcohol meters effectively, quality and safety. 4: Increase capacity by addressing, managing and ensuring security goals, enforcing laws, as well as surveying, recording, gathering evidence and reporting.
5: Provide traffic police with knowledge, skills and rescue equipment to the victims at the scene before sending to the hospital.
6: Increase the skills to continue training along with the ability to educate people to use the road to understand the effects of driving under the influence of alcohol.
Please note that CaMSafe under the support of APIWSA will continue to cooperate with the National Police to organize the same training with the ongoing education campaign in Sihanoukville.
