By: Chea Chanboribo, APSARA Authority and ICC-Angkor will monitor the site inside-outside Angkor
(Siem Reap): Experts from APSARA Authority, including representatives of ICC-Angkor Secretariat, will visit the site inside and outside Angkor to see the actual situation and report to the 33rd ICC-Angkor Technical Meeting. Coming in December 2019.
This orientation was made in the follow-up meeting to follow up on the recommendations received through the 32nd Technical Meeting of the ICC-Angkor Committee on the implementation goals of the work in the Angkor area in terms of conservation and development today. August 21, 2019 in the presence of Mr. Hang Pov, Director General of APSARA Authority.
The main purpose of this meeting is to monitor all the recommendations set to promote the implementation of work more effectively. In addition, each recommendation was discussed to find out the problems, shortcomings, questions, feasibility of implementation and solve the challenges that occurred at the joint site.
After the expert meeting, APSARA Authority, including representatives of ICC-Angkor Secretariat, will visit the site inside and outside Angkor to see the actual situation and report to the 33rd ICC-Angkor Technical Meeting to be held in This coming December.
