Tbong Khmum CamControl Officers Continue to Test Food Chemicals in Suong Market, Results Are Good
(Tbong Khmum): In order to ensure the health of the people who consume, Mr. Meas Mora, Head of Camcontrol Branch in Tbong Khmum Province, on August 22, 2019, led the CamControl officials in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce to continue to inspect and strengthen the quality and Product safety by testing some food kits at Suong Market in Suong City, Tbong Khmum Province.
Mr. Meas Mora said that today, in fact, we immediately tested the kit on some foods, as a result, there were no banned chemicals in the product samples, including:
* 3 samples of locally made palm sugar to detect the presence of banned chemical sodium hydroxide * 2 samples of locally produced palm to detect the presence of banned chemical boracic Imported from Vietnam.
Separately, CamControl officials sampled 10 kinds of vegetables imported from Vietnam and 8 kinds of fruits, a total of 18 kinds, to be sent to CamControl for analysis to find pesticide residues in those products.
