After opening an investigation, the police arrested the four accused and sent them to court for legal action. Turkey announces two months for illegal Syrian refugees to leave Istanbul
(Istanbul): Turkish Interior Minister Suleyman Soylu confirmed to local television on Tuesday evening that Turkey has given two more months until October 30 for Unregistered Syrian refugees to leave Istanbul. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua in the morning of Thursday, August 22, 2019.
In July, the mayor of Istanbul announced a deadline of August 20 for Syrian refugees to return to their provinces of origin or face deportation. Forced. But on Tuesday evening, Turkish authorities announced a two-month extension for them, until October 30.
The war in Syria, which has lasted for more than eight years, has led to the influx of millions of refugees into Turkey, Lebanon and other neighboring countries. Currently, about 3.6 million Syrian refugees are currently living in Turkey. They are provided with "temporary protection" and are required to live where they first registered, and travel to other provinces requires prior approval from the authorities.
Official data show that Istanbul has nearly 548,000 registered Syrian refugees. However, according to the mayor of Istanbul, this figure could exceed 1 million.
Cambodian Defense Chief calls on people to beware of corrupt groups who want to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, calls on all people to beware of corrupt people Who wants to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government of Cambodia that emerged from the election.
In a political message on Facebook on the morning of August 22, 2019, Samdech Picheay Sena stated: "Other crimes, especially the attempt to overthrow the legitimate government that emerged from the election."
The message of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh was made after Sam Rainsy announced his return to Cambodia on November 9, 2019. At the same time, the inmate who had called for anti-government citizens also confirmed that his return would not be an arrest by the Royal Government, but a return to arrest the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
However, the police also announced that they are ready to implement the court order to arrest Sam Rainsy to be convicted when he is present in Cambodia at any time.
Ministry of Economy: Cambodia's major development partners applaud progress made in implementing public financial management reform program
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance confirmed that Cambodia's development partners, including the European Union, the Asian Development Bank, the World Bank, its French counterpart and other representatives, expressed their appreciation for the progress made by the Royal Government of Cambodia. In implementing the public financial management reform program. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Economy released on August 22.
The meeting was attended by representatives of government ministries and agencies and development partners such as the European Union, the Asian Development Bank, the World Bank, its French counterpart and many other partners.
The report on the implementation of the third phase of the Public Financial Management Reform Program in the first and second quarters of 2019 shows that in the section "Budget reliability, financial accountability, and linking the budget to policy". Achieved "good" results. In the section "Preparation for the next step and support for the implementation of a successful and sustainable reform program" achieved "excellent" results.
The Deputy Prime Minister thanked the development partners for their continued support and assistance to the Royal Government's efforts to reform public financial management.
The Deputy Prime Minister also stressed that Cambodia needs further support from cooperation with development partners for a stronger and more energetic step in reform.
On that occasion, the Deputy Prime Minister also praised and thanked the efforts of all relevant ministries and institutions in the past to participate in the implementation of public financial management reform program.
He said that the reform program of the Royal Government has reached a more energetic stage, where the role of ministries and institutions is also more important and more, especially in the allocation and more efficient use of public financial resources to respond. In all areas of priority of the Royal Government.
