Minister Thong Khon made the call during the closing ceremony of the first international conference on Cambodian food tourism, which took place on August 21, 2019 at the Sokha Hotel in Phnom Penh.
The conference, co-chaired by XU Jing, Asia-Pacific Regional Director of the World Tourism Organization, requested the Royal Government of Cambodia to consider the possibility of proposing five types of Khmer cuisine, including: Hormone soup (popularly called Amok) and noodles, as well as five other desserts, including: Ansam cake, Chakra moon cake, Sangkhya rice cake, Ai fruit cake and fresh leaf cake, a UNESCO Intangible World Heritage Site.
In relation to this work, Mr. Thong Khon said that the Royal Government is still starting to do, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia is also very motivated.
He said that in terms of food and desserts, Cambodia has a lot of variety, in addition to the above food and dessert, there are also soups such as pickles, tamarind pickles, ripe pickles, pickles, pickles, leaves, leaves, etc .. Desserts are also many, such as Bananas, desserts, nuts, light brown fruit or brown porridge, sweets, fruits, that is, only the food and desserts that the ancestors recorded from ancient times are collected and prepared to apply for registration.
Mr. Thong Khon said, "Along with the implementation of this work, we need to have standards, hygiene, quality and highlight more attractive to attract tourists to taste or eat at a meal, whether in Cambodia. "Or abroad, to make them eat and remember our country, Cambodia will become more attractive tourist destination through this food, which is called food tourism."
He said that food is an important part of culture and plays an important driving force in attracting tourists who have never been out. In this sense, the development of food tourism will help attract more new tourists to visit Cambodia.
According to Minister Thong Khon, in the context of increasing competition, food is the key to creating more diversity, providing more diverse options for tourists, as well as contributing to strengthening the attractiveness of each destination.
This morning, the CPP will hold a meeting of the Central Committee
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 22, 2019, the Cambodian People's Party held its Central Committee meeting at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
The meeting will be chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, with the participation of all members of the Central Committee, including party representatives from a number of ministries, institutions and localities. This is according to Mr. Chhim Phal Varun, the spokesman of the Cambodian People's Party, who told Fresh News.
He stated that every year, the CPP holds two standing committee meetings, which set the committee's direction for six months and will review and evaluate what the party has implemented in the past six months. .
