Director General of Taxation: The launch of a data management system for online services makes it easier for taxpayers
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, said that the launch of information technology systems to manage the collection of tax revenue through online services is very important for the tax sector and Private companies, and even more convenient for taxable private companies and other private companies to pay taxes to the state.
Mr. Kong Vibol confirmed this morning, August 21, 2019, when he chaired a Vipassana forum with the private sector on the launch of information technology systems to manage tax revenue collection held at Garden City Hotel Phnom Penh. The forum was also attended by officials from the General Department of Taxation and representatives of nearly 1,000 private companies.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that the Vipassana forum with the private sector on the launch of information technology systems to manage tax revenue collection is very important for the tax sector and private companies because the private sector is a partner of the General Department of Taxation. Pay taxes to the state, and the launch of this new technology will make it easier for private companies to pay taxes.
He said that in the past, tax payment was multi-stage and took a long time, but now it has been reduced to only two stages. We have prepared online tax payment to make it easier for you. Come pay all the taxes as well.
It should be noted that the information technology system that the General Department of Taxation decided to do in 2019 includes: double tax avoidance management system, value added tax return management system, tax management system, tax calculation program For transportation and vehicles 2019, enterprise registration management system, personal information management system, tax collection management system and online tax management system.
China does not legalize same-sex marriage
(Beijing): Marriage between a man and a woman will still be legal, and same-sex marriage will not be legal in China. This is according to a spokesman for the Chinese National People's Congress quoted by CNA on Wednesday afternoon, August 21, 2019.
Taiwan, which is recognized as just one of China's provinces, passed a law in May that allows LGBT people to marry legally. China does not recognize the law, but there is no anti-gay law in China.
Minister of Tourism: Food is an important message to remind tourists of tourist destinations
(Phnom Penh): Under the collaboration between the Ministry of Tourism and the World Tourism Organization (UNWTO), the first International Conference on Food and Tourism in Cambodia was held on August 21, 2019 under the theme "Promoting traditional values and heritage. For the development of sustainable tourism.
Food tourism refers to the travel of tourists to a certain area is to taste the food in that destination area.
It aims to join the efforts of the World Tourism Organization and ASEAN initiatives, especially to promote the value of Cambodian food as an attractive tourism product in Cambodia, as well as to promote national cultural traditions and heritage. Through food tourism as well.
Minister Thong Khon said that "food has contributed to the creation of memories for tourists about the destinations visited and as a messenger about the culture, identity, life of the local people to tourists."
He instructed officials and stakeholders to jointly process, compile, interpret and present food as cultural heritage, these heritage will contribute to improving the livelihood of the people in the area through the arrival of national and international tourists.
The minister added that such tourism will help attract national tourists to visit those food destinations, as well as attract tourists from the area to visit food destinations.
Food tourism not only contributes to attracting national and international tourists, improves people's livelihood and promotes national heritage traditions, but also contributes to job creation, entrepreneurship, innovation and innovation.
Clearly, the food profession requires both will, knowledge, skills, high attitude, art and creativity that are indispensable. The development of food tourism really brings career growth in tourism, especially to prevent migration and increase patriotism.
(Phnom Penh): Grab Cambodia on August 21, 2019 announced that the company has reduced the base price for all tuk-tuk rides in Phnom Penh with the aim of providing the best service with reasonable price for its passengers. As well as ensuring that the income of the driving partner can remain the same or increase. This program starts from today until August 31st.
With this new campaign, the minimum base price for tuk tuk booking through Grab mobile travel booking app will be reduced from 3,000 Riel to 2,500 Riel, and the next kilogram price will remain the same. The same, which is 1,000 riels per kilometer.
As Grab enters its second year of operation since launching in the Kingdom of Cambodia in 2017, the company is constantly evaluating and evolving its pricing model to ensure that it does deliver. The most reasonable price in this competitive market.
In addition to providing market-leading affordability, Grab also provides passenger and driver services with the latest features in the app, with a focus on convenience and safety for passengers and driving partners.
In addition, Grab also provides driving partners with many other benefits to help them work more efficiently and productively.
