US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo has told dozens of prominent businessmen and economists that a trade war with China may end before the 2020 US presidential election (Video inside). Trade between the United States and China could end by or before the 2020 US presidential election. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Wednesday, August 21, 2019.
Pompeo made the remarks at a dinner with more than 40 well-known businessmen and economists in New York on Tuesday. According to US economist Stephen Moore, who attended the event, Pompeo believed that China and the United States could reach a trade agreement before the 2020 US presidential election, which would be good for the United States. America.
In early August, Donald Trump announced a 10 percent tariff on nearly $ 300 billion worth of Chinese goods, which will take effect on September 1. But Trump has decided to postpone the tax until December 15, 2019, to allow US and Chinese officials to continue talks to find an agreement to end the current trade war.
