According to a press release from the Ministry of Economy, obtained by Fresh News on August 21, while Cambodia is experiencing economic growth and population growth in cities and towns, especially in Phnom Penh. , The amount of garbage and solid waste has increased alarmingly.
In fact, in Phnom Penh, during the last 5 years, the average amount of garbage was more than 2,800 tons per day, which increased by around 10% to 13% per year. The amount of garbage in the city is projected. That there will be further increases that require effective management measures.
