(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, has announced to encourage people to make delicious noodles and cucumbers to sell to tourists for consumption or to reach the export (cucumber) to contribute to the promotion of Cambodia's tourism destinations. He also asked stakeholders to help promote this work.
Mr. Thong Khon made this statement during the first international conference on Cambodian food tourism, which was held on August 21, 2019 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The Minister said that through this food is also contributing to the growth of tourism around the world, as well as in Cambodia, meaning that in addition to Angkor Wat, other intangible culture, international tourists also know Cambodia through this food.
Regarding Khmer noodles, which is one of the famous Khmer food, Minister Thong Khon said that the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, also promoted this work in order to make noodles become a national identity. Real Khmer.
The Minister stated that he has commissioned a book on how to make noodles and compiled a translation into several languages to tell how to make delicious noodle soup in order to promote this Khmer identity food to the world and The area is better known and, most importantly, hygienic and delicious.
As for the Cucumber, the Minister said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen had also recommended to promote this work, he vowed that from now on we will jointly carry out this work, and not just the Cucumber, but some other food of Cambodia needs to research how to make it hygienic, put in cans or bottles for domestic use and can be sold abroad.
He said that if Cambodia promotes this work, noodles and cucumbers will become attractive tourism products, as well as participate in promoting and promoting national cultural traditions and heritage through food tourism.
(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation organized a two-day outreach workshop on justice services for the disabled at work on August 21-22, 2019 in Siem Reap. The workshop focused on policy making, respect for the rights of persons with disabilities in the workplace and the payment of contributions.
At the same time, Mr. Nak Naron, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, said that this workshop showed the care of people with disabilities in the workplace, how to ensure justice for people with disabilities while working in accordance with the law. Provided in force.
Mr. Nak Naron added that this workshop is also a good sign to ensure the rights and duties that people with disabilities have to receive, along with fair protection for all people living in society.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has implemented a law on the rate of disability to work and encourage both the public and private sectors to recruit people with disabilities to work. As a result, we see that the number of people with disabilities to work. Increase.
In fact, in 2018, there were 2,839 people with disabilities working in 40 government ministries and institutions, including 756 women with disabilities and 1,478 people with severe disabilities, equivalent to 4,471 people, accounting for 1.93%.
