Pence made the announcement at a meeting of the US National Space Council. The Space Military Command will be responsible for space-related defense operations, and will be the 11th U.S. military headquarters, along with several other military headquarters, to serve specific geographical functions and responsibilities.
The inauguration ceremony will take place on August 29, next Thursday, and will have a total of 87 officers under the command of John Raymond, who is currently in charge of operations. Space Division in the U.S. Air Force.
US President Donald Trump announced his intention to create a "space force" in the US military in 2018, and he officially introduced the idea in February 2019 by issuing an order to the US Department of Defense. Prepare to create a space force that will be a brand new US military force, along with the Army, Navy, Air Force, Marine Corps and Marine Corps.
After all, the "Space Command" and the "Space Army" of the United States are two separate institutions, the differences between the two institutions are similar to the differences between the other five divisions and the number of military headquarters. The other 4 are in charge of special functions as well. However, the space military headquarters can be considered the first step towards the formation of the US space force by 2020.
