Kampong Thom Provincial Governor Provides Funds and Gifts to Two Disabled Candidates After the Bankruptcy Exam Session
(Kampong Thom): After receiving the news that there are two disabled students who are candidates for the high school diploma exam, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, met with them after they finished the second day of final exams. Finished at 5 pm on August 20, 2019 at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall.
Candidate Tuy Sok Dong lives in Po Ta Un village, Srayov commune, Stung Sen city, Kampong Thom province. He is a student at Stung Sen High School. Sok Dong, despite his congenital disability and poor family situation, is ranked between two and five in the classroom every month.
Candidate Ul Kosal lives in Treas village, Chhouk Khsach commune, Baran district, Kampong Thom province. She is a student at Baray High School. Shea rubber in Santuk district has to work far away from home, making him live with his siblings and grandmother. Classroom studies are ranked second or third each month.
Mr. Sok Lou donated 2,000,000 Riels to each of them and some other food items. He will also provide a laptop at the time of posting the results, regardless of the exam results, if both candidates receive an A grade, he will provide a motorcycle like the other A candidates.
In addition, Mr. Sok Lou will provide 100% scholarships and full support during the study period for both of them who continue their studies in Kampong Thom, but if they go to study in Phnom Penh, he will look for philanthropists to continue to support.
Noble gestures and generosity now really show that the provincial governor, who always cares about the well-being of the people really.
