Samdech Techo Hun Sen Urges Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission to Discuss Border Work and Cooperation in All Areas
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission to meet on August 21, 2019 to discuss border work and cooperation in all fields between the two countries. Make that discussion a success.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs Pham Binh Minh to pay a courtesy call on the afternoon of August 20, 2019 at the Peace Palace in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, said that during the meeting, Samdech Techo and Mr. Pham Binh Minh exchanged views on relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam. Samdech Techo made some recommendations to the Vietnamese Foreign Minister to make the 17th Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission meeting tomorrow a success and based on the principles of friendship, development and cooperation between the two countries.
According to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, during the meeting, Samdech Techo encouraged the Joint Commission to discuss work to promote cooperation and strengthen bilateral relations in all fields. In particular, the preparation for the signing of the border labor agreement between the two countries, as the border work is now 84 percent complete and only 16 percent left, the Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Boundary Commission will continue to do this work.
In addition to discussing work related to the meeting of the Joint Commission of the two countries, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Vietnamese Minister of Foreign Affairs also discussed some work related to the planned visit of Samdech in Vietnam in September.
The Prime Minister requested Vietnam to organize a Cambodia-Vietnam Business Forum during Samdech's visit to Vietnam, in order to provide more opportunities for Vietnamese investors to come to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that trade between the two countries needs to be further increased because currently the trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam is large and nearly 6 billion dollars.
In this meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister of Vietnam expressed his pleasure to see the achievements and progress of Cambodia. He said that under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia has made great progress, especially in the economic and construction sectors. In addition, he pledged that during Samdech Techo's upcoming visit to Vietnam, the Vietnamese side will be ready to make the visit a success.
It should be noted that Mr. Pham Binh Minh on August 20 led a Vietnamese delegation to Cambodia. On August 21, he will lead a delegation to the 17th Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission Meeting organized by the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
