Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, told the media after the meeting that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. On Nak Yong discussed many issues on trade and investment relations between the two countries as well as regional affairs. . In particular, the outgoing Ambassador highlighted the achievements made during his tenure in Cambodia.
The Prime Minister noted that investment, trade and economic cooperation between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea in the bilateral framework has increased, but Samdech wants to see the trade volume between the two countries increase. Samdech Techo urged both sides to find ways to expand and increase bilateral trade.
The Prime Minister also requested the South Korean side to continue importing Cambodian agricultural products to the Korean market, while Cambodia has a lot of potential for agricultural products such as mangoes. In addition, the Prime Minister also wants to see the Republic of Korea increase investment in Cambodia.
