Minister of Planning Introduces 4 Recommendations to Subordinates in Meeting to Disseminate Anti-Drug Campaign to Civil Servants Under the Ministry
(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of August 20, 2019, Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Chhay Thorn, Senior Minister of the Ministry of Planning, presided over a meeting to promote the fight against drugs to civil servants under the auspices of the Ministry of Planning. Leaders of the Secretary of State, Undersecretaries of State, as well as leaders of civil servants in all general departments under the Ministry of Planning, attended in large numbers.
Speaking at the event, Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Senior Minister said that today we are very happy to jointly celebrate the National Anti-Drug Campaign Meeting set up by the Royal Government to inspire and Remind everyone to support and participate in all anti-drug activities, understand the effects and dangers of all kinds of illegal drugs.
Through the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, which clearly and firmly confirms the firm position and will in the fight against drugs and the attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia to eliminate prevention. Suppress and fight drug crimes from the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In this regard, in order to contribute to support the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against drugs, Mr. Kittisetha Bandith has introduced and made some recommendations to all civil servants of the Ministry of Planning as follows:
1. All units must prepare and strengthen mechanisms for the fight against drugs in the unit in accordance with their relevant roles and responsibilities.
