(Phnom Penh): About 400 people from Santuk district, Kampong Thom province, including monks, have been invited to receive eye treatment, including: cataracts and free dental treatment from a team of volunteer doctors. From Humanitarian Aid for Health Australia under the auspices of the Khmer Vision Foundation and under the auspices of Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
