(Siem Reap): The CamControl Officer of Siem Reap Province, with Mr. Preav Khemrith as the Branch Manager, on August 20, 2019, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce, continued to promote and inspect food products in Prasat Bakong District.
Mr. Preav Khemrith said that this morning, August 20, his CamControl officer conducted an educational campaign on the quality and safety of products and food to Kampong Phluk Primary School students in Dey Krahorm Village, Kampong Phluk Commune, Prasat Bakong District. Participation from school principals, deputy directors, commune councils, village chiefs, teachers, business people and more than 400 students.
According to the branch manager, in the afternoon of the same year, the team cooperated with the owner of Rolous Market, located in Daun Teav Village, Rolous Commune, Prasat Bakong District. There are 9 products on display in the market: 2 samples of sausage, fish prahok, cabbage, navy beans, noodles, ginger, lemongrass, fish meatballs.
As a result of this market inspection, we did not find any chemicals in those products. The team continued to check the packaging products displayed in the stalls to see the expiration date of the use of canned lentils, etc. will continue to distribute posters to traders and students in the school.
After that, the professional officials instructed other traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products and services to avoid affecting the health of the people will be able to face the law.
