(Phnom Penh): The 7th meeting of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the Cambodian, Lao and Vietnamese parliaments was held in Vietnam recently.
This is according to Mr. Chheang Vun, Member of the National Assembly of Cambodia, who led the delegation to attend the above conference, told the media on the way back to Cambodia on the night of August 19, 2019.
Mr. Chheang Vun said that at the conference, the three parties discussed the development of the triangle area, which Cambodia has four provinces: Kratie, Stung Treng, Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri, Vietnam has five provinces and Laos has four provinces.
"Our meeting during the two days of advocacy was very lively, so we are happy with the result because we advocated to protect the interests of our nation," he said.
Regarding the discussion on the issue in the triangle, Mr. Chheang Vun claimed that the Cambodian Parliament asked the Lao side to help prevent drug imports into Cambodia. Because in the past, we were often caught at the border of Stung Treng province. This problem is being suppressed by Cambodia all over the country. Cambodia loses a lot due to drugs.
