Cambodia Hosts Fourth Meeting of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia will host the 4th rotating meeting under the theme "Roles and Duties in the Monitoring Committee of the National Defense and Security Committee of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam in Building Cooperation" And develop a peaceful and friendly border. ” This is according to the announcement of the National Assembly, which was received by Fresh News on August 20, 2019.
The meeting will be held for 4 days, from 26 to 29 August 2019. Dr. Nguon Nhel, First Vice President of the National Assembly, will be represented by Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, at the opening ceremony of the meeting on the morning of August 27, 2019 at Sokha Residence Hotel, Phnom Penh.
According to the statement, the fourth meeting will be attended by the Chairman of the National Assembly Defense and Security Committee of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, Chairman of the National Defense and Security Committee of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and Chairman of the Committee on Interior, National Defense and Public Function of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, discussing some important topics such as:
First, the results of work and the direction of implementation in maintaining security along the border.
Second, the progress and role of the Commission / Committee in monitoring and promoting cooperation and the development of a peaceful and friendly border.
And 3: Review, discuss and sign the minutes of the 4th meeting.
