(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, requested the Japanese Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary to Cambodia, Mr. Horino Ochihide Iza, to help attract investors from Japan to invest in the production of components and bicycles to boost the manufacturing and manufacturing industries. Promote the export of finished products to international markets.
In a meeting with the outgoing Japanese Ambassador at the Ministry of Commerce on the morning of August 20, 2019, Mr. Pan Sosak informed the Japanese side about the trade reform and measures facilitated by the Head of the Royal Government. The Cambodian government, as well as business opportunities where Japanese investors can profit from production and export to third countries.
The Minister also thanked the Ambassador and the Government of Japan for providing substantial grants to Cambodia to build democracy and socio-economic development. At the same time, the Minister also requested the Japanese side to continue to support Cambodia's development in the fields of education, infrastructure, health, agriculture and rural development, etc.
In response, Mr. Horino Ochihide Iza expressed his appreciation for the progress of relations and cooperation in all fields between Cambodia and Japan and praised the sharp reforms introduced by the Royal Government of Cambodia to facilitate the business of Japanese investors. Especially the import of goods at the border.
The Ambassador also expressed high optimism for the future of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and pledged to continue to support Cambodia's economic development by encouraging more Japanese investors to invest. In addition, to create jobs for the people and contribute to poverty reduction. Sandan District Authority Disseminates the Importance of Breastfeeding to People in Sandan District, Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): Sandan District Authority in collaboration with Kampong Thom Provincial Health Department and Adra this morning, August 20, 2019, celebrated World Breastfeeding Week under the theme "We all support breastfeeding. "By breast milk" held in Kleng village, Kleng commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province to spread awareness to local people about the importance of breastfeeding.
The event was held in the presence of Mr. Lang Kiseng, Governor of Sandan District, with the support of Adra Cambodia Hug Project and with the participation of Mr. Rath Romnea, Hug Project Manager in Kampong Thom and Preah Vihear Provinces, as well as the Armed Forces, Village and Commune Authorities. 359 people and students.
Mr. Rath Romna said that the organization of the World Breastfeeding Week aims to strengthen the awareness of mothers, including:
* First: The mother must start breastfeeding immediately during the first hour after delivery, which will provide the first useful milk * Second: Only give breast milk to Babies during the first 6 months of their life * Third: Continue to breastfeed until the child is at least 2 years old and give appropriate supplements.
