Camcontrol officers found nearly 16 kilograms of expired goods for sale at O'Yadao Market and Bor Keo Market, Ratanakkiri Province.
(Rattanakiri): For food safety as well as people's health, on August 20, 2019, Camcontrol Branch in Rattanakiri Province, in collaboration with the Provincial Department of Commerce, the Market Commission and the local authority, continued to disseminate the quality of food safety and product inspection. Food and pre-packaged goods at O'Yadao and Bor Keo markets in Ratanakkiri province, nearly 16 kilograms of expired goods were found.
Ratanakkiri CamControl officials said that the purpose of the inspection was to prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit labels, expiration dates and the presence of banned chemicals that could affect people's health.
During the inspection, officials conducted preliminary tests, including some food and seafood, and as a result did not find any banned chemicals that could harm people's health.
However, CamControl officers found a total of about 15.90 kilograms of defective and expired goods on display.
