(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Education, Youth and Sports has decided to allow the Documentation Center of Cambodia to use the premises of the two pedagogical institutes and the two regional pedagogical centers under the Ministry's control to establish an office called: Khmer Rouge Document Library ”to be a place to educate, disseminate and research about the history of the Khmer Rouge to the community of teachers and students to understand the history.
Mr. Rasy stated that "The Victims Support Section of the Khmer Rouge Tribunal made a request to the Royal Government. At that time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen supported and agreed to establish research and information offices in the provinces. According to this letter, we sent a letter to the Ministry of Education to reach the establishment of this office.
He said that the establishment of this office in the provinces at the request of the Khmer Rouge tribunal was made to provide information about the history of the Khmer Rouge to the community and provide education that provides additional training in history to teachers who will become teachers in the future.
"According to a letter from the leadership of the Khmer Rouge tribunal requesting the Ministry of Education to open an office in the six regional talent centers, we have now set up the first office in the Prey Veng regional talent center, named "The Khmer Rouge Research and Library Office," which plays an important role as both a library and a research facility, as well as a source of information for the community.
He added that the office will provide and disseminate information about the history of the Khmer Rouge to the student community and educate teachers on teaching methods that are not rigorous or that do not use historical events in other ways, such as politics.
