Others say the protesting youths are wreaking havoc on the cities that provide them with a place to live and shelter. On the other hand, while wanting to be free for themselves, they are obviously destroying the freedom of others in Hong Kong.
Demonstrations in Hong Kong began in June against a controversial extradition plan aimed at handing over Hong Kong suspects to the mainland government. Around this issue, both Beijing and many international experts claim that the black palm or the third palm is behind the burning anger of young people in Hong Kong.
Although the mayor of Hong Kong has agreed to cancel the project, protests have continued for 11 weeks now, as clashes with police escalated while initially peaceful and non-violent. Serious disturbances in the city like recently.
(Trat, Thailand): The Tourism Technology Working Group of the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia and Thailand have agreed to continue tourism cooperation on the Joint Action Plan 2019-2021, focusing on six tasks to promote tourism growth. Even more so.
The agreement was held at the 5th Cambodia-Thailand Tourism Technical Working Group Meeting on Tourism Cooperation from 17-19 August 2019 in Koh Chang, Trat Province, Thailand. The Cambodian side is led by Mr. Thong Rathasak, Director General of the General Department of Tourism Development and International Cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism.
He said that at the 5th Cambodia-Thailand Tourism Technical Working Group Meeting, both sides agreed to continue tourism cooperation on the Joint Action Plan 2019-2021, focusing on six tasks:
1: Promote the flow of mutual tourists, both Cambodian and Thai tourists, as well as tourists from third countries to visit both countries with the implementation of some other relevant work, including: Facilitation of travel, immigration. Border Transport, Fitness and Infrastructure Infrastructure Discussion on the Joint Implementation Process of ACMECS Single VISA.
2: Joint Tourism Market Study and Promotion "Two Kingdoms, One Tourism Destination": In order to carry out this work, both parties need to do some related work, including the production of joint tourism promotion videos, the creation of joint tourism packages. Organizing study tours for journalists, organizing joint exhibitions, examining the possibility of promoting tour videos and tour documents on the plane.
4: Develop tourism human resources, train tourism officials in border provinces on tourism skills, manage tourist destinations, resorts, tourism and hospitality, continue to monitor the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding with the Ministry of Tourism and Rajamangala University, Thanyaburi.
5: Support each other in promoting tourism investment between the two countries, discuss the potential to invest in waterway infrastructure, find investors to invest in Cambodia-Thailand coast, organize the second tourism investment forum from 30- October 31, 2019 in Cambodia Invitation to the Thai side to participate in the River Festival, International Conference on Tourism, Food and other tourism events in Cambodia.
APSARA Authority: Hot measures will be applied to a plot owner if the hill and pond are not restored after the violation of this archeological site
(Siem Reap): The APSARA Authority has inspected the illegal activities of a person named Chhit Sodang (holding ID card number 180927593) who poured soil to make a road into the pond and paved the foundation and erected a fence post around the ancient hill. Near the pond, even considered a violation of the law can not be allowed to continue to act absolutely.
According to a letter from the APSARA Authority, received by Fresh News on August 19, 2019, the flower pond and the flower hill above are an archeological site in the Angkor Heritage Protection Area, located in Bos Kralanh village. Sangkat Chreav, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province, there are also ancient stones and some remnants of ancestors.
According to some sources, this person named Chhit Sodang is the owner of the plot of land in Bos Kralanh village. According to the Chreav commune chief, he was not involved in the stamping of this person to encroach on the ancient hill land as personal property.
In relation to the above case, Mr. Ratha, Director of the Department of APSARA Authority, also confirmed that two weeks ago, he sent a letter to the person concerned to stop the encroachment on the ancient site, ordering the person concerned to attack the construction. That throw it all back to its original state.
The APSARA Authority has reminded that it has the role of preserving, protecting and preserving as a national heritage property, so any activities such as pouring soil, building, clearing, causing damage to those archeological sites without permission is a crime of destroying cultural heritage.
Motorcycle thief arrested in Meanchey district escapes court when police arrive
(Phnom Penh): The accused, a motorcycle thief, was reported to have escaped from the Phnom Penh Municipal Court at 4:50 pm on August 18, 2019 yesterday. Yesterday.
The accused who escaped was named M. Rattanak, alias Akandor, male, 32 years old, false occupation, a former police officer of Boeung Tumpun Ros Administration, Prek Toal Village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey 2, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the report, the accused was arrested by the Stung Meanchey 1 police force on the night of August 16, 2019, under the Stung Meanchey flyover, when he stole people's motorcycles.
Please be informed that when sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Deputy Prosecutor Long Cheab opened an investigation and charged M. Ratanak alias Akandor with theft and sent the case to the investigating judge for legal action.
Defendant was handcuffed and escaped while Meanchey district criminal police were seeking an arrest warrant from Ouk Reth Kunthea, Investigating Judge and Deputy Chief of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
However, for this incident, Meanchey District Police Inspector Meng Vimean Dara expressed regret for the negligence of his officers, but he said that this time he ordered a professional force to search for the return.
Please be informed that the escape of the suspect and the accused in the Phnom Penh Municipal Court is not new, that is, it has happened very often.
