Agricultural importers vow to help farmers in agricultural development in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Seiha Power Cambodia, a company that imports agricultural fertilizers from Thailand and distributes them in Cambodia in collaboration with Thailand's legal PSK, is highly committed to engaging with service providers in the development of the sector. Agriculture in Cambodia for the better. This is according to Mr. Dam Seiha, General Director of Seiha Power Cambodia.
Mr. Dam Seiha stated that the main purpose of importing agricultural fertilizers from Thailand to distribute in Cambodia so that Cambodians have the opportunity to use fertilizers, which are pure natural products for agriculture, because Cambodia is an agricultural country and in accordance with the policy of The Royal Government, which always pays attention to farmers' livelihood.
He added that he also wants to see farmers use good products and have the opportunity to export agricultural products that are free from various toxins and want farmers to have a better life.
Mr. Dam Seiha said that Seiha Power Cambodia is a company that imports agricultural fertilizers from Thailand to distribute in Cambodia in cooperation with the Thai company PSK legally. So far, the company has been importing this fertilizer for one year.
Mr. Ley Sopheap announced his commitment to support and join the Royal Government in developing the agricultural sector in Cambodia to be more modern and high yield and is cooperating with the Ministry of Agriculture to find markets to sell more agricultural products to farmers.
Mr. Ley Sopheap said that this is a good and very important thing that the two Cambodian-Thai companies have joined hands to promote the development of the agricultural sector in Cambodia to modernize through the import of agricultural fertilizers. Nature helps save the farmland of Cambodian farmers to get high yields safely (in crops).
"This is also a start for the private sector to show support and join the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Ministry of Agriculture, which has a vision to develop the agricultural sector to be more advanced as in some countries," he said.
Mr. Ley Sopheap continued that although the participation is still limited, but he himself, all his associations involved in this field, as well as private companies that are partners of his association, are still committed to continue to participate with the Royal Government. Under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, to help improve the lives of Cambodian farmers and reduce the impact on the health of consumers as well as consumers.
Ms. Chea Chansrey Neang is a student at Angkor High School and has to take the exam at the examination center in North 10 Makara High School. Regarding the late examination of Miss Chan Srey Neang, the reason has not been confirmed yet.
According to the regulations of the Ministry of Education for the examination, candidates who enter the examination center after the second round intentionally or negligently will not be allowed to enter the examination and will be given a zero score in case of violation of the rules and regulations.
Spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Ros Sovacha, confirmed that candidates who come to the exam after the second round for 15 minutes can apply for the right to enter the exam from the director of the examination center and the director of the center to decide whether or not to enter. Login. In the case of Miss Chea Chan Srey, she was late for up to 30 minutes.
The spokesperson added that in the case of Ms. Chea Chan Srey Neang, who did not pass the exam in the first hour subject, she was given a zero score and also automatically failed.
In relation to the case of Ms. Chea Chan Srey Neang, it was also spread on some social media that the Governor of Siem Reap, Mr. Tea Seiha, facilitated him to enter the exam. But this information was denied by the provincial governor and immediately rejected.
