Ms. Men Sam An: Buddhism has made a significant contribution to the promotion of moral education in the society
(Svay Rieng): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection and Chair of the National Assistance Team for Svay Rieng Province, stated that Buddhism has made a significant contribution to the promotion of moral education. Society will build many achievements for the society, and of course the progress of the Buddha and the Empire must go hand in hand and give to each other.
This morning, August 19, 2019, Ms. Kittisongkhab Dr. Men Sam An said this on the occasion of presiding over the dissemination of the contents of the 27th National Congress of Priests at the Svay Rieng Provincial Hall.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province and Mr. Visoth Nhean Mom Soy, Chief of Svay Rieng Province, as well as officials, monks, abbots and nearly 1,000 pagoda committee members.
In order to contribute to the dissemination of the contents of the 27th National Congress of Priests in Svay Rieng, Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An also provided eight recommendations, such as:
First, priests at all levels must strictly abide by the provisions of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Existing laws and regulations, such as the Royal Decree, the Royal Kram, the Sub-Decree, the Prakas, the Declaration, the Decision, and the NCC of the Office of the Council of Ministers - must also be strictly enforced to become an important driving force for the promotion of God. Buddhism to be stronger and better.
Second, priests at all levels must better cooperate in accordance with the rules and regulations in order to strengthen the unity and solidarity in Buddhist institutions as a good example, a good template for Buddhists and contribute to moral education to society.
Third: Priests at all levels must maintain better cooperation with the provincial Department of Cult and Religion, as well as the Office of Cult and Religion in all cities and districts to work together to achieve better results with mutual understanding and tolerance. Each other.
Fourthly, the Provincial Department of Cult and Religion and the Provincial Council must pay attention to strengthening the quality of Buddhist schools at all levels to become a training ground for Dharma, Pali, Sanskrit, general knowledge and a good professional skill in the society.
Fifth, the Provincial Department of Cults and Religions and the Provincial Council must pay attention to strengthen the work of the pagoda administration and disseminate the Dharma by various means to help Buddhists to do good deeds, adhere to social truth and avoid all kinds of sins.
Sixth, monks at all levels should move the Buddhist monks to contribute to the Royal Government in promoting drug prevention and creating conditions for respect for traffic laws in society through the introduction of sermons, education. Community schools to reduce the devastation caused by the effects of drugs.
Seventh, officials at all levels of the Department of Cults and Religions of the Provincial Department of Cult and Religion and the Provincial Council shall continue to encourage the monks under their supervision to study the Dharma Discipline to be proficient in and practice the Dharma Discipline to the best of their ability and to establish Have a meditation program to educate, train the mind to be calm and calm the greed, guilt and ignorance from the heart.
Eighth: The pagoda chiefs of all pagodas throughout the province must pay attention to the preservation of scriptures, manuscripts, rules and regulations, including the need to protect and preserve nature, preserve all ancient buildings to contribute to the promotion of culture, tourism and social environment in a consistent manner. According to the rules and progress of Buddhism. La Trobe University visits Cambodia
