(Phnom Penh): For the past 11 days, more than 100 Century Plaza vendors, representing more than 800 people, have been protesting to prevent the company from demolishing the Old Market to build a seven-storey shopping mall. In this way, the company gets a lot of benefits, but for them to lose completely and face difficulties, no access to supermarkets and no money to pay the bank.
Due to several days of protests and no solution, at 11 am on August 19, 2019, they closed the Boulevard of the Russian Federation in front of Century Plaza Market, Sangkat Kakap 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh. The traffic was so congested that the authorities agreed to withdraw.
At present, there are 802 mobile vendors without stalls and booths like them who are protesting, 341 right-hand stalls and 326 stallholders, and the total number of sales is 1,469 places.
On August 8, 2019, after being informed that the company was planning to demolish the market to build a new one, they were very surprised and immediately gathered to protest to ask not to There was dismantling and asking the authorities to help solve, but because there is no solution, on the morning of August 19, they decided to block the road in order to expedite the settlement as soon as possible.
Not only that, on the morning of August 20, they will gather again and gather in front of Samdech Techo's mansion so that Samdech can see and know about their hardships directly. Separately, the market company has issued a clear policy on the construction of Century Plaza shopping mall with 19 points and divided into 3 parts.
In the above content, also confirmed the various contracts between the company and the traders and the project to build a 7-storey market, as well as the lease of state land to create a temporary market at the children's park for all traders to sell temporarily. The construction of the new market will be completed by the 24-month deadline.
