Mr. Chhum Socheat led a forum to consult with people in Ta Sanh commune
(Battambang): On the morning of August 19, 2019, General Chhum Socheat, Chairman of the National Assistance Team in Samlot District, Battambang Province, led a working group to organize a consultation forum with people in Ta Sanh Commune, Samlot District, Battambang Province.
This forum is designed to listen to the opinions of the people as well as to find out about their challenges at the grassroots level in order to effectively participate in solving the people's problems.
Mr. Chhum Socheat said that in Samlot district, his team has already organized a consultation forum to listen to the concerns of people in five communes, including: Meanchey commune, Samlot commune, Kampong Lpou commune, Ta Tok commune, Ta Sanh commune. He confirmed that the working group will continue to open forums in two other communes, in O'Samrel commune, Song commune.
During the consultation forum in Ta Sanh commune, many people raised a number of issues, including issues related to basic rates, birth certificates, agriculture, lack of transportation and roads, land issues and so on. The people requested the national team to help Samlot district to solve their problems quickly.
In addition to listening to the concerns of the people on that occasion, the national working group to help Samlot district also disseminated the policy of the Royal Government and the progress throughout Cambodia to the people who voted and promised to send their problems to the Ministry. Relevant institutions to solve these problems better.
