The confirmation of the outgoing European Ambassador was made during the farewell ceremony of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia this morning, August 19, 2019.
According to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, after the meeting, Mr. George Idgar mentioned some of the tasks that he considered as important achievements in the four-year mission in Cambodia. George Edgar, who was also the British Ambassador to Cambodia in the past, praised Cambodia's strong progress.
Mr. George Edgar also highlighted the important work that the European Union has taken care of and encouraged to contribute to the development of Cambodia. Especially in the agricultural sector, which provides many benefits to the people and Cambodia. The outgoing ambassador confirmed that on Wednesday this week, the European Union will announce more than 100 million US dollars in assistance for the fisheries sector.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed this assistance because the Royal Government is also paying close attention to this fisheries work. In fact, in 2012, the Royal Government decided to cancel the fishing lot and give it to the community.
In this meeting, Mr. George Edgar highlighted the contribution to the field of climate change, which Cambodia is a country in Southeast Asia that is vulnerable to climate change, which is a global problem. In addition, the European Union will continue to assist in the forestry sector, which is currently a priority for the Royal Government of Cambodia in combating illegal deforestation.
The outgoing EU Ambassador also stated that the EU has made significant contributions to the success of the Khmer Rouge Tribunal.
The senior minister's new instructions came after the public reacted strongly to an official of the Siem Reap Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport pointing out the license plates of people's cars when inspecting the new technical specifications. Recently. After a public outcry, the female official was fined for moving out of her minute.
The seven new guidelines on strengthening the roles, duties and ethics of officials in providing services that Senior Minister Sun Chanthol just released on August 19, 2019 include:
1. To fulfill the role of a citizen servant with professional ethics, honesty, dignity and high responsibility.
2. To adhere to the attitude of being a good official as a servant of the people at all times, providing public services with warmth and respect, as well as making the people satisfied with all their work activities effectively.
3. To determine the working system by meeting the actual needs of the people who come to receive the best service.
4. To provide clear information on procedures and procedures in accordance with the provisions of the law and to solve problems for the people in a timely and efficient manner.
5. Participate in implementing mechanisms to reduce complex procedures and immunity to make it easier for people to access public services.
6. Do not use your role and position to threaten or cause difficulties to the people.
7. Must be able to coordinate and have good communication with the relevant ministries and institutions at all levels to fulfill the role of serving the people in the best way.
