(Phnom Penh): It is really sad for two boys living in Village 3, Koh Samrong Commune, Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province, who were the children of the victims who died in a traffic accident in front of Boeung Trabek High School in 2017 until today. On August 19, 2019, they have not yet received compensation from the perpetrators and insisted that the leaders intervene so that they can solve their daily lives.
The perpetrator was sentenced to three years in prison but sentenced to two years in prison and $ 30,000 in damages. The verdict is only on paper, especially compensation, but the real money has not yet fallen into the hands of the two poor little boys.
Mr. Sok Sam Ath continued, "So far, we have not received compensation according to the verdict." Sitting on his back, raising his arms and saluting with his two orphaned grandchildren, Mr. Sam Ath appealed to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to seek justice and expedite the settlement of the victims' families, especially the grandchildren who are living helplessly.
On February 1, 2018, Mr. Nou Veasna, Trial Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, sentenced to 3 years imprisonment with 2 years imprisonment and fined 10 million The state will require the plaintiff $ 40,000 in compensation for "negligent driving resulting in the death of another person."
