During the rainy season, Leang Dai commune residents ask for rain, an ancient tradition
Hai Voeun, a 70-year-old elder who initiated the rain prayer ceremony, said that the ceremony was a tradition of the villagers to wash their hands and never miss it, every year when it is raining or damaged. Drought and so on.
She added that this year observed that there was a severe drought, the villagers did not expect to receive too much rain after the rain ceremony, but the villagers still do to swear to the angels to take care of the planet. Provide rain to save rice fields and animal life.
The sacred power of Neak Pean temple has made the villagers there very confident because every time they ask for rain, it always rains. Mrs. Hay Voeun confirmed that while praying on the evening of the 13th, suddenly there was a heavy rain, drowning the villagers while there was no rain before. She continued that here, only vows are known.
Duong Chhom, one of the organizers of the event, said that the villagers believed in the ceremony and were unhappy when it was not held.
She said that this rain festival is not just about rain, it is about praying for peace for the whole Cambodian people. At the same time, as an elder and a person who strives to hold this ceremony, as Duong Chhom wants the younger generation to continue to hold this ceremony forever, because it is an ancient tradition as well as an identity of The villagers wash their hands too.
For this ceremony, according to the explanation of Mrs. Duong Chhom, it is very important to show the work to the younger generation in preserving the traditions of Khmer ancestors, as well as attracting tourists who want to know and explore in this ceremony.
