(Preah Vihear): To alleviate the hardships of farmers who suffered from drought caused damage to rice crops, this morning, August 19, 2019, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province brought a number of rice seeds. 5 tons to be distributed to 200 families in Kulen Cheung commune, Kulen district, Preah Vihear province.
The rice distribution ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and local authorities of Kulen District.
Mr. Peng Trida said that the rice seeds distributed to farmers now came with the support of the Cambodian Food Reserve System Program through the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Preah Vihear Provincial Disaster Committee. This is a light, non-seasonal rice variety (fragrant rice variety).
Mr. Peng Trida also expressed his condolences to our farmers who suffered from the drought that caused damage to rice crops. He said that in order to alleviate the shortage of farmers to earn money to buy rice seeds to grow again, the Provincial Department of Agriculture and local authorities have distributed rice seeds to our farmers for free.
The director of the department pointed out that the rice seed brought to distribute to farmers at this time is 5 tons to be distributed to 200 families, with each family receiving 25 kg. At the same time, he also advised our farmers to take the rice seeds received today to sow and transplant in time, because this is the rainy season with enough water.
