High-level Cambodian delegation to attend 40th ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly in Thailand for 6 days
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, will lead a high-level delegation of the Cambodian Parliament to attend the 40th ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) in Bangkok, Thailand from August 25 to 30. 2019.
The 40th ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly was held under the theme "Promoting Parliamentary Partnership for Sustainable Community Development". This is according to the announcement of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly on August 19.
During the General Assembly, there will be meetings of various IPA committees attended by the President of the National Assembly and members of the delegation, including the Executive Committee Meeting, the Plenary Meeting of the Women's Parliamentary Committee (WAIPA). ) Political Committee meetings, Economic Committee meetings, Social Affairs Committee meetings, Organizing Committee meetings and meetings between IPA and observer countries.
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) is an inter-parliamentary body representing the legislatures of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), which includes Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam and the Philippines.
According to the statement, the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly is a gathering of the voices of the people of the ASEAN Community, ASEAN's partner in advancing the goal of a single ASEAN Community. The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly is held annually by the member countries in alphabetical order of the names of the countries in Latin letters.
