Outgoing Japanese Ambassador: Cambodia-Japan relations have grown steadily in terms of diplomacy, economy and trade
Mr. Heidi Hahori Nouchi said so during his courtesy call and farewell to Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia at the National Assembly building this morning, August 19, 2019.
The Japanese Ambassador emphasized that his diplomatic mission in Cambodia was at a time when the Cambodian economy was growing and Cambodia-Japan relations were growing steadily in terms of diplomacy, economy and trade. In particular, Cambodia and Japan have exchanged visits between the legislature and the executive.
He said his diplomatic mission in Cambodia over the past three years had been successful. Success due to the support and facilitation of the President of the National Assembly. In that regard, Samdech urged the National Assembly of Cambodia and Japan to exchange visits with each other.
Samdech Heng Samrin thanked Japan for its support and assistance to Cambodia so far. Samdech said that during his stay in Cambodia, the Ambassador saw the process of implementing Cambodia's democracy. Cambodia has fully implemented a multi-party liberal democracy. He thanked Japan for its support for electoral reform and the promotion of human rights in Cambodia.
The President asked Japan to support Cambodia more, especially the development of human resources and capacity building so that Cambodia can develop the country to grow.
