Ros Sovacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, told Fresh News that the ministry had already prepared and qualified for the exam, the district exam officer and the subjects for the exam. In other words, everything goes according to plan, nothing changes. However, only one examination center in Kampot province was relocated due to flooding.
Mr. Ros Sovacha said, "The preparation of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports for the high school examination on August 19-20, 2019 is ready as planned, while the 404 boxes were transported. To the examination center is ready.
"One of the districts in Kampot province was allowed to change its cause due to the floods," he said. "Apart from that, there is no impact, but after this change, the total number of constituencies is still 202."
In order to make the exam a success as planned, the Ministry has deployed a total of 17,430 officers in charge of the exam, including 606 subordinates, 2,405 student assistants, 10,631 custodians, and 202 district presidents. The building inspection committee has 1,181 members and the central committee has 2,405 members.
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that the officers in charge of the exam have traveled to their respective destinations and are ready to welcome the candidates and fulfill their roles and responsibilities.
During the in-depth reform mission of Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, since 2014, the Anti-Corruption Unit has always sent observers to monitor and observe this exam. But in 2019, there will be no observers from the Anti-Corruption Unit to monitor and observe the exam.
Despite the absence of observers from the Anti-Corruption Unit, the Ministry of Education claimed that the exam was still conducted on the basis of accuracy, transparency and fairness on the principle of "those who know".
"If there is a case of corruption at any stage of the high school examination, the Ministry of Education will continue to cooperate with the ACU by taking action in accordance with the law in force," he said.
Mr. Ros Sovacha also claimed that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports continues to strictly enforce the provisions that come into force with the conduct of candidates and educators.
The spokesperson of the Ministry of Education also thanked all stakeholders for continuing cooperation with the Ministry, including the Anti-Corruption Unit, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Tourism, the Ministry of Health through health departments in all capitals. Provinces as well as pagodas and local authorities.
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that "success in the high school diploma exam depends on the cooperation of all parties involved."
Please note that the exam on August 19 for science classes include: History, Biology, Chemistry and Foreign Languages. Social science classes include: Earth and Ecology, History, Geography, and Foreign Languages.
August 20 for science classes include: Khmer Literature, Physics and Mathematics. The social sciences include subjects: mathematics, ethics, civics, and Khmer literature.
