Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture Distributes 20 Tons of Rice to 440 Drought-Stricken Families in Chey Sen District
(Preah Vihear): The Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province, in cooperation with Chey Sen District Authority, on August 18, 2019 distributed 20 tons of rice seeds to 440 families from 2 communes: Putra and Khum. Struggle Chey Sen District, Preah Vihear Province. The ceremony was attended by Mr. Peng Trida, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Ros Heng, Governor of Chey Sen District and many other leaders.
Mr. Peng Trida said that the rice seeds that are being distributed to farmers now are supported by the Cambodian Food Reserve System Program through the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Preah Vihear Provincial Disaster Committee.
The Director of the Department further stated that this is a high consideration from Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, in accordance with the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Improve the living standards of farmers by providing both material and technical support.
Mr. Peng Trida added that the rice seeds that are given to farmers at this time are non-seasonal rice varieties (fragrant rice varieties). For distribution to 360 families in Putra commune, with each family receiving 2 bags equal to 50 kg, and distribution to 80 families in Su commune, with each family receiving 1 bag of rice equal to 25 kg. .
Today, traffic police inspected 11,481 motorcyclists, forcing 2,913 to wear helmets
(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police has launched a nationwide campaign to promote the wearing of helmets for the full month, and on August 18, 2019, the traffic police force in 15 capitals and provinces inspected a number of motorcyclists. 11,481 people were forced to wear helmets, 2,913 or 25 percent. This is according to the report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department, which was obtained by Fresh News.
Please be informed that General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner, has issued an order for the traffic police throughout the country to start taking measures to promote the wearing of helmets to all motorcyclists and tricycle drivers.
This measure is implemented nationwide, with the requirement to find a helmet to be worn before being allowed to travel without penalty for one month from July 19, 2019 onwards.
