Tbong Khmum Governor Thanks to Chinese Volunteer Doctors for Free Medical Treatment and Free Rice
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, together with Suong Municipality Authority and Provincial Health Department, this morning, August 18, 2019, paid a courtesy call on 313 volunteer doctors from China. Visited for medical treatment, provided 10 kg of medicine and rice to about 2,000 people in Suong City for free in the area of Wat Chrey Bit Meas in Suong Sangkat, Suong City.
On that occasion, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, on behalf of the guardians of the people throughout the province, expressed his pleasure, welcome, gratitude and appreciation to the team of volunteer doctors from China who came to provide warmth, love and humanity in the field of health to Citizens in the province.
He also called on people to take good care of their health, take care of their children, be very careful about dengue fever and keep clean, drink clean, eat clean and live clean to avoid diseases.
It should be noted that this group of volunteer doctors from China will visit for 5 days in 5 cities and districts in Tbong Khmum province, providing general treatment, providing free medicine and 10 kg of rice per person. More than 10,000 people.
According to Mr. Keo Vannak, Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department, for the participation of various organizations in the field of health in a humanitarian manner, focusing only on practical medical services in the first six months of this year, a group of doctors visited Illness to people throughout Tbong Khmum province.
