(Phnom Penh): As planned, nearly 120,000 candidates will take the Baccalaureate exam on Monday, August 19, 2019 tomorrow, as the measures on the exam are confirmed to be strictly implemented and Strictly adhere to the principle of "know is stuck" even in the absence of the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) observers.
Ros Sovacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, told Fresh News on August 18, 2019 that the ministry has already prepared and qualified for the examination and examination center and subject. That is, everything will go according to plan, nothing will change. However, only one examination center in Kampot province was relocated due to flooding.
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that the officials in charge of the exam have traveled to their respective destinations and are ready to welcome candidates and fulfill their roles and responsibilities.
In the mission of in-depth reform of the failed exam of Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports since 2014, observers of the Anti-Corruption Unit have always been involved in monitoring and observing this exam. But in 2019, the Anti-Corruption Unit will not deploy observers, but will send civil servants to participate.
Despite the absence of the Anti-Corruption Unit observers, the Ministry of Education claimed that the exam was still conducted on the basis of accuracy, transparency and fairness on the principle of "those who know".
Please note that the exam on August 19 tomorrow for science classes include: History, Biology, Chemistry and Foreign Languages. Social science classes include: Earth and Ecology, History, Geography, and Foreign Languages.
August 20 for science classes include subjects: Khmer literature, physics and mathematics. The social sciences include subjects: mathematics, ethics, civics, and Khmer literature.
