The Minister made the remarks while presiding over the closing ceremony of the traditional international boat race "Dragon Boat" for the Tonle Sap Lake Regional Championship held on the afternoon of Saturday, August 17. In 2019, with the participation of the administration of Pursat Provincial Hall, senior officials of the Cambodian Canoeing and Roofing Federation, representatives of the private sector and a large number of people.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the Cambodian Canoeing and Roofing Federation for cooperating with the Pursat Provincial Administration in organizing the above event successfully to provide opportunities for athletes to work. Unleash the talents, measure the technical abilities that have been trained in the past, as well as provide entertainment to people and tourists of all nationalities who come to visit and travel through Pursat.
Mr. Pan Sosak emphasized that "the victory that the players get now is really inseparable from the regular training effort combined with the struggle to respect good discipline, ethics and technical standards in the game." .
The Minister also briefed the ceremony on the progress of national economic growth and social achievements under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen, which resulted in Cambodia receiving high praise and trust from the community. International to host the Southeast Asian Games (SEA Games) in 2023.
