TOP NEWS: Cambodia issues statement in support of Chinese government's necessary measures to maintain peace, order and security in Hong Kong
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on the evening of August 17, 2019, issued a statement expressing its support for all necessary actions of the Chinese government to maintain peace, public order and Security in Hong Kong.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated:
1. Cambodia adheres to the "One China Policy" and considers the evolving situation in Hong Kong as an internal affair of the People's Republic of China.
2. Cambodia supports all necessary actions of the Government of the People's Republic of China and the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region to maintain peace, public order, national security and social coexistence in accordance with laws and regulations. Of the country and international execution.
3. Cambodia wants to see a return to normalcy as soon as possible for the peaceful life of all Hong Kong people.
The statement from the Royal Government of Cambodia comes as Hong Kong erupts in protests against the extradition, which is suspected of inciting a color revolution in the region.
The following is a statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs:
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh Visits Elder Bou Thong, who is being treated at Calmette Hospital
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of August 17, 2019, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, led the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense to pay a courtesy call on Elder Bou Thong, Advisor to Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum. President of the Senate of Cambodia at Calmette Hospital, Phnom Penh.
On this occasion, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh expressed his condolences to Elder Bou Thong, an dignitary who sacrificed his life and energy in the cause of the motherland, and also paid a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister. Of Cambodia as well.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh wished the elder good health as soon as possible from all diseases and longevity, as well as happiness and prosperity forever.
In response, Mr. Bou Thong expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh for taking the opportunity to visit him to the hospital, which shows his mutual respect and love. .
Despite being in bed in the hospital, Elder Bou Thong never forgot the political situation in the country and the developments along the border with Cambodia's neighbors, showing his patriotic spirit. For Cambodia and all Cambodians as well.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng will lead three ministers to visit Germany at the end of next month to exchange experiences on sub-national transfer of power
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, will lead an inter-ministerial delegation, including three other ministers, to visit the German Federation at the end of September to explore and exchange experiences related to the transfer. Power to the sub-national level.
The three ministers who attended the visit were Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Environment, Say Sam Al, and Mam Bun Heng, Minister of Health. In addition, there are some senior officials.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Interior confirmed to Fresh News on August 17, 2019 that the main purpose of the visit of the Cambodian inter-ministerial delegation to the German Federation is to exchange experiences related to lower-level administrative reform. The nation that the Royal Government of Cambodia is currently striving to implement is decentralization and deconcentration reform.
During the visit, the Cambodian delegation also met with some senior officials of the German Federation, met with some MPs involved in decentralization work, met with some governors and mayors to find out more about their practice. It is good to implement the work of the Central Committee in Cambodia effectively.
In addition, there are visits to a number of locations to learn about health management, education, vocational training, natural resources, forest management, environmental management in each region being implemented in Germany.
Wife and husband were seriously injured in a traffic accident between a car driven by a Chinese man and a motorbike in Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province
(Preah Sihanouk): The wife died at the scene and the husband was seriously injured in a traffic accident between a car and a motorbike on National Road No. 4 in O Ta Sek village, O Oknha Heng commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province in the afternoon. August 17, 2019.
The local official confirmed that the motorcyclist, Hem Hean, 50, her husband (severely injured) and the passenger, Chhem Khom, 49, his wife, died immediately at the scene. Both of them live in Smach Deng village, Ream commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
Authorities handed over the bodies of the victims to their families for traditional rites, while the victims were sent to a private clinic for treatment. Interrogation at the Prey Nup District Police Inspectorate temporarily.
Prey Nup District Deputy Inspector of Traffic Planning told Fresh News on the evening of August 17, 2019 that his specialized force is building a case to send the driver of the car and its passengers with evidence to the Sihanoukville Provincial Police for further action.
