Meanwhile, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen appealed to all people with the following content:
* Take good care of your health to reduce household expenses by living hygienically, drinking boiled water and eating right, avoiding leukemia, heart disease, arthritis or diabetes.
* Clean the environment around the house, eliminate mosquito nets, sleep under mosquito nets, avoid dengue fever - malaria, and if you have a fever or any symptoms, hurry to the hospital for immediate treatment, avoid prolonging the time to affect life.
* Pregnant women should go for regular prenatal check-ups, follow the doctor's instructions and give birth at the nearest health center. With a doctor to prevent mother-to-child transmission.
* Please join together to eliminate drugs, alcohol and gambling of all kinds to promote the policy of safe villages and communes.
* People should consider traffic safety, which is a challenge that causes death and disability every day.
Please note that the gifts distributed to each family include: 30 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish, 1 kit (mosquito net, blanket, sarong, krama, T-shirt) and a budget of 10,000 Riels. Cambodian food experts: In order to process high quality food, it is necessary to know the nutrients in raw materials first
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chrun Rithy, Technical and Human Resources Director of the Cambodian Food Science and Technology Association, said that in order to process a high quality food, we need to know the ingredients in the product to be processed first. Food processing must be done to have enough nutrients, safe and beneficial to consumers.
Mr. Chrun Rithy said this on the afternoon of August 17, 2019, when he was invited as a speaker in the business matching forum for food processing and agricultural products 2019 at Koh Pich Exhibition Center, Building A. The forum was also attended by Dr. Pheng Vutha, Deputy Director of Prek Leap Agricultural School, Dr. Sreng Navin, Director of the Environment and Food Safety Laboratory, as well as speakers and many other participants.
He added that if we process without knowing how to process properly, it will lose nutrients and vitamins without giving us the food we process.
Interior Ministry spokesman dismisses VOA coverage of Chinese abduction and deportation case
(Phnom Penh): A spokesman for the Ministry of Interior on August 17, 2019, issued a statement dismissing VOA's coverage of the Chinese deportation in connection with the crime. Crime back to China. This is according to a press release from a spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, obtained by Fresh News this afternoon.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Interior confirmed to the national and international public as follows:
* First, the arrest of Chinese nationals involved in the commission of crimes and the expulsion of these Chinese nationals from the Kingdom of Cambodia was made in the spirit of a memorandum between the Ministry of Interior of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Interior. Public security of the People's Republic of China and in accordance with the Immigration Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Second, the perpetrators arrested and deported from the Kingdom of Cambodia are those who have an arrest warrant from the competent authorities of China, which will be subject to further legal proceedings to seek justice. Victims in China are not released.
* Third: Foreign offenders arrested and deported from the Kingdom of Cambodia in accordance with the Immigration Law will be blacklisted by the Immigration Control System and will not be allowed to enter. Cambodia again.
* Fourth, in the past, the Cambodian authorities have arrested and deported other foreigners involved in the crime in their own country in accordance with the spirit of the memorandum between the two countries. From 2014 to July 2019, Cambodian authorities deported more than 2,700 Chinese nationals, a number that could be a major burden on the national budget if they were detained in Cambodia.
* Fifth: All operations to crack down on crime and arrest the perpetrators, whether the perpetrators are Cambodian citizens or foreigners, the competent authorities of the Kingdom of Cambodia always investigate, research and collect all the legal evidence first.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Interior would like to categorically reject the statements made by some analysts on this issue, which lacks a clear information and legal basis, which could confuse the national and international public about the measures and legal process. The way of the competent authority of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Interior would like to confirm that the Ministry of Interior will continue to work closely with stakeholders to ensure security, social security and public order to all citizens.
Please read the details in the press release of the spokesperson of the Ministry of Interior:
