According to the agreement signed on Saturday, a council will be formed this weekend, consisting of six members from the opposition and five from the Sudanese military council, which will lead the country until the election. One is made. In addition, both the opposition and the military have agreed to change the council chairman every three years, with a civilian prime minister likely to be appointed next week.
