A 12-room, two-story school building at Ta Kream Secondary School, Banan District, Battambang Province, was laid to build a high school
(Battambang): On the morning of August 17, 2019, in the campus of Ta Kream Secondary School in O'Pong Moan Village, Ta Kream Commune, Banan District, Battambang Province, a groundbreaking ceremony was held for the construction of a 12-storey building. Room upgraded to high school.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Sok Phal, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the National Task Force for Banan District, and was attended by about 1,000 teachers, residents and students.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Sok Phal said that this new achievement will be used to meet the needs of local people, especially to help the children of school-age people to study in the new school year.
"We have good schools, good places to study, especially good teachers, we will not have students drop out, instead we will make our students want to study more," he said.
Mr. Thong Khon: We are tired of maintaining peace and stability rather than tired of fighting
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Baray and Taing Kork District Assistance Working Group, Kampong Thom Province, once again called on the people to continue to participate in maintaining the current peace and stability by Mr. He stressed that we are tired of managing security and stability better than we are tired of fighting.
Minister Thong Khon made the remarks during a meeting with villagers in Kork Trabek village in Sralao commune, Taing Kork district, while the minister, government officials and the team visited the Vesna Candle Parade. To give to monks at Wat Kork Trabek on August 17, 2019.
Mr. Thong Khon told the people that in order to save the country as it is today, this miserable Cambodia has gone through a lot of problems since the Khmer Rouge era, Pol Pot, Cambodia took decades to rebuild the country. Under the leadership of the Royal Government of the Cambodian People's Party, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of this poor country has returned to full peace and stability.
He added that, however, the people in this era of peace must join the Royal Government with Samdech Techo Hun Sen to maintain the existing peace for a long time to come because the maintenance of peace is. On all citizens.
Minister Thong Khon said: "We are tired of maintaining peace, stability, rather than tired of war. We must continue to work together to prevent unscrupulous people from inspiring and creating a color revolution in our country. "To a chaotic war like in the past."
Mr. Thong Khon cited the example of the color revolution as well as the war crises in some countries that have led those countries to ruin, only tragedy can not find peace.
He added that in the future, the authorities of Kampong Thom and Taing Kork districts will distribute land to all people in Kork Trabek village with about 120 plots, but he requested the people Please leave that land for future use and enjoyment by your children, do not resell it and demand more land from the authorities, which can lead to other problems.
(Kratie): On the evening of August 17, 2019, the Kratie Provincial Court issued a detention order for Tycoon Kong Kreung and his son-in-law in connection with a forest crime in Kratie province's Snuol district. This is according to the detention order issued by Mr. Meng Tony, Investigating Judge of Kratie Provincial Court, which was received by Fresh News this evening.
In the detention order of the court, Oknha Kong Kreung and his son-in-law were charged with "harvesting non-timber forest products without a license and exporting non-timber forest products without a license" in Chrap Thmey village, Snuol commune, Snuol district during the year. 2018 and 2019 in accordance with the provisions of Article 98, paragraph 2, point 1 and point 7 of the Law on Forestry.
