(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police has launched a nationwide campaign to promote helmet wearing for a full month, and on August 17, 2019, the traffic police force in 14 capitals and provinces inspected a number of motorcyclists. Of the 6,106, 2,291 were forced to wear helmets, accounting for 38 percent. This is according to the report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department, which was obtained by Fresh News.
