By: Chao Chak Smok, Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province On August 17, 2019, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan was elected as the Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Committee, Tbong Khmum Branch, Second Mandate.
(Tbong Khmum): The Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Tbong Khmum Province on the morning of August 17, 2019, held the second mandate Branch Meeting (2019-2025) under the chairmanship of Mrs. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross on behalf of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Seak Leng, Honorary Vice President of the Branch, Mr. Cheam Chansophorn, Chairman of the Branch Committee of the second mandate and Chairman of the Assembly, as well as the Honorary Committee, full members, technical officers, headquarters, observers, relevant departments. Branch Executive Team and CRC Youth Group.
In this second mandate meeting, the Cambodian Red Cross, chaired by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, appointed Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Honorary Chairman of the Branch, and Mr. Sak Leng, Honorary Vice President and 22 Vice Chairmen.
The second mandate meeting was held for the following main purposes:
The second mandate meeting elected Mr. Cheam Chansophorn as Chairman of the Branch Committee, Mr. Hak Sok Makara, Permanent Vice Chairman of the Branch Committee, Mr. Kun Sophea and Mr. Keo Vannak as Vice Chairman, Mr. Sok Pheakdey, Treasurer and Mr. Mao Dong as Secretary. Branch Committee.
Follow the guidelines of the Cambodian Red Cross to successfully fulfill humanitarian duties, maintain unity within the Branch Committee and accept consultation with the Branch Honors Committee and unite to solve challenges with high responsibility and lead The direction of the branch operation team to perform the tasks in accordance with the strategy of the Cambodian Red Cross.
Speaking on that occasion, Ms. Pum Chantyny conveyed the important recommendations of the President to the Branch Committee, which really promotes the spirit of responsibility in front of the Central Committee to pay attention to the implementation of the strategy of the National Association, continue the governor to guide the executive team. To all sub-branches to work hard in a team spirit, implement in unison and help each other.
