Cambodian Microfinance Association Statement on LICADHO and STT Distortion Report and Demand Reporters
The Cambodian Microfinance Association (MICA) has confirmed that after a preliminary review of the report of LICADHO and STT under the heading "Damage to mortgages" released on August 7, 2019, That this report is a complete distortion of the lending practices of microfinance institutions (MFIs) in Cambodia.
At the same time, the Cambodian Microfinance Association requires the authors of this report to cooperate with the association in order to provide a complete picture of the reality of lending in the microfinance sector.
The Cambodian Microfinance Association claims that the reports of these two organizations present a very negative picture of microfinance through the use of a small sample with an image of an anonymous borrower. Defame the entire microfinance sector in a false and negative image.
The Cambodian Microfinance Association stated that it really wanted to find out the truth about this report and worked with the association members to try to investigate the background of a handful of case studies presented in this report. From negative results from a small sample only.
The Cambodian Microfinance Association added that on behalf of the microfinance sector in Cambodia as a whole, it has implemented strict guidelines designed to avoid any adverse events and has also regularly monitored the implementation of lending to Protect against practices that lack professional ethics.
