Kampot Provincial Police Commissioner General Phkay Pi Mao Chanthurith told Fresh News that Nuth Pech, 63, a former member of Chhuk District Council and former Deputy Chief Executive Officer of Chhuk District, Kampot Province, was arrested. His police force arrested him at around 11 am this morning in connection with an illegal gathering at the local level.
According to the General Commissioner, the accused was transported from Chhouk district to the provincial police commission by his authority and sent to the court for legal action.
According to the arrest warrant issued by the Kampot Provincial Court, Nuth Pech was charged with "not complying with the court's decision (against the Supreme Court's ruling) and conspiring to commit a crime" in Prey Samnang Leu village. Khchay Khang Cheung, Dang Tong district, Kampot province, in April, May 2019.
