The following is the Senate announcement: The chief abbot of Wat Dey Thmey in Oddar Meanchey province killed a man and threw him into the forest, because the victim knew the story of a monk stealing a girl
(Oddar Meanchey): The chief abbot of Dey Thmey pagoda in Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, brutally killed a man and threw him into the forest in order to eliminate the evidence.
The General Commissioner further stated that the reason for the murder was because the monk was angry with the victim, who was a motorbike taxi driver, who knew that he had stolen a mistress, which was against the monk's discipline. Another reason is that the killer monk also borrowed more than $ 4,000 from the victim, but no repayment.
The General Commissioner described that on August 14, 2019, the police received a complaint from the victim's family that she had lost her husband and ran away on a motodup.
On the morning of August 15, the victim's motorcycle and the victim's clothes were found dumped on a bridge west of Anlong Veng town along the highway in Kampot Prey. The motorcycle was stained with blood.
After that, the specialized force conducted a thorough investigation until the afternoon of August 16, 2019, the police identified two suspects, one a monk, a pagoda chief and the other a brother of God. Priests.
The commissioner further stated that after finding the body and based on the confession, the specialized police force asked the cult department to invite the monks to perform a Buddhist decapitation ceremony and make arrests according to the procedure.
