Tomorrow, the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes will send Duke Kong Kreung and his son-in-law to court.
(Kratie): On the morning of August 17, 2019, tomorrow, the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resources Crimes will send Duke Kong Kreung and his son-in-law to court after being arrested in connection with forestry crimes. This is according to the official of the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes, which confirmed to Fresh News.
The arrest of Duke Kong Kreung and his son-in-law took place under the direct command of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Chairman of the National Commission, and with the coordination of the National Prosecutor's Office. Kratie Provincial Armed Forces. This is according to Brigadier General Eng Hee, spokesman for the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes.
He claimed that according to the Code of Criminal Procedure, in response to the necessary requirements of the investigation, judicial police officers could detain individuals suspected of involvement in crimes.
It should be noted that on August 15, 2019, the working group of the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes summoned Duke Kong Kreung to comment on forest crimes at the Kratie Provincial Gendarmerie Command. Oknha Kong Kreung, a resident of Dey Chrap Thmey village, 2 Thnou commune, Snuol district, Kratie province, the owner of Mattasat handicraft factory, must come to explain at the appointed time and bring the relevant documents with him.
