Mr. Heng Sok Kong said this morning, August 16, 2019, when he chaired a business matching forum for food processing and agricultural products 2019 at the Koh Pich Exhibition Center.
The forum was also attended by Mr. Sam Sereyroth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Oknha Sok Dara, Vice President of the Coalition of Cambodian Small and Medium Enterprises Association, Mr. Seang Sopanha, Acting President of the Young Entrepreneurs Association of Cambodia, as well as many other speakers and participants. Also.
Mr. Heng Sok Kong said that currently, the agro-industrial sector in Cambodia is growing and growing rapidly, and along with the growing momentum, there are still some shortcomings, especially in the processing of materials. Originally to be a finished product.
He said that the business match between raw material producers and processors is very important to make it more valuable to farmers so that they can earn more if we Produce raw materials and export at once, it is really a lot of loss, especially if we produce and we process ourselves into finished products and export, it is very profitable.
Mr. Heng Sok Kong added that, in fact, rice products if we export at once is not very profitable, but if we process into other products, we will get more profit from those products and more Both get more value added.
The official of the Ministry of Industry added that in order to help small and medium enterprises to grow further, the Royal Government of Cambodia has also introduced a number of measures, such as a sub-decree on tax exemption for the first two years of business start-ups. Sub-decree on tax exemption for small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in some priority areas between 3 and 5 years and many other tariff facilitations.
Oknha Sok Dara, Vice President of the Coalition of Small and Medium Enterprises Association of Cambodia, also said that in the context of competition and the opening of free markets, all kinds of goods have been capturing the market for Cambodian products, especially food products that require Great attention from Cambodian producers, otherwise even the local market we can not maintain, not to mention the export market.
He added that based on this need and demand that food processing enterprises and agricultural producers, experts and suppliers and other service providers must meet to discuss how to help produce with high standards and quality. Will reduce costs to serve the business development in the future and ready to pave the way for exports in the near future.
Oknha Sok Dara stated that the growth of the food processing and agricultural products sector not only makes each enterprise more profitable, but also helps to create a bigger market for farmers. Without having to rely entirely on the export of raw materials from neighboring countries, which leads to a huge loss of value added.
