Samdech Techo Hun Sen Issues a Sub-Decree Determining the Working Rule of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) The spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia has been clearly defined by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The Sub-Decree on the Organization and Functioning of the Spokesperson Unit of the Royal Government of Cambodia was signed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on August 15, 2019. This sub-decree has 7 chapters and 14 articles.
In the sub-decree obtained by Fresh News on August 16, 2019, it was stated that the establishment of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit for the effectiveness of information work to inform the national and international public about the work, achievements and policies of the Royal Government.
The sub-decree also states that the composition of the spokesperson unit of the Royal Government consists of an official in charge of the spokesperson of the Royal Government as the chairperson of the unit and the spokesperson of each ministry and institution as the deputy chairperson and members determined by the decision of Royal Government. The Government Spokesperson's Unit consists of advisors and assistants, and the Vice-Chairmen and members shall be appointed by the Chairman.
Article 3 of the sub-decree stipulates that the Vice-Chairman and the members of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit shall attend the meeting at the invitation of the Chairman. The Head of the Government Spokesperson's Unit can invite dignitaries, representatives of relevant ministries and institutions and other experts to participate in solving work and request cooperation as needed in the field of information.
The Government Spokesperson's Unit consists of a secretariat located at the Council of Ministers and has three subordinate departments: the Department of Administration and Finance, the Department of Public Affairs and Training, and the Department of Information, Archives and Digital Technology.
It should be noted that the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit consists of Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, accompanied by 5 Vice-Chairmen and 25 other members, all of whom are spokespersons from various ministries. The unit regularly holds press conferences on social issues every Thursday.
