Donald Trump is due to pay a visit to Denmark in September, during which he will meet with the Danish Prime Minister and Greenland leaders. Greenland has an area of 2.1 million square kilometers (excluding glaciers), the same size as Saudi Arabia, the world's top oil tycoon.
In addition, Greenland belongs to Denmark as it is located closer to North America than Europe and has a larger area and glacier coverage in northeastern Canada. Although much of the island is icy, it contains enormous amounts of natural resources, including oil and gas, worth tens of billions of barrels. Greenland also has 10 percent of the world's freshwater resources.
But most likely under the Greenland ice sheet is a rare resource called Rare Earth, which is critical for today's high-tech industry, from manufacturing to smartphones to military equipment and more. Weapons.
Minister Thong Khon Recommends to Siem Reap Provincial Administration and Relevant Authorities to Continue Efforts to Manage and Develop Tourism Destinations Effectively
(Siem Reap): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, recommended the Siem Reap Provincial Administration, especially the Siem Reap Municipality, APSARA Authority and relevant institutions to continue to work together to develop the Siem Reap-Angkor tourism destination effectively, sustainably and responsibly.
The recommendation was made at a meeting on strengthening the management and development of Siem Reap-Angkor tourism destinations at Siem Reap Provincial Hall on the morning of August 16, 2019, with the participation of Mr. Ing Hoeun, Chairman of Siem Reap Provincial Council. Mr. Sok Sangva, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, Member of Siem Reap Tourism Development Committee, civil servants and related parties.
On that occasion, Mr. Thong Khon requested the Siem Reap municipal authorities to work hard to free up the city's sidewalks, leaving the sidewalks in the city for tourists to travel and shop easily.
At the same time, he further advised the provincial and municipal administrations of Siem Reap, APSARA Authority and relevant departments and units to continue to work together to solve some problems such as:
* Must continue to strive to repair a lot of roads in the city, prepare good street lighting, beautify, strengthen public order, how to organize public traffic, travel of citizens and tourists by drawing a good traffic direction in the city. Avoid congestion and speed up the preparation of new parking lots.
* To consider the problem of solid waste, liquid, sanitation and the environment in the whole city of Siem Reap to be effective, to discuss and resolve with the waste collection company completely, do not let the company take the government hostage.
* Efforts must be made to prevent and curb the construction of buildings that violate the guidelines of this heritage city conservation principle.
* Must strive to continue to improve the Siem Reap River with beauty and attractiveness.
* For tourism services and businesses of all kinds must continue to pay attention to strengthen the quality to stop selling fake goods and souvenirs to tourists, which leads to the disgrace of national honor and tourism destinations by taking educational and administrative measures Come practice strictly.
* Eliminate any noise that affects the guests' stay in the hotel or guest accommodation.
* In addition to the night market, consider creating a more orderly nightlife venue, especially should create a luxury sales area for Chinese tourists. For European guests, there must also be entertainment for them.
* Continue to increase the training of human resources in the tourism sector to meet the needs of the tourism sector.
* Consideration should be given to setting up tourist ports in floating communities in a proper and standardized manner.
* Continue to pay attention to providing good hospitality to tourists so that they get warmth and so that they can help spread the word to other tourists.
* The Minister expressed his support for the APSARA Authority, which is strengthening and improving sanitation in the Angkor area. At the same time, he also asked the APSARA Authority to consider creating new attractive tourism products at night appropriately.
The Minister emphasized that the issue of tourism security and safety is a major issue and a fundamental issue in the development of the Siem Reap-Angkor area, which all must continue to strive to further strengthen.
Minister Thong Khon briefed the meeting on the preparation of the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan, which has been actively promoted, which will be completed by February 2020.
With the support of the APSARA Authority, Mr. Ung Hoeun also advised all officials to pay attention to the effective and responsible work by holding regular inspection meetings.
Minister Thong Khon, APSARA Authority and Siem Reap Provincial Authority also agreed to continue to meet at least once every three months, inviting stakeholders from the private sector and development partners to participate. Inauguration of E-Commerce of Cambodia Post, Minister Tram Iv Tek requested to support and use together
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Intellectual Property Association on August 16, 2019 organized a meeting and election of the council and the president of the association of its second mandate. The conference was held at the Angkor Wat auditorium of the Ministry of Commerce.
This conference is an opportunity for the members of the association to share their knowledge about Mr. Varuthsan, Mr. Op Rady and Mr. Sim Satta, who are also highly experienced intellectual property officers in the context of the association, the legal framework. National and international intellectual property, especially the benefits of the Beijing Convention and the Ben Convention, to its members.
It should also be noted that the Cambodian Intellectual Property Association was registered and established in 2016, and in the first term for 3 years, Mr. Pech Ang was the President of the Association and the Council was led by Mr. Ny Vichet.
In the first mandate, the association organized more than 17 seminars on its own and cooperated with national and international institutions to disseminate intellectual property law and strengthen the capacity of intellectual property agencies as well as other stakeholders.
In addition, representatives of the Association also gave lectures on intellectual property 6 times in the program organized by the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, Royal School, Judges, Trade Training Institute and the National Committee for Combating Counterfeit Goods.
In addition, the members of the Association also participated in many meetings and participated in the interpretation and dissemination of intellectual property laws on various television programs, as well as participate in the development of laws and activities that are beneficial to the protection of intellectual property in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In the second mandate, there are two candidates for the presidency of the association, of which Ms. Seng Vouch Hun is elected as the president of the association. For the Board of Directors, there are 9 candidates, of which 7 are elected as members of the council, which is chaired by Mr. Panha Pheng Thea.
