In the above crackdown operation, under the coordination of Deputy Prosecutor Song Chhavorn and led the crackdown by Mr. Ros Sopheak, Deputy Governor of Chbar Ampov District, together with the Chbar Ampov II Police Force.
According to the authorities, as a result of the crackdown, the authorities detained four men and women, including three gambling addicts, including a female chief, and confiscated several computers.
Authorities said that after the command agreed to crack down, the equipment and four people were brought to Chbar Ampov district to proceed with the procedure.
Victory Monument will be partially expanded in the second phase
(Phnom Penh): The Victory Monument, a symbol of Cambodia's win-win politics, will be partially expanded in the second phase of construction.
The second meeting on the construction of the Win-Win Monument was held this morning, August 16, 2019, chaired by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the Committee for the Construction of the Win-Win Monument. Participation from representatives of other relevant ministries and institutions.
When construction will be expanded, the Victory Monument Construction Commission has not yet announced.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh told reporters after the meeting that the expansion in the second phase includes the decoration of sculptures that are still lacking, the construction of a lotus pond behind the Victory Monument, as well as the construction of a new building. .
Samdech emphasized that this Victory Monument will become a historic building for storing history and documents that make the country peaceful and developed to this day.
In this second phase meeting, the working group and relevant units are committed to cooperate more strongly to make this historic building of Cambodia even more prominent.
It should be noted that the construction of the Win-Win Monument started in February 2016 on an area of 8 hectares in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, north of Phnom Penh, which was inaugurated on December 29, 2018. 20 years of win-win politics.
This monument is a symbol of the peace that Cambodia has achieved after the end of decades of civil war, and this monument has become a legacy for future generations.
According to the latest report on the construction of the Victory Monument, in the first seven months of 2019, the working group visited about 2 million local and foreign delegations, national and international public, and studied the population. The average daily visit is 500 to 1,500 people. In particular, on national holidays and public holidays, the number of visitors increased significantly from 1,000 to 3,000 people per day.
