Watch the video and picture: The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia strives to attract microfinance institutions in Cambodia into the securities sector
(Phnom Penh): After two MFIs entered the bond market, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia continued its efforts to attract other microfinance institutions to attract their capital. Through the securities sector.
In fact, on August 16, 2019, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SECC) in collaboration with the Microfinance Association of Cambodia organized a workshop on "Sources of Financing through the Securities Market for Microfinance Institutions in Cambodia" chaired by Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and Mr. Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia.
A press release from the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia states that the workshop was organized for the purpose of disseminating the procedures for raising capital through the issuance of equity securities and / or bonds or corporate bonds as a source of capital. Rich districts rather than seeking foreign capital.
At the same time, the participants also gained more understanding on investor protection and law enforcement in the securities sector in Cambodia. The contribution of microfinance institutions in the securities sector will help boost investment as well as the development of financial markets and the national economy as a whole.
