Life Music is an influential next-generation film about love, war and family relationships, accompanied by "Champa Battambang", a famous song written by the Golden Voice Emperor Sin Sisamouth. The story shows three different periods in which the lives of people in those three generations were changed by the arrival of the Khmer Rouge regime.
Sok Visal, co-director of the film Life Music, said that music always played an important role in the Cambodian war. He says there are many opinions that music is the soul of the Cambodian people.
The film Life Music premiered at the Asia Pacific Film Festival in May 2018 in Los Angeles, California and then went on to become an international hit. It was also screened in Phnom Penh in March 2019.
Life music films are now being submitted to the Academy for consideration on the Oscars' "International" category. However, it remains to be seen whether the film will be shortlisted for the Oscars.
It should be noted that yesterday evening, the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes decided to arrest Tycoon Kong Kreung and his son-in-law after a day of interrogation related to forest crimes at the Police Command. Kratie Provincial Armed Forces. This was confirmed by Brigadier General Eng Hee, spokesman for the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes.
Brigadier General Eng Hee confirmed to Fresh News: "Under the direct command of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Chairman of the National Commission and Coordinated by the Kratie Provincial Military Prosecutor's Office, two individuals were arrested in connection with forestry crimes, including the suspect, Oknha Kong Kreung, and Matt Nasat.
He claimed that according to the Code of Criminal Procedure, in response to the urgent needs of the investigation, judicial police officers could detain individuals suspected of involvement in crimes.
The decision to arrest Tycoon Kong Kreung came when the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes summoned Tycoon Kong Kreung to comment on forest crimes at the Kratie Provincial Gendarmerie Command. Oknha Kong Kreung, a resident of Dey Chrap Thmey village, 2 Thnou commune, Snoul district, Kratie province, is the owner of the Matt Nasat handicraft factory.
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin Receives 40 Million Riels for the Construction of a Crown at Wat Kranhong and Wat Preah Lean Preah in Tbong Khmum Province
(Tbong Khmum): The suffix of Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia and Lok Chumteav handed over 40 million Riels to Preah Chao Athikar and the committee of Wat Kranhong and Wat Preah Lean Preah to build a crown, with each pagoda receiving 20 million Riels for Build a crown.
The fund was handed over by Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, on August 16, 2019.
Addressing the grandparents on that occasion, Mr. Vong Soth said that our country is peaceful and prosperous in all areas, whether empire or Buddhism, in which the field of Buddhism is very much taken care of by the leaders. On every floor, today, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei and Lok Chumteav provided funds to contribute to the construction of crowns in the two pagodas above.
He said that the maintenance of peace and prosperity depends on the people, grandparents who have always supported the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, although some unscrupulous people try to destroy by some foreign incitement.
On this issue, Mr. Vong Soth also called on grandmothers, grandfathers and people to continue to support the Cambodian People's Party, headed by Samdech Techo, continue to lead the country to progress in all areas, especially to achieve the growth plan to become a rich country. The economy will reach a high average by 2030 and a rich country by 2050. Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum sends a message congratulating Lok Chumteav Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An on the occasion of his 66th birthday
Once again, the President of the Senate would like to pray for the merits of the three jewels, all the sacred objects in the New Year Deity, the Deity to take care of the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Men Sam An, as well as all sons, daughters and grandchildren, please meet only the four blessings of the Buddha: age, class, happiness and strength, do not be lazy.
Authorities and health officials close two illegal Chinese drug stores in Bavet
(Svay Rieng): The working group of the Secretariat for the Elimination of Counterfeit Medicines in Svay Rieng Province closed two medical treatment centers and sold illegal drugs in Bavet City on the afternoon of August 15, 2019.
The operation was led by Mr. Touch Poliva, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province and Chairman of the Provincial Commission for the Elimination of Counterfeit Medicines and Illegal Health Services, and Mr. Men Chanra, Deputy Governor of Bavet City and Deputy Chairman of the Bavet City Commission for the Elimination of Counterfeit Medicines and Illegal Health Services.
The team found that the place has 4 medicine cabinets and 4 beds for patients and 4 patients who are being treated for serum. The Secretariat team has already inspected the site three times, but is still providing medical services.
The team confiscated medicine and medical equipment in the treatment room as evidence, including: 3 cases of medicine. The confiscated drugs are all made in China and are not listed.
The second location of the illegal drug dealership in Le Macau Casino was provided by Li Pengyong, a 43-year-old Chinese man, and Li Peng Qin, a 47-year-old Chinese man, as the owner. In collaboration with Cambodian doctors.
The team found that the site has 6 medicine cabinets and 5 beds for patients, and there are many cases of medicine and serum stored in the bathroom and on the wall. The Secretariat team has inspected the site in the past and has already signed a contract to stop providing services, but is still continuing to provide medical services.
The team confiscated 23 cases of medicine and medical equipment in the treatment room as evidence. The confiscated drugs are all made in China and are not listed. FAO Country Director for Cambodia Meets Minister of Agriculture to Amend Fisheries Law
