Senior Minister Kun Kim and President of "Caritas Cambodia" Donate to Flood Victims in Ratanakkiri
(Rattanakiri): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on August 16, 2019, visited and distributed humanitarian aid to 500 families affected by the flood in Chey Udom commune. Lumphat District, Rattanakiri Province. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Kim Ratana, Director of "Caritas Cambodia" and officials from many other provinces.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim brought a message from Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all the affected people.
The Senior Minister said to the victims, "Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always pay attention and monitor the living conditions of all people, especially during the floods. . Both princes always remind me to come down and solve your problems. Please do not worry at all, Samdech always misses and cares for you, do not leave you.
Mr. Kun Kim also thanked Caritas Cambodia for joining the Royal Government in providing humanitarian donations to all flood victims in Lumphat district.
