Nearly $ 90,000 Water Supply Station in Preah Vihear Province's Chey Sen District Officially Inaugurated
(Preah Vihear): A water distribution station of Putra Sen Chey community, built at a cost of nearly 90,000 USD, was inaugurated on the afternoon of August 15, 2019 in the area of Wat Seila Nimmit, Putra village, Putra district. Chey Sen, Preah Vihear Province.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Sou Serey, Deputy Governor, Representative of Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as well as leaders, government officials and local authorities, many other partner organizations.
Mr. Mop Thirith, Director of the Department of Rural Development of Preah Vihear Province, said that the project to build a community-level water distribution station under the cooperation between World Vision Cambodia in Chey Sen District and Putra Samaki Vattanak Meanchey Community with technical support from the Provincial Department of Rural Development. .
He said that with the cooperation in good partnership between the Department of Rural Development, World Vision in Chey Sen district with the agricultural community and with the full support of district leaders, provincial leaders.
Chey Sen district has built three community-level water distribution stations at a cost of $ 257,675, which is a source of funding for World Vision Cambodia. He said that the construction of these three community-level water distribution stations has been approved by the Preah Vihear provincial governor.
Mr. Mop Thirith pointed out that the three water distribution stations include:
* First: Kampong Putra Village Water Supply Station was built with a total budget of $ 8802525 * 2: Revolution Village Water Supply Station was built with a total budget of $ 82,225 and the Water Supply Station in Kork Village, Saang Commune was built with a total budget of $ 88,225 Well.
On that occasion, Mr. Sou Serey expressed his happiness with the people of Chey Sen district, where today a new achievement was unveiled and inaugurated to serve the common good of the people here. . He also thanked the district authorities, the provincial Department of Rural Development, as well as World Vision for co-constructing this achievement to meet the needs of the people.
The Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province continued that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has taken care of the daily lives of the people. At the same time, the main issue that the head of the Royal Government pays attention to is that apart from the health and transportation sectors, the supply of electricity and clean water to remote rural areas for people to use.
He said, "As of today, the use of electricity and clean water has reached the villages and communes of a large number of our people, which he hopes that in the next mandate, the electricity and water supply and access. To every house in the countryside, of course.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor also called on the Cambodian people to support Samdech Techo Hun Sen to lead the country so that the country can have peace and development more and more.
Donald Trump said US and Chinese officials had a telephone conversation a few days before his administration decided to postpone raising tariffs on more than $ 150 billion in Chinese goods until December 15. . These include smartphones, laptops, computers and other products commonly used by consumers. However, some goods will be taxed on September 1 as planned.
However, Beijing said it was a breach of contract between Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping during the G20 summit in Japan in June, and China warned of retaliation. But also insisted that the United States agree to reach an agreement.
A new round of trade talks between Washington and Beijing is scheduled for September.
