Mondulkiri Provincial Governor: The clearing of forest land for road construction in Oreang district has been completely suspended, waiting for the professional officers to inspect and take further action
Mr. Svay Sam Eang stated that after the machine is completely suspended, he will send provincial officials and professional officers to inspect the scene for further action, regardless of the company and any person to be punished. If found guilty.
It should be noted that a few days ago, Mr. Seak Mony, the newly-appointed governor of Oreang district, was claimed by some Oreang district officials to be clearing a forest road with a width of not less than 20 meters, clearing hundreds of thousands of meters of forest and pine trees. Without the permission of the Ministry or the administration of Mondulkiri Provincial Hall.
The clearing activity is located in Purang village, Sen Monorom commune, Oreang district, Mondulkiri province. Immediately that day, Mondulkiri provincial governor Svay Sam Eang ordered the Mondulkiri Forestry Administration and the provincial military to seize the machinery operating at the site.
In particular, on the morning of August 16, 2019, Mr. Seak Mony, Governor of Oreang District, confirmed that the road was really cleared, but all the clearing did not clear the new road, but cleared the old road. Wujisan Company, a pine company owned by the company and the administration of Oreang District Hall, has also agreed with the above company, and the district has already notified the provincial and district authorities.
The district governor added that the clearing of the road did not affect the state forest land, but affected the pine forest land of Wujisan Company (land of Wujisan Pine Company) owned by Wujisan Company and the road clearing It is inevitable that some of the pine trees will be affected, and this clearing is for the public good.
According to the spokesperson of O'Raing district administration, "The clearing of a road in Putang village, Sen Monorom commune, O'Raing district, Mondulkiri province, the district hall administration is planning to open the construction site in the future for the clearing of some pine trees. In order to see the land situation for the road construction project, the district administration has also held outreach meetings with many families, ”he said.
Despite the interpretation from the governor of Oreang district, but the public and civil servants request the district governor to release sufficient documents related to the law and the approval of the relevant ministries, administrations, provincial halls, districts. Towards the legitimacy of the law. However, the district governor said that all the clearing of this road, he stopped activities on the evening of August 13, 2019.
Phnom Penh International Port CamControl Branch Inspected Food Goods at 5 Markets in Chbar Ampov District
(Phnom Penh): In addition to regular inspections of goods in the market every day to strengthen the protection of people's welfare, on August 16, 2019, Camcontrol Phnom Penh International Port in cooperation with officials of the Department of Commerce brought a test vehicle Mobile inspection of food products in 5 markets, including: Chbar Ampov Central Market, Chbar Ampov Vegetable Market, Prek Pra Market, Champouk K'aek Market and Prek Eang Market.
The team analyzed 66 samples of food products and found that none of the products contained banned chemicals.
Mr. Bun Chamroeun, President of CamControl Phnom Penh International Port Branch, said that all these activities are carried out regularly in the responsible areas of CamControl Branch throughout the capital, provinces and cities under the careful guidance of the leadership of the General. Camcontrol Department and the leadership of the Ministry of Commerce.
He said that the work of surveying and monitoring in the market is to continue to be more active and strong, to increase trust and protect the well-being of people across the country, contribute to reducing people's poverty by helping to prevent To avoid diseases caused by eating contaminated food and toxic chemicals in it.
