Chinese Ambassador: "Absolutely against the unrest in Hong Kong, expecting Hong Kong tomorrow to be better" (Video inside) Extremist violence through reliance on external forces.
The facts show that the protests in Hong Kong have now gone beyond the limits of normal protests and have turned into extremist acts that have seriously affected the social stability and security of the lives and property of Hong Kong people. From the beginning, Cambodia has strongly supported the Chinese side on any issues related to China's core interests, and we are deeply grateful for this.
In order for my Cambodian friends who are worried about Hong Kong to understand the true story of this unrest, I would like to clarify the following:
1: The achievements of "one country, two systems" can not be denied. Hong Kong is the territory of China. Since the return of Hong Kong, "one country, two systems" has clearly achieved world-renowned achievements. The "one country, two systems", "Hong Kong people, Hong Kong" autonomous principles were strictly incorporated.
Hong Kong maintains stability, prosperity and is recognized as the world's most liberal economic pole, business environment and international competitiveness, and is widely recognized by the international community. The people of Hong Kong enjoy unprecedented democratic rights and universal freedoms that are rare in the world. Hong Kong's Rule of Law Index ranks first in the world.
The results clearly show that "one country, two systems" is the best system for maintaining long-term stability and prosperity after Hong Kong's return. China's central government will continue to adhere to the "one country, two systems" policy, keeping this goal unchanged or unshakable.
3: Support the Hong Kong authorities to strictly enforce the law. The government and some Western media outlets, such as the United States, have refrained from citing unlawful acts of violence by illegal activists, but instead indiscriminately accused Hong Kong authorities of protecting and tolerating law enforcement. Instead.
The bad "performance" in the chaotic situation of Hong Kong by some Western politicians, including the United States, clearly shows what is interfering in the internal affairs of other countries. The bad character of the United States playing a role in the unrest in Hong Kong reminds me of the color revolution that took place in Eastern Europe, Central Asia, and some countries in Africa.
The United States considers itself a beacon of world freedom, claiming that it will solve world problems. In fact, under the pretext of defending "democracy" and "freedom" in disguise and causing unrest in internal affairs and shifting political power in other countries is a tactic that the United States has always pursued.
In relation to Cambodia, outside forces have recently fabricated rumors regarding the internal affairs of Cambodia, a sovereign country. At the same time, they constantly fabricated information, alleging that China and Cambodia had signed a "secret agreement". It is said that China wants to build a naval base and a military airport in the territory of Koh Kong province, Cambodia.
