Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, confirmed to Fresh News on August 15, 2019 that the report was submitted on August 12, 2019.
"The report clarifies all the details and shows the progress of the process of strengthening democracy, respect for human rights, space, freedom and labor rights," he said. "What the government expects is for the European Commission to make a transparent decision based on the rule of law and justice for Cambodia."
