(Tbong Khmum): Speaking at the seminar on multi-sectoral response to HIV and AIDS by Tbong Khmum Provincial Committee for Combating HIV / AIDS in the second half of 2019 on the afternoon of August 14, 2019 Senior Minister Ieng Moly, President of the National Authority for Combat "We can not remain silent and ignore this issue because it can spread again if we do not work together to prevent it," he said.
He also called on the authorities, partner organizations, entertainment institutions and all citizens to work together to prevent the spread of HIV / AIDS to be successful.
Participants in the workshop included leaders of the National AIDS Authority, Mr. Cheng Bunnara, Deputy Provincial Governor, Representative of the Provincial AIDS Committee, Mr. Keo Vannak, Director of the Provincial Health Department, Representative of the Provincial AIDS Secretariat, Representatives of relevant provincial departments. More than 50 civil society organizations (AHF MHC & KWWA), local authorities and the armed forces.
This workshop was held to review the progress and learn about the multi-sectoral HIV / AIDS situation at the sub-national level through the inclusion of HIV / AIDS work in the policy of safe villages and communes towards achieving the 95-95 goal. -95 in 2025.
The Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection can assist in disseminating the law on non-discrimination against people living with HIV / AIDS. Non-discrimination against people living with HIV must be done together. We need to educate people to protect themselves. If you suspect you may be infected, get a blood test and use a condom to protect yourself. People with HIV, unlike other diseases, are ashamed, do not fear death, and do not seek medical attention.
The Senior Minister said that today, the work of AIDS as a whole, we are successful, we have achieved the goal of 90-90-90 in 2017. We estimate that there are more than 70,000 people living with HIV. Of those, more than 60,000 people came for treatment, and it is estimated that more than 10,000 are missing. The senior minister also stressed that we can not remain silent about HIV / AIDS because it can recover. We are concerned that infections are on the rise among homosexuals.
