With pity! Mr. Khieu Kanharith and Mr. Thy Khemrin donated 2 million Riels to the police officers affected by the fire in Siem Reap
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Information, Mr. Khieu Kanharith and Mr. Thy Khemrin, donated 2 million Riels to the police officers who caught fire during the firefighting operation in Siem Reap on August 14, 2019 yesterday.
Huot Mony Pisak, a police officer in the intervention unit, was engulfed in flames while he was intervening to evacuate people from the scene.
After the incident, Mr. Huot Mony Pisak was sent by his family to a hospital in Ubon Ratchathani, Thailand. Mr. Huot Mony Pisak is currently being treated at a hospital in Ubon Ratchathani. According to the family, after careful treatment, the condition of this police officer has improved a bit.
When Facebook users saw the situation of the police officer Huot Monipisak, they expressed their sympathy and some expressed their admiration for the sense of responsibility of the police officer. Some consider this to be one of the heroism of this police officer in the operation to save lives from the flames.
Out of sympathy and admiration for the heroism of this police officer, many philanthropists have donated money to alleviate suffering and medical treatment, as well as to encourage the sacrifices in the work of this police officer.
The company's statement came after the Phnom Penh Municipal Court announced the auction of real estate of Ms. Keo Maly and Ms. Keo Suy Chheng for more than $ 7.2 million.
