Mr. Lim Keanhor stated: "The whole world is raising and seeking to address two issues besides other issues: First, the issue of climate change. "As a global issue, not just in Cambodia, the second issue: which the world as well as the region has been interested in is water security."
On the issue of water security, Mr. Lim Kean Hor said that it is necessary to have clean water for people to use, and in our whole world, only 2.5 percent of the water is clean. Is all salt water. He said that Cambodia is very lucky to have a lot of fresh water, which is different from other countries that have rich seawater, which has become the head of the world to discuss the issue of water security. .
In particular, he said that now the floods in neighboring countries have become a challenge for the government to solve immediately because it destroys the lives of people, livestock, houses, infrastructure and people. Tens of thousands were evacuated to safety. In particular, Cambodia is still small.
It should be informed that during the rainy season of 2019, eight provinces of Cambodia were affected by floods, including: Sihanoukville, Kampot, Koh Kong, Kep, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Battambang and Kampong Thom. To 9,520 people.
According to the report, the floods in the eight provinces affected 6,900 houses, affected 5,447 livestock, affected 5,208 hectares, damaged 300 hectares and affected 2,275 hectares of crops, damaged 940 hectares.
Please note that these days, floods have hit some provinces in Cambodia after a series of rains across the country. Floods in Sihanoukville have left three people dead, including two Cambodians and a Chinese national, while property and household items were damaged.
