Minister of Tourism: Rain these days did not cause harm to tourists, but damaged access to some communities
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, claimed that the repeated rains in recent days have not caused any harm to any tourists, just disrupted some tourist trips, but also caused damage to the road. Hold some tourism community, which requires stakeholders to find a solution as soon as possible.
The minister confirmed that in general, during the rainy season, tourists do not go out to visit much. He heard reports from the Department of Tourism in the provinces that there are no problems or harm to any tourists.
He added that the issue of security for tourists during the rainy season, he has already recommended to the Department of Tourism, capital - provinces, but still face another problem is the damage to the road to some tourist communities damaged by Floods in the past and in recent days.
Mr. Thong Khon also mentioned the statistics of tourists that for international tourists, especially Europeans, there is some decline because this season is the rainy season, visitors do not go abroad, and in Europe is also the dry season that they Like to travel in their country.
As for national tourists, they are not worried about the decline, although this season is the rainy season, but in Cambodia, there is also a national traditional festival, Dak Ben, Pchum Ben, which is a strong driver of tourists. .
"People will visit their hometowns during the upcoming Pchum festival, after they get home, they will go to the pagoda and can visit the resorts," he said.
The Minister of Tourism has directed all capital-provincial tourism departments to prepare for security, improve sanitation, service quality, parking lots and improve roads in tourist areas, tourist communities, pagodas and tourist destinations. Visit many attractions and other tourist attractions to receive guests with warmth and hospitality.
On the afternoon of August 14, 2019, a gas explosion occurred at a gas station in Wat Bo village, Sala Kamroeuk commune, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, causing a fire and injuring up to 13 people. Including foreigners.
In a press release issued on August 15, 2019, the Ministry of Mines and Energy claimed that the station did not have a valid permit from the Ministry and local authorities for the construction and operation of the gas station. The ministry is currently conducting further investigations into the case.
The Ministry of Mines has also advised the public that the business of operating a gas station. In particular, liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) must have professional, technical, safety and clear and requires permission from the relevant ministries and institutions to avoid causing such risks to themselves and others.
Please be informed that at around 1 pm on August 14, 2019, there was a fire caused by the explosion of a gas tank at a gas station along Mr. Tanuy Street in Wat Bo Village, Sala Kamroeuk Commune, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province. The fire injured 13 people.
Mr. Huot Mony Pisak, a police officer in the intervention unit who participated in the firefighting and rescue operation in this case, was engulfed in flames while he was intervening to avoid people from the scene.
