KOICA and a well-known Korean medical university help train Ang Duong Hospital nurses on infection prevention
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) and Sunjunyang Medical University on August 14, 2019 held a joint Cambodian-Korean workshop on "Prevention of Infectious Diseases for Nurses" with Preah Hospital. Ang Duong.
The team of Sunjunyang Medical University decided to take this topic for training, especially for the nurses who manage infection and safety management in the hospital, and it is a necessary program not only for the patients but also for the safety of the patients. Hospital staff as well.
During the workshop, two Korean nurses, who specialize in infection control, gave a presentation on infection prevention and control. In the operating room. Twenty-six nurses from Ang Duong Hospital participated in the workshop. They share information from the basics to practical methods of managing infections.
All participants expressed their gratitude to KOICA and Sunjunyang Medical University for their support, and they expressed their high participation and commitment in the course to enhance capacity building. For a comprehensive understanding of infection prevention and control in the operating room as well.
The Korean government, through the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA-KOICA), has provided a grant of $ 8 million for the "Capacity Building Project for the ENT Center at His Hospital." Duong ”to be implemented from 2018 to 2022.
A five-story building will be built in Preah Ang Duong Hospital and will be equipped with the most modern and necessary equipment for examination, treatment and surgery to improve the quality of services in the hospital to another level.
In addition to improving the physical infrastructure, the capacity of all specialized doctors and staff is enhanced through training programs and the transfer of knowledge and know-how from Korean doctors.
