In the first 6 months of this year, there were 181 foreign victims and 450 foreigners in Cambodia
This was stated by General Thong Lim, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Chairman of the Hotline with Foreigners in the Kingdom of Cambodia, to the representatives of the embassies in the Kingdom of Cambodia in a meeting on the morning of August 15. 2019 at the meeting hall of the Ministry of Interior.
General Thong Lim added that from April 20, 2019 to June 19, 2019, compared to the second quarter of 2018, there were 178 cases, a decrease of 9.5% in nationality. The worst affected are China, Vietnam, France, Britain, the United States, and the most affected areas are Siem Reap, Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville.
He added that in addition to the foreign victims, there were 84 foreigners who committed crimes, in which the police arrested a total of 450 people (17 nationalities) for 11 crimes (compared to the second quarter). In 2018, there were 88 cases, a decrease of 4.54%). The most crime-prone nationalities are China, Vietnam, India, South Korea, Ukraine, and the most common geographical areas are Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Svay Rieng.
It should be noted that the HOTLINE team with foreigners in the Kingdom of Cambodia has good relations and cooperation with embassies and missions, as well as protecting delegations and foreign diplomats during visits and visits. Perform high security missions, especially to intervene, solve problems and rescue foreign investors and foreign tourists in a timely manner.
