235 students successfully graduate from Khemarak University
(Phnom Penh): After many years of hard work, 235 students successfully graduated and graduated from Khemarak University on the morning of August 14, 2019.
The program was presided over by Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia. Among the 235 students were 122 women and three monks. Successful graduates include PhD, Master, and Bachelor.
At the same time, Khemarak University always invites famous national and international speakers to give presentations to share their experiences with students of all generations while studying and provides students with the opportunity to do internships to connect theory to practice. Obviously, a significant asset in writing a dissertation and a dissertation.
Khemarak University In addition to congratulating the successful graduates in the 2019-2020 academic year, Khemarak University has decided to automatically provide 50% scholarships for 2 years to all students who come. The first 117 students enrolled for a two-year bachelor's degree.
As for scholarships for students who take the high school diploma exam in the 2018-2019 academic year, students from A and B, Khemarak University will provide 100% scholarships for two undergraduate studies. Students who receive C and D degrees from Khemarak University will be offered 70% scholarships for 2 years of undergraduate study and students who receive E degrees from Khemarak University will be offered 50% scholarships for 2 years for undergraduate studies. Bachelor.
Samdech Say Chhum: Japanese Grants Really Benefit to Develop the Economy and Improve the Livelihood of the Cambodian People
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of Cambodia, stated that the grant aid of the Royal Government and the people of Japan is a very useful aid to help develop the socio-economic and improve the livelihood. Living of the Cambodian people.
Mr. Hidehisa HORINOUCHI also expressed his great pleasure to see that the Cambodian economy is growing and developing rapidly, including strong growth in investment, trade and tourism under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. . He stated that despite his new role as Japanese Ambassador to the Netherlands, he continued to support both the spirit and good relations with Cambodia.
On behalf of the Senate of Cambodia, Samdech Vibol Sena Phekdey Say Chhum also expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the success of the Japanese Ambassador's mission in Cambodia, which has contributed to the strengthening of cooperation between the two countries and peoples. There are huge mutual benefits.
The President of the Senate also noted that the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia has performed his duties well and has good cooperation and communication with the leadership of officials at all levels and with ministries, institutions, provincial authorities, especially with And the Cambodian people. During his tenure, the Cambodian ambassador received many achievements, such as grants, loans, concessions and technical assistance provided by the Government of Japan.
The President of the Senate also thanked the Government and people of Japan for their generous loans and concessions. Japanese aid has enormous benefits to socio-economic development and to improve the lives of Cambodians. At the same time, Samdech also thanked for the support for the election process in the Kingdom of Cambodia and the assistance for the Khmer Rouge Tribunal.
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, visited and distributed gifts from the Provincial Hall to 26 children in Sihanoukville, including 26 girls in Village 01, Sangkat 03, Sihanoukville. At noon on August 14, 2019.
During the meeting with Borey Komar Sihanoukville, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun instructed all children to take good care of their health, live clean, drink boiled water and sleep under a mosquito net, especially to study well. Beware of less biting insects during the flood season.
Please be informed that the gifts distributed to Borey Komar Sihanoukville each person receive 50,000 Riels and donations for Borey Komar Sihanoukville include: 50 kg of sugar, 50 packs of salt, 50 packs of beech, 50 scarves, towels 30 beef belly, 2 big pong fish and 50 pure water. More than 200 Families Affected by Floods in Mondulkiri Province's Koh Nhek District Receive Donations from the Cambodian Red Cross
(Mondulkiri): Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Chairman of Mondulkiri Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, together with members of the District Sub-Branch Committee, visited and brought humanitarian aid to flood victims in Nong Buor village, Nong Khileuk commune, Koh Nhek district, Mondulkiri province, on the morning of August 14, 2019.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang said that Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always cares for the people who are vulnerable and affected by various disasters, regardless of political affiliation.
The provincial governor instructed all citizens to pay attention to health problems by keeping clean, drinking boiled water and sleeping in front of them to avoid dengue fever, malaria, diarrhea and other diseases, especially Beware of venomous animals If there are snake bites, please rush to the hospital for timely treatment.
In addition, care must be taken to ensure the safety of young children not to play in the water to avoid drowning, and when the water recedes, people must prepare crops and cooperate with professional institutions to restore agriculture.
At the same time, he advised all professional officials and local authorities to work together to repair infrastructure issues to facilitate travel.
He added that humanitarian donations are being distributed to people affected by the floods now to alleviate short-term shortages. On that occasion, Mr. Svay Sam Eang distributed CRC donations to 249 flood victims, each family received food and some money.
Vital has signed an agreement to support 10 tons of rice per year for 3 years to Angkor Hospital for Children
(Siem Reap): Vital Company has continued to support Angkor Hospital for Children in Siem Reap Province by signing an agreement to support 10 tons of rice per year for 3 years from 2019 to 2021.
The signing ceremony took place on the morning of August 14, 2019 at Angkor Hospital for Children in Siem Reap, Siem Reap Province, with the participation of representatives of Vital and many representatives of Angkor Hospital for Children.
Mr. Tep Navy, Operations Director of Angkor Hospital for Children, praised Vital, a national model company that focuses on humanitarian programs, especially the provision of development assistance to Cambodia.
The signing is aimed at promoting and encouraging hospitals and teams to be more motivated to provide better medical services to Cambodian children.
(Takeo): The General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance this morning, August 14, 2019, organized a workshop to disseminate new laws, regulations and guidelines for small and medium enterprises in the priority areas and procedures of Refund and use of VAT credit online at Takeo Provincial Hall.
Mr. CHHOU Sothea considered the dissemination of new regulations to small and medium enterprises as very important and recommended the cooperation between relevant units and relevant departments around the province with the provincial tax branch to support the collection. Potential tax revenue in line with tax reform policies and programs, benefits more funds for further local development.
Dr. said that the General Department of Taxation always pays great attention to disseminating and mainstreaming tax regulations, especially the recently updated regulations to taxpayers through the seminar on Facebook, Fresh News TV. In particular, the website of the General Department of Taxation aims to strengthen the culture of tax payment and tax compliance.
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, called on people throughout the province to eat pork normally to encourage farmers to continue to raise pigs.
This call was made during the Safe Pork Eating Ceremony on the morning of August 14, 2019 at the roundabout in Kampot, with the participation of Mr. Chheng Phalla, Chairman of the Provincial Council and officials of the three armed forces. Judicial institutions, teachers, students, students, about 400 business people.
Chiao Tai said that African swine fever is a highly contagious disease that is transmitted from pigs to pigs and between domestic and wild pigs, and the disease does not infect or adversely affect human health. . Therefore, leaders, government officials and all citizens, please do not be confused and please eat pork as usual.
The provincial governor added that during the outbreak of African swine fever in Cambodia, there were some opinions that eating pork could affect human health, but now on behalf of the provincial administration together with The Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries would like to confirm that eating pork that has passed the proper inspection by veterinary authorities and under normal cooking is still safe for human health.
Mr. Chan Rith, Director of Kampot Provincial Department of Agriculture, stated that according to the statistics, there are 89,601 pigs in Kampot province, while there are 20 pig farms with a total of 21,155 pigs.
In the first half of 2019, the management and officials of the Office of Production and Veterinary conducted biosafety (spraying disinfectants) in 67 pig farms in the villages and people's cages 17 times, 99 slaughterhouses and On the national road 7 times.
