The Cambodia Securities Exchange has doubled its trading hours from August 19, another step towards becoming an international market.
With this new trading hour, CSX expects to get a lot of positive results by launching longer trading hours, which will make trading easier and easier for all market participants. According to the market situation, faster.
CSX expects the new trading hours to be another step towards becoming an international market. The new trading hours, which increase to 7 hours per day, will make it easier for foreign investors living in countries with different time zones to trade securities on the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
Two women riding a motorbike on the road were crushed by a French tamarind tree, causing serious and minor injuries in Svay Rieng commune
(Svay Rieng): Two women, brothers and sisters, were seriously and lightly injured after riding a motorbike to work for compensation. On the morning of August 14, 2019, in front of the gate of Wat Sandepheap, called Wat Khloah Heur, in Svay Rieng village, Svay Rieng commune, Svay Rieng city.
According to Svay Rieng City Police, the victim, 55-year-old Koy Rom, suffered a broken right thigh and several other injuries, and the passenger did not know his name, only that he was his sister. Both of them live in Thmor Sor village, Svay Chrum commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province.
Later, the people reported to the intervention authorities to transport the two women to the Svay Rieng Provincial Referral Hospital.
Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign August 14: 942 Illegal Vehicles Found and 497 Fines
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for August 14, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 6,207 vehicles, found 942 vehicles violated the law (51% motorcycles), educated 445 vehicles and fined 497 units, according to the official report of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 3,117 helmets and goggles were inspected on August 14, 474 education helmets and 180 glasses were fined.
(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police has launched a campaign to promote helmet wearing nationwide for a full month, and for the 14th of August 2019, the traffic police force in 24 capitals and provinces inspected a number of motorcyclists. 11,536, of which 5,473 or 47% were forced to wear helmets. This is according to the report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department, which was obtained by Fresh News.
This measure is implemented nationwide, with the requirement to find a helmet to be worn before being allowed to travel without penalty for one month from July 19, 2019 onwards. Ministry of Health inspects food hygiene and safety at restaurants in Kratie province
(Kratie): Mr. Oeun Borarath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, on the morning of August 14, 2019, with the participation of Mr. Pen Lina, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, led a technical team to inspect the quality, hygiene, food safety and implementation of good principles in restaurants. In Kratie province.
Mr. Oeun Borarath said that through the Inter-Ministerial Proclamation No. 868, the Ministry of Health has an important role to play in inspecting the quality, hygiene, food safety, issuance of hygiene certificates and certificates of good practice in restaurants.
The Ministry has a team that regularly inspects the quality, hygiene, food safety in restaurants in Phnom Penh, as well as in capitals / provinces throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia.
According to past inspections, the Ministry of Health has issued two types of certificates: First, the certificate of good hygiene for restaurants or family restaurants, which is inspected by the team and specific technical equipment of the Ministry and evaluated to Out of 32 points, before issuing certificates to 32 standard restaurants, so far, the Ministry has obtained a total of 2,452 certificates.
He added that today he led a technical team to inspect the quality, hygiene, food safety and good practice of some restaurants in Kratie province, noting that most of those restaurants have not yet received hygiene certificates. Not yet. In fact, there are many restaurants in the province that practice good hygiene, as in the case of JASMINE BOAT, it is possible to obtain a Type B certificate.
