This afternoon, Prince Sar Kheng presides over the 3rd National Interfaith Forum "To Combat Human Trafficking and Modern Slavery"
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC), presided over the National Forum on August 14, 2019. The Third Interfaith "To Fight Human Trafficking and Modern Slavery." The event was held at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center.
The National Interfaith Forum is organized by the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, the Ministry of Cults and Religions, and Caritas Cambodia, with the support of religious leaders, including Buddhism, Islam, Catholicism, and the Gospel, and non-governmental organizations. Working to combat human trafficking in Cambodia.
Speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Him Chhem, Minister of Cults and Religions, said that in order to continue to contribute to the fight against human trafficking, the third national interfaith forum was organized for three main purposes, including:
* First, to raise awareness of human trafficking and the important role of religious leaders in educating the people to prevent and combat human trafficking and the abolition of modern slavery.
* Second: To expand and strengthen good cooperation between relevant institutions, especially religious institutions in education, dissemination of human trafficking and modern slavery in pagodas, temples and religious ceremonies.
* Third: For the sound of this prayer to give hope to the victims of human trafficking and wish them a speedy return to freedom.
He stressed that the Interfaith Forum to Combat Human Trafficking is not only a national model forum, but also a regional and global forum. This forum is a testament to the harmony of all religions in Cambodia.
Not only that, this forum confirms the commitment and joint implementation of all major religions on a single vision: the fight against human trafficking, the promotion of human dignity, the building of peace and the well-being of people in society. The whole of Cambodia.
According to Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice Chair of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, the Royal Government has actively worked to overcome all obstacles in preventing, suppressing, prosecuting and protecting the victims.
In particular, in the first six months of 2015, education, dissemination and prevention activities were taken care of and carried out in all forms, including legal protection, direct and indirect education through various media to reach many people. Millions of people, in fact, the current National Interfaith Forum is also a way to contribute to the prevention of human trafficking and modern-day slavery.
According to Ms. Chou Bun Eng, ministries, institutions and units at both the national and sub-national levels have taken preventive measures in their respective fields to manage the situation from falling victim to human trafficking.
As for the crackdown, the judicial police investigated, investigated and cracked down on a total of 78 cases, compared to the same period in 2018, there were 62 cases (an increase of 16 cases equal to 25%), arrested the suspects and sent them to court. 97/85 people (an increase of 12 people equal to 14%), including 22 women, 9 minors, 18 foreigners (12 Chinese and 2 Americans).
