(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance, in collaboration with the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Planning, the Ministry of Public Works and the Ministry of Justice, organized a one-day forum on "Legislative Functions and Reform of the Royal Government" on 13 August. 2019, held at Sokha Phnom Penh Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The forum was presided over by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Legislative Council of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Nation for democratic development at the sub-national level.
The forum was also attended by senior leaders and civil servants from all ministries and institutions, including the legislature, the executive branch, the central and local administrations, the judiciary, as well as higher education institutions and academies. A total of about 650 people. This forum is organized for two purposes as follows:
1: Share, exchange, understand each other, experience, knowledge and challenges in the implementation of the legislative functions of the legislative units in the ministries-institutions in support of the reform work of the Royal Government.
2. Cooperate, consider and discuss the establishment of common values for the legislative function in contributing to increase the efficiency of management, implementation and evaluation of the implementation of reform work in accordance with the policies and strategies of the Royal Government.
At the opening of the forum, the Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, emphasized that this forum is a rare opportunity for the Ministry of Institutional Reform and the Legislative Leadership Unit of the Royal Government to come together to Discuss relations and mutual support in order to accelerate the pace of reform for good governance.
The Deputy Prime Minister also gave two key recommendations to the forum for consideration and discussion:
First, review and discuss the framework of the relationship between the legislative function and the reform function in each ministry-institution, especially on the institutional mechanism to be responsible for leading or coordinating and
Second, review and discuss the importance or necessity of establishing a system of leadership and management, the implementation and monitoring of the effectiveness of the implementation of laws and regulations of the Ministry-institution at the inter-sectoral, inter-institutional or government level to support the reform work. Of the Royal Government at each reform site or as an inter-reform site as well as the policies and strategies of the Royal Government.
Next, under the guidance and coordination of Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Mr. Youk Bunna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Function and Chairman of the Public Administration Reform Committee.
The forum was held through the keynote presentation of the Ministry of Reform and Strategic Planning of the Royal Government and actively discussed the experiences, challenges and roles of the legislative function to accelerate the reform work by dividing the group discussions. .
Discussions focused on legislative functions for reform, feasibility, challenges, successful experiences, and the future of legislative functions for reform.
At the closing ceremony, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development, warmly congratulated the forum on its expected outcome. This.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also highlighted the key points of importance and interconnection of the implementation of the legislative function and the reform work, and recommended that each ministry-institution review and consider strengthening the implementation of the legislative work with the work. Reform for the effectiveness of good governance.
