Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Inaugurates Chrang Chot Bridge and 4 More Bridges in Battambang Province
(Battambang): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, this morning, August 14, 2019, presided over the inauguration ceremony of Chrang Chot Bridge in Rong Village, Cheng Meanchey Commune, Banan District and Bridge 4. Others in Samlot, Bavil, Ek Phnom and Kamrieng districts, Battambang province, financed by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
In response to this new achievement for the people of Battambang province, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng encouraged all people to use this newly inaugurated bridge for the special benefit of extracting the products from the construction of this bridge in order to improve their daily life. More days.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that Cambodia is now completely peaceful without any illegal army to come to war with the Royal Government, which is the luck of all Cambodians under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government. Cambodia. Samdech stressed that if the district is not peaceful, people will not have time to do daily business.
This was confirmed by the Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Cambodia, Mr. On Nak-yong, while sending 32 Cambodian industrial workers (two women) to work in the Republic of Korea.
The departure of the above Cambodian workers took place on the afternoon of August 13, 2019 at Phnom Penh International Airport. The departure was also attended by Mr. Heng Sour, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
During the meeting with Cambodian workers, Mr. On Nak-yong instructed that while working in the Republic of Korea, if there is any problem, please contact all the workers who are already stationed there to solve any problems that occur in When working in Korea.
Mr. Heng Sour also advised the 32 workers to work hard and be patient if they want to change jobs, consult with the Foreign Workers Support Center near the workplace, because if you change jobs voluntarily, it can lead to action. Breaking the agreement can also lead to problems.
He expressed the hope that all Cambodian workers would maintain dignity for the entire Cambodian nation and take care of health, hygiene, safety in living and traveling.
In an interview with the press, Heng Sour said that to date, Cambodia has sent more than 60,000 of its workers to the Republic of Korea, mostly in industry, followed by agriculture and construction.
He added that the Republic of Korea has a good system for managing foreign workers because there are no less than 40 centers for the protection of foreign workers, and in those centers there are always people who know the language of the workers of each country, for example. Cambodia has Khmer-speaking staff stationed at these centers as well. When workers have any problems, they can contact them by phone and they will get help to solve them.
In addition to the Labor Support Center, Cambodia also has two labor advisors in charge of the Cambodian Embassy in the Republic of Korea, as well as officials of the Committee for Training and Sending Workers Abroad of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. Help solve labor problems in the Republic of Korea as well.
The Korean Ambassador stated that according to the majority opinion from Korean employers on Cambodian workers, they are very satisfied with the ability and patience of Cambodian workers.
According to the ambassador, the Embassy of the Republic of Korea in Cambodia will work to urge his Korean government to increase the quota for more Cambodian workers to work in the Republic of Korea. To date, there are 16 foreign workers working in the Republic of Korea, of which the number of Cambodian workers has increased significantly among other foreign workers.
Before leaving Cambodia, On Keo Moniroth and Vick Chhengly said they expected to earn a higher salary when they worked in Korea, which could be sent back to their families to make a living. Their families are getting better.
