(Svay Rieng): At the Svay Rieng Provincial HIV / AIDS Committee's Multidisciplinary HIV / AIDS Response Workshop in the Second Half of 2019, Senior Minister Ieng Moly, Director of the National AIDS Authority, stated that people living with HIV / AIDS In Svay Rieng province, it has decreased.
Speaking on the afternoon of August 13, 2019, Senior Minister Ieng Moly continued that although the rate of HIV infection in Svay Rieng has decreased, but not to be underestimated, so all relevant officials must continue to fight. And HIV / AIDS to be stronger to participate in achieving the national goal 95-95-95 in 2020 and to eliminate new infections in 2025-2030.
Mr. Ieng Moly also commended the Provincial AIDS Committee and all relevant units in the province for their active participation in the fight against HIV / AIDS, which has reduced the rate of HIV infection. .
According to Mr. Toch Poliva, Deputy Governor and Chairman of the Provincial AIDS Committee, the HIV / AIDS epidemic in Svay Rieng province is estimated to reach 1,791 people living with HIV in 2019. Fourteen new infections and 77 deaths.
In response to the prevention and treatment of HIV patients in the first half of 2019, there were 12822 HIV testing services, 33 positive test cases and referrals to antiretroviral drugs. Thirty percent, 90 percent, and 1395 active HIV patients were receiving services, of which 1,393 were receiving antiretroviral drugs, 99 percent had low HIV infection, 15 had died and five had died.
