Authorities and Water Resources Officers Demarcate the Main Water Reserve for Citizens to Use and Prevent Invasion in Batheay District, Kampong Cham Province
(Kampong Cham): Batheay District Authority, in cooperation with the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Cham Province, on August 13, 2019, together with relevant professional officers, surveyed the border and erected a border post on the main dam in Popit village, Tang Kraing commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province. In order to allow people to farm, in the past, this area was always traded.
Mr. Phen Sophal, Governor of Batheay District, said that the demarcation of the border post of the Mekong River at the above location to prevent the sale or purchase of public property such as the Mekong River. He said that in the past, there have been corrupt traders who have violated the law by buying and selling public property, where no one has the right to buy or sell.
The governor of Batheay district requested the people who are enjoying the main dam as well as the farmers to cooperate to maintain, protect and prevent as a source of water for dry rice and wet rice, do not encroach on state land Private property, do not believe the incitement of others to use natural resources for personal business is to work together to maintain common property for the benefit of all citizens.
But after an agreement was reached, the authorities demarcated the area, and there were protests from some residents not allowing officials to do so. According to some villagers, the protesters were traders who used to encroach on land in the river behind them. CamControl Officers Find Defective Goods and Contain Nearly 10kg of Chemicals at Svay Rieng Veal Yon Market
(Svay Rieng): In order to ensure food safety for the people, Mr. Pheng Nil, Chief of CamControl Svay Rieng Branch, this morning, August 14, 2019, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce, led the working group to continue to inspect various goods in In Veal Yont Market, Svay Rieng City, 8 kilograms of defective goods and half a kilogram of dried goods were found to contain chemicals.
Mr. Pheng Nil stated that after inspecting nearly 20 items in the field market, they found defective goods, including 3 kg of sausage, 2.5 kg of dried eel, 2.5 kg of dried fish and dried fish. The seller also agreed to stop selling defective products because they were all aware of the impact on people's health.
Mr. Pheng Nil called on all people to be careful when eating food, to check the date label clearly before buying to eat. In particular, the food that children like to eat must be checked properly before eating to participate in promoting the well-being of all, and CamControl officials will continue to inspect the goods in the markets in Svay Rieng province.
