Dressed as a security guard, Mr. Yem Sao, Head of Security of the Thmar Kral Nature Resort Community, described that tourists at this resort do not have to worry about personal safety because the community is protected 24 hours a day.
Meanwhile, a vendor in the resort area, Kim Neang, said that food and goods were sold at a reasonable price, not too expensive to take advantage of passengers. She said that selling less than other resorts is a principle to attract more tourists.
Take a look back at the entrance to the tourist area for the rainy season, which is the season for rice farmers, the streets are full of lush green rice plants, blinding the eyes of travelers under the dim sky. Accompanied by the flow of individual houses is a great scene to serve the feeling of getting rid of fatigue from work or study.
Hel Oeun, president of the Thmar Kral Natural Resort Community, said the infamous tourist area has cool water for all seasons. "Considering the speed of the water, it has not receded since the drought since the rains," he said.
Another interesting thing is that the bamboo shoots that grow there are curved and spherical, arranged in a purely natural way. At night, there is a kind of mushroom that emits a flash of light accompanied by the sound of running water and the sound of wild animals crying in an unimaginable way.
