OWSOs and Citizens' Offices in 4 Border Areas in Battambang Province Officially Inaugurated
(Battambang): OWSOs and People's Offices in four border districts, including Kamrieng District Administration, Sampov Loun District Administration, Rattanak Mondul District Administration and Banan District Administration, Battambang Province, were officially inaugurated together. This morning, August 12, 2019, chaired by Mr. Uy Ry, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang.
After Mr. Sok Kim Khon, Governor of Kamrieng District, read the welcome report and reminded about the history of the establishment of the People's Office, the first pilot was set up at the OWSO in Battambang and Siem Reap, which followed the decision No. 47 pillars dated March 11, 2003 of the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak instructed and instructed the administration of the four target districts: Kamrieng, Sampov Loun, Rattanak Mondul and Banan districts to continue to pay attention to the implementation of five important tasks, such as:
* First, to effectively implement the mechanism of the OWSO and the Citizens' Office in accordance with the letter of regulation and to widely disseminate the service price list.
* Second, the provision of administrative services must ensure transparency, accountability, efficiency, responsiveness, equity and citizen participation.
* Third: Post price list to the public in various public places to make it easier for people to see.
* Fourth: Regularly inspect to ensure the strengthening of all administrative services in accordance with the principles and procedures set.
* Fifth: Administrative discipline must be imposed on civil servants and employees who cause resentment by neglecting to provide administrative services.
