According to the letter sent by the Ministry of Interior to the Capital-Provincial Governor on August 12, 2019, the Ministry of Interior has found that some of the chairmen and members of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Councils of the third mandate have been appointed. Advisors or assistants before the election, and some are appointed as advisors or assistants after the election.
In this case, the only person left in the position is the Chairman or a member of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council. At the same time, for the preparation and opening of the monthly allowance, each person receives a monthly allowance in the position of Chairman or Member of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council.
Separately, for the chairmen and members of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Councils of the third mandate who were appointed as advisors or assistants after the election, the Ministry of Interior has confirmed that the positions of the chairmen and members of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Councils Not lost because the president and councilors of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts, Khans are public officials whose mandate is elected.
The Ministry claims that in this case, the person concerned must decide to choose any position as an advisor or assistant or chairman or member of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District, Khan of the third mandate. For the preparation and opening of the monthly allowance, each person receives a salary or a monthly allowance in the selected position.
