The 6th National Film Festival will be held for 5 days from August 25-29, this year expects a lot of contestants!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts will organize the 6th National Film Festival Competition for 5 days from 25-29 August 2019 to take the films of Cambodian filmmakers to compete and enhance the ability to Produced a film, and this year expects a lot of competition for the film.
The Film Festival is an event of the collection of Cambodian films that have received public support in the past to compete for prizes and awards. This is the sixth time that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has organized this event.
In fact, on August 12, 2019, the National Film Festival held a press conference on "Organizing the 6th National Film Festival under the joint theme to promote Khmer cinema" with the participation of Mr. Sin Chansaya, Advisor of the Ministry of Culture And Fine Arts, Pok Borak, director of the Department of Film and the Arts and many other producers.
Mr. Pok Bo Reaksa said that for the 6th National Film Festival competition, all films must focus on the following topics: 1: Educate and disseminate knowledge about culture, traditions and national traditions. 2. Promote culture, peace, strengthen national unity 3. Create creativity or reflect social reality.
He continued, "For all films that compete with the conditions, such as: Khmer films produced by local production and received a screening visa from the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, Khmer films produced during 2016 to 2019. And have never competed in the National Festival before.
He stressed that the film festival is not only a competition of works, but also a good opportunity for producers and film technicians from all productions to draw on each other's experiences to improve and enhance quality. Its film works to meet the needs of the local film market and compete in the regional market.
Mr. Sin Chansaya said that the film festival has a common goal to promote the film industry in Cambodia, both producers and the public sector as well as the private sector and would like to attract all circles to participate in this event to promote our film industry better. Up.
He added that all the films that participated in the competition and were judged based on 8 main works, including: 1: Screenwriting, 2: Directing, 3: Filming, 4: Works Performing, 5: Stage decoration work, 6: Light technical work, 7: Image installation work and 8: Sound assembly work.
He added that the above eight works were selected in two additional stages, including: Selection of eight outstanding films for the finals of the festival, the films selected in the first phase will be evaluated. Winner of the 6th National Film Festival 2019.
(Phnom Penh): Day by day, people are more interested in doing business (creating their own business) and increase their ability to do business by learning business skills in various forms.
Obviously, no matter what skills we learn, we can do business as long as we have a clear plan for doing business. You will need a lot of knowledge to start a business, but it will not be easy to succeed if you try to master many skills at the same time without a clear job management.
Important Factors You need to analyze which core skills are important for the development and growth of your business.
According to research, as a trader, you always communicate and negotiate with your investors, suppliers and customers, so communication and negotiation skills are what traders need to have in order for their business to be stable and functioning. Smoothly.
On the other hand, you also need to have the skills to create and manage your business plan properly, because to ensure that the work that is being carried out in accordance with the plan that they set.
And most importantly, successful traders always have the ability to capture cash flow in their business, they can use their financial resources effectively and can predict the sales and profits of their business. The next period was right, too.
These four points are important for individuals who want to develop into successful entrepreneurs in the future, and for young students who want to continue their studies in business should also consider what skills. That suits your passion, avoid trying to master multiple skills at the same time, because it will make you unsure of any skill or, in short, know nothing for sure.
You know the same skill, but it is better to know more than one, but not sure about one skill. In fact, many business colleges are now established to provide training in business management as a whole, but there are very few colleges that teach basic business skills.
Cam Ed Business Institute, on the other hand, is a school that provides training in one of the most important skills in business: accounting and finance.
The curriculum is designed in accordance with IFRS International Accounting Standards and is also accredited by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, in particular the International Association of Certified Public Accountants (ACCA) with 183 accreditation. Countries around the world).
Studying at CAMED Business School Students will gain an excellent educational experience and extracurricular program, with students earning two degrees in the same curriculum, one of which is accredited by the ACCA. By 183 countries worldwide.
