(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of Cambodia this morning, August 12, 2019, voted to give confidence to Mr. Ith Rady to become a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy for the new term to replace the old one who has expired.
Speaking at the Extraordinary Session of the National Assembly of the 6th Legislature on the morning of August 12, National Assembly President Samdech Heng Samrin announced that Mr. Ith Rady has been elected by 109 National Assembly members as a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy for the new term from now on. .
The General Secretariat of the National Assembly, Mr. Leng Penglong, said that Mr. Ith Rady was the only candidate who had applied to be a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy for the new term.
He said that Mr. Rady is an dignitary who has experience as a judge and served the Ministry of Justice for 15 years and was a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy for one term in the past.
It should be reminded that the Supreme Council of the Magistracy is under the presidency of the King and has 11 members as stated in Article 4 of the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the New Supreme Council of the Magistracy, which is signed by the King. To be used on July 16, 2014 to guarantee and independence of the judiciary.
This institution has jurisdiction and core role is always to transfer and remove judges and kings.
