Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, August 12: 825 illegal vehicles were found and 453 fines were imposed.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for August 12, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 3,761 vehicles, found 825 vehicles violated the law (58% motorcycles), 372 education vehicles and fined 453 units, according to the official report of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 1,884 helmets and goggles were inspected on August 12, 254 education helmets and 187 helmets were fined.
For the results of the 12-day inspection from August 1 to 12, 2019, the police inspected 90,289 vehicles and found 16,417 offending vehicles (58% motorcycles), including education 7,976 units and fined 8,441 units. Cambodian National Assembly Group of Women Parliamentarians Meet to Discuss and Continue to Seek and Protect the Interests of Women, Children and Vulnerable People
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly and Chairperson of the Cambodian National Assembly Group of Women Parliamentarians, on the afternoon of August 12, 2019, chaired a meeting to discuss, continue to seek and protect the interests of Women, children and vulnerable groups on three agendas. The meeting was held at the National Assembly.
The above three agendas include: 1: On the decision on the role and responsibilities of the Cambodian National Assembly group of women parliamentary politicians, 2: on the action plan and further direction of the Cambodian National Assembly group of women parliamentary politicians, 3 : Participation of the opinion of the members of the Cambodian National Assembly group of women parliamentary politicians.
Ms. Khuon Sodary said at the meeting, "As women parliamentarians, we must do all we can to support the interests of women, children and vulnerable groups, because promoting gender equality means both men and women. "There are equal rights, equal opportunities and joint obligations."
"A prosperous country starts from all social cells, that is, the participation of people at all levels, regardless of race, color, sex, age, status and political affiliation," she said.
At the same time, Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary highlighted the efforts and commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in achieving the sustainable development goals of Agenda 2030 "No one is forgotten" by promoting the implementation of three key development policies:
1. Establish a social protection policy framework to develop a strategic plan to ensure income security and reduce economic and financial vulnerabilities, as well as increase people's well-being and strengthen social cohesion.
2: Providing quality and affordable health care services through the Health Equity Fund, which provides free health care services to the poor, as well as providing cash support to women giving birth, as well as to women. Pregnancy and children under 2 years of age from poor families.
3. The introduction of a national policy on the elderly that supports and solves the problems of the elderly.
In addition, she highlighted the work of women MPs in the international arena, especially in early 2019, the Cambodian Parliament hosted for the first time in its history the first Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Women's Forum. 27 abbreviated as (APPF-27). This emphasizes the respect and empowerment of women in participating in international forums.
She added that later, each female MP was also invited to participate in other international forums, such as:
On that occasion, Ms. Kittisangha Bandith encouraged, praised and appreciated the women MPs who sacrificed their physical and mental strength and time to play two roles at the same time, both members of the National Assembly Expert Committee and members of The Cambodian National Assembly of Women Parliamentarians to achieve common goals for the benefit of the Cambodian people by saving money to work responsibly and transparently.
The Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary also thanked all the members of the meeting for their good ideas for the direction and implementation of the work in the future.
According to the announcement of the results of the 48th meeting of the second mandate of the National Anti-Corruption Council, which was received by Fresh News on the afternoon of August 12, 2019, said that Mr. Liam Bunroeun, Director of the Department of Border Management Land, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Pursat Province, inaugurated in 2016, took 140 cases of illegal services.
It should be noted that the leaders of Pursat Provincial Land Management Department, including the Director, Deputy Director and 3 officials of the Cadastral Department, were arrested by the Anti-Corruption Unit in Pursat Province on July 27, 2019 on suspicion of committing corruption. Conspiracy to illegally demand $ 100,000 from landowners in exchange for a building permit.
The three Pursat Provincial Cadastral Officers were sent by the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, including: First: Liam Bunroeun, Director of Pursat Provincial Cadastral Department, Second: Cheang Wutty, Deputy Director of the Department of Labor Construction and 3rd: Te Buntheng, Provincial Cadastral Officer in charge of the port.
