Turkey signed a $ 2.5 billion deal to buy Russia's S-400 air defense missile system in December 2017. On July 25, Russia completed the first phase of handing over the system to Turkey. Due to the adoption of this system, Turkey was withdrawn from the US partnership in the F-35 development program and announced that it would no longer sell stealth fighter jets to Turkey.
