(Tbong Khmum): The Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bunheng, said that the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital, Tbong Khmum, worth about $ 50 million, will be completed on October 27, 2021.
The construction project will be completed according to the plan agreed with Cambodia. In particular, on February 1, 2020, the Chinese-Cambodian side will review half of the contracts or half of the construction to know the quality of these constructions.
This statement was made by the Minister of Health on the occasion of inspecting the construction of this hospital, visiting and treating and providing medicine and mosquito nets to flood victims in safe places in the province. Ratanakiri on August 11-12, 2019.
On that occasion, Minister Mam Bunheng thanked the Chinese government, people and Chinese companies for their support in promoting health care in Cambodia. The Minister confirmed that the project to build this hospital is the second major project with a grant from the Government of the People's Republic of China, the first project is the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Preah Kosom: which just held a groundbreaking ceremony last month. October 2018 recently.
Please be informed that this Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Tbong Khmum was built on March 1, 2019 and completed at the end of October 2021, which covers an area of 24,300 square meters on a total area of 55 815 square meters. This project is built in 40 months.
At the same time, the new hospital will be a regional hospital covering some of the population of Kratie, Ratanakkiri, Stung Treng and Mondulkiri provinces. The new large hospital needs about 456 more staff. It should also be reminded that Tbong Khmum is a newly established province, cut off from Kampong Cham on December 30, 2013, with all the infrastructure being rebuilt. .
