Meanwhile, Ms. Hean Poline, Cambodian Representative to Icha (Icha-Cambodia) of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Vice Chair of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, stated that the "National Youth Advocacy for Human Rights 2019" will be held on From September 18 to 20, 2019, she confirmed that the topic to be discussed is not yet known because the host party requires female candidates to vote.
Separately, the three candidates expressed their high expectations and determination to do their best to win the honor of the motherland, especially to mention the rights and freedoms of the Cambodian people under the current peace. To the young men and women who participated in this competition to know more about the situation of Cambodia in that forum.
The three contestants said that participating in the ASEAN Youth Advocacy "on Human Rights 2019" held in Thailand is an important factor that makes young people in ASEAN as a whole more aware of the problem. Human rights through this debate.
Ministry of Labor Warns Brick Owners Who Use Children for Work to Take Immediate Penal Code
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has again warned that if there is a case of child labor, the Ministry will impose restrictions, if the severity is severe, the Ministry will punish only if the accident can cause loss of body or reach Any loss of life, the Ministry will cooperate with the relevant authorities to implement the Penal Code immediately.
This was confirmed by Mr. Veng Heang, Secretary General of the National Committee Against Child Labor and Director of the Department of Children of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. Along National Road 6A, Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva on the morning of August 12, 2019.
He said the campaign to eradicate child labor in the brick industry was a major step in preventing and changing the attitudes of workers, employers and the community to ensure that all children are protected and that children are protected. Adults get a decent job, not dangerous.
"What we expect at this level of efficiency is that all workers and employers are aware of the use of child labor, preventing children from entering the brick-making industry and good cooperation with institutions to ensure that children "Learning and skills training are the future of contributing to Cambodia's economic competitiveness."
Mr. Veng Heang confirmed that this campaign has been inspected several times by the inspection team, but at the national level, the team visited four times, the first time in 2008, the second time in 2016, and the third time in 2019 and this campaign will continue in 2020 to promote the guarantee and prevention of child labor to a certain extent in almost no or almost no child labor in the brick industry.
