(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism, in collaboration with the Hainan Provincial Department of Commerce of the People's Republic of China, has launched a training course on the development and management of Cambodia's tourism industry towards Industry 4.0 to contribute to meeting human resource needs in the tourism sector. They gain knowledge related to the development of digital technology.
He said that strengthening and developing solidarity and cooperation with developing countries is a fundamental concept of the Chinese government's foreign policy, including the provision of training assistance to the Hainan Provincial Department of Commerce. This is in line with the Chinese government's "Belt and Road" development strategy.
He said, "The nature of the development of the tourism industry in the context of Industry 4.0 will be taught to Cambodian participants on the basis of big data networks and the use of artificial intelligence and e-commerce, which are the core technologies in "Management of tourism services."
Mr. Hor Moniroth reminded that in 2018, the Cambodian-Chinese side had already organized a training course for the development of the Cambodian tourism industry in Sihanoukville, with 50 participants from public and private institutions.
