(Rattanakiri): Dr. Ung Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, this morning, August 12, 2019, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the new Director of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Women's Affairs, with Ms. Vath Ieng Heng as the new Director. Women's Affairs to replace Ms. Chak Meul, who will return to the position of Ratanakkiri Provincial Councilor.
The event was also attended by Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, Mr. Nab Bunheng, Chairman of Ratanakkiri Provincial Council, as well as the leaders of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, the Deputy Governor, the Deputy Director of Provincial Administration, representatives of the Provincial Court Representatives of the provincial prosecutor, the commanders of the three armed forces, the mayor, the district governor, the heads of various departments and units around the province.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Ouk Kimlek, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, said that after research and study by experts in the field of fire prevention and fighting found that some high-rise buildings under construction and operation in Cambodia. Safety for escape in the event of a fire.
Mr. Ouk Kimlek emphasized that in addition to the evacuation gates in the event of a fire, all buildings must be equipped with fire prevention and extinguishing equipment themselves to facilitate the intervention in the event of an accident. . In addition, all buildings must be equipped with an alarm siren to notify those inside the building when an incident occurs.
In response to this, the senior official of the Ministry of Interior in charge of fire safety also presented three forward measures for the owners of various buildings must implement:
First, to prevent fire hazards: The construction of the building must comply with the technical standards of fire, which means that during construction must be equipped with all the materials specified by fire experts.
Second: For rescue operations: High-rise buildings must have a way to escape when a fire occurs, while so far some high-rise buildings do not have this way, and the siren is not equipped, which is why Let people inside the building not know when an accident occurs.
Third, the wiring must find someone who has clear skills on this issue to avoid fire hazards caused by electric shock. If the Ministry finds that those who networked do not have clear skills and when an accident occurs, employees will be held accountable before the law.
Mr. Ouk Kimlek emphasized that all building owners who do not comply with the standards set by the Ministry of Interior, as well as the National Police General Commission, will face the responsibilities set by law. .
However, the Secretary of State for the Ministry of Interior also raised some challenges for fire prevention and fighting operations in Cambodia, as high-rise buildings are now growing significantly and rapidly. The rescue equipment of the authorities is still limited, so the building owner must comply with the standards during construction.
According to the report of Lt. Gen. Sek Phum, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, in the first half of 2019, there were 429/351 fires across the country compared to the same period in 2018. An increase of 78 times.
Chbar Ampov District Administration Holds a Dialogue Forum between Khan Leaders and Khan Councils, Sangkat Forces, Officers, Officers and Village Chiefs
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 12, 2019, Chbar Ampov District Administration held a forum for dialogue between Khan leaders and Khan councilors, Sangkat forces, officials, specialized offices and village chiefs, chaired by Mr. Ou Mareth, Chairman of Khan Council and Mr. Cheng. Monira, Chbar Ampov district governor.
Mr. Cheng Monira said that this is the second time that the Chbar Ampov district administration has held a public forum with the Khan / Sangkat Council, the Armed Forces, the Office of the Specialist Offices and the eight village chiefs who are subordinate to the district hall, different from before. That we do only with the people.
The purpose of this forum is to enable all officers to work under their supervision to raise concerns and difficulties that they are carrying out. At the same time, the forum also focused on discussions on a number of key issues, such as the implementation of village, commune safety policies, public service delivery, environmental sanitation, and infrastructure development.
The district governor stated that through this forum, we will all find important issues as a priority for the district administration to consider reform in the implementation of its activities to improve the quality of life of the people in Khans, especially the poor people in the eight Sangkats to be even better.
The participation of all officials has brought a huge compass and potential for the district administration to reflect on the shortcomings and inactivity points that have been implemented in the past and enable the district board to consider for improvement. Appropriately respond to the needs of the people.
