Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Kouch Chamroeun confirmed to reporters that the recent flooding in Sihanoukville had a number of major causes, such as the high rainfall of nearly 300 mm, which is an unprecedented level. In the last 20-30 years, the loss of rainfall due to increased construction and another reason is that the discharge of water in canals and streams is not fast because the canals and streams are narrowed or landed. Shallow and so on.
According to the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, the canals and natural streams in Sihanoukville, which are the main source of water flow, are very shallow and some places have been built in violation of the canal's food. O loses the ability to release water.
In connection with the construction of canals and streams, it was found that both the construction of people's houses and the construction of hotels and other commercial buildings were built in violation of the canals and streams. The construction of encroachments on canals and streams slowed the release of water, and when it rained heavily, the city was flooded.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, and Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, arrived in Sihanoukville on August 10 after heavy flooding. And find ways to rehabilitate canals to increase drainage capacity.
Currently, many vehicles of the Ministry of Water Resources, Ministry of Public Works and Chinese road construction companies are being deployed along the canals and streams in Sihanoukville to expand and rehabilitate canals.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun asserted that with the blue rain from Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, the rehabilitation of this canal will be done according to the original size of Lay or O. And if there is no dismantling, action will be taken according to the law.
Officials from the Ministry of Water Resources confirmed that the remaining work is to strengthen the isolated area.
During the past 10 days, there has been continuous rain, especially on the night of August 10, with a volume of up to 139 mm (total rainfall up to 350-400 meters), causing landslides in the head. 15 meters long dam and 15 meters diversion dam body, total 30 meters.
