(Preah Vihear): A woman has been lost in the forest for 2 nights and 3 days while entering the forest to pick mushrooms with many other villagers since August 7, 2019.
Tbeng Meanchey district police chief Lt. Col. Rith Sona told Fresh News that prior to the incident, the woman, along with about 19 villagers, had driven a car from Bak Kam village, Chhean Mok commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, to pick it up. Mushrooms in the forest, school point, road to Preah Vihear temple.
The district inspector added that while entering the forest to remove mushrooms for about two hours, the driver of the car also called the person who was removing mushrooms in the forest to return. But at that time, the victim was missing and could not be found, so they did not return the phone call.
Mr. Rith Sona continued that after receiving information from the residents and the families of the victims, the police and about 80 villagers immediately went into the forest to look for her but could not find her. At 11:37 pm on August 9, 2019, the district police and residents arrived at Prey Chea Phleung in Yeang commune, Choam Ksan district and met a woman who was lost in the forest and brought her back. The village reunites the family safely.
