Opinion: What are the necessary measures to be taken to avoid flooding Sihanoukville?
(Phnom Penh): A heavy rain on the night of August 8 to 9, 2019 caused the worst flooding in history in Sihanoukville, the second largest economic city after Phnom Penh. . Homes, property, and many urban infrastructure systems were damaged and devastated.
Many questions have been raised as to what caused the floods. Mistakes from Chinese investors coming in? Caused by high rainfall? Caused by the deletion of Boeung Prek Dam or because the drainage system was violated?
Increased construction, removal of lakes, dams, loss of surface area and heavy rainfall were one of the reasons for the floods. But one of the major problems that has been found to be causing such severe flooding is that drainage systems such as canals and streams have been blocked by landslides for residential and other construction.
Officials have leaked that canals and streams, which are a system for releasing rainwater in Sihanoukville, have been encroached upon by up to 50 percent of the land used for residential, commercial and hotel construction. Among them, some canals and streams up to 10 meters wide have been filled with soil and used for construction up to 8 meters.
So what measures need to be taken to alleviate flooding in Sihanoukville?
The flooding of Sihanoukville is one of the new issues that requires the provincial authorities as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia as a whole to find effective ways and mechanisms to solve it. Liberation of canals and streams is a must.
Buildings, including people's homes and other small and large buildings, flooded with canals and streams, must be demolished without permission. Then, the rehabilitation of canals deeper and widening with the proper arrangement of infrastructure along canals and streams is also a matter of great concern.
Another thing is that the provision of space for rainwater in Sihanoukville is also important and necessary. Rainwater can not be allowed to flow into the sea immediately because it will cause the sea water to freeze quickly.
About 21 vehicles belonging to the Ministry of Water Resources, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and a Chinese road construction company were also sent to Sihanoukville for operation to rehabilitate canals and streams.
Plans to liberate Sihanoukville from flooding could not be achieved if residents, homeowners and other builders who violated canals and streams did not participate. Therefore, the cooperation of the owners of the construction site, encroachment on canals and streams is another important and necessary thing to achieve the plan to save Sihanoukville from flooding.
