Legal Awareness: Applying for a Construction Permit
(Phnom Penh): The construction sector in Cambodia is now beginning to grow and prosper due to the increase in investors and population growth, so the demand for people is also increasing, which we observe See that there are houses or other buildings are being built to meet the needs of the people as well as foreign investors.
At the same time, to ensure that the construction and constructions are carried out in accordance with legal standards and do not cause any problems or accidents eventually, those who wish to build new buildings must obtain a construction permit. First of all, the conditions for requesting this letter are also specified by the law of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
To better understand the above procedure for applying for a permit, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, would like to explain and share the topic of "Application for a Construction Permit". To all students as follows:
Pursuant to Sub-Decree No. 86 on the Construction Permit of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia dated 19 December 1997 Existing (in case the reconstruction changes the shape or aspect of the building) in cities and towns.
Article 9 of the sub-decree on the construction permit states the necessary documents for the following applications:
According to the above sub-decree, the period for reviewing the construction permit is limited to 45 working days. This period counts from the day that all the documents attached to the construction permit application are completed. At the end of this deadline, the applicant will be notified of a written decision on permission, denial or authorization, but requesting further amendments.
According to the Inter-Ministerial Prakas between the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction No. 033 January 12, 2006 The application fee is based on the size of the area and the type of construction project.
Example: For a residential construction project with a construction area of 500 square meters, the service cost varies depending on the type of house, such as the villa must pay between 600,000 riels to 1.8 million riels. For flats, the service fee is between 400,000 Riel and 1.2 million Riel, and for stone houses under the upper tree, the price is between 140,000 Riel and 220,000 Riel.
At the same time, all citizens should understand and strictly implement the above procedures, because all construction that started without a construction permit from the competent authority will be considered a crime and the construction site. Will be stopped immediately.
In addition, individuals who violate the orders of the competent officials will be charged and all equipment at the site will be confiscated and may be subject to transaction penalties. (Pursuant to Article 24 of Sub-Decree No. 86 on Construction Permit dated 19 December 1997 and Pursuant to the Inter-Ministerial Prakas on Procedures and Procedures for Construction Inspection No. 118 PRK / DNS) Posted on August 2, 2019).
