Senior Minister Kun Kim Meets and Distributes Gifts to More Than 300 Veterans in Kandal Province
(Kandal): Mr. Kun Kim, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, met with 311 Veterans Association members at the headquarters of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Koki Commune, Kien Svay District. Kandal Province.
The ceremony on the morning of August 10, 2019 was also attended by Mr. Ek Kret, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, General Meas Savon, Director General of the General Department of Military Service, Ministry of National Defense and Director General of Koh Thmey Technology and Many other relevant officials as well.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim also sent a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to all veterans living here and instructed them to be careful and protect themselves from various diseases and strive to do their job. Already to help family life and be united to help each other in business, regardless of color, race or political affiliation.
The Senior Minister also instructed the Provincial Veterans Association to visit the landless members in order to respect the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to build more.
Senior Minister Kun Kim added that a total of more than 130,000 veterans across the country are key players in defending the motherland to achieve peace, which is why development is as progress as it is now. Therefore, they should receive encouragement and support in return for this sacrifice.
It should be noted that the gifts distributed to the people at this time received 100,000 Riels, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 kg of sugar, 1 packet of bean curd and 25 kg of rice, which was sponsored by Koh Thmey Technology Co., Ltd., which is conducting investment operations in Cambodia, always pays close attention to supporting the heroism of soldiers and veterans in Cambodia.
