Senior Minister Kun Kim: Floods continue to hit Kon Mom district as more than 200 families are evacuated to safety
(Ratanakkiri): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, told Fresh News from Ratanakkiri province on the afternoon of August 10, 2019 that floods are continuing to hit Serei Mongkul commune, Kon Mom district. Affecting homes, about 646 families were flooded.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, who is working hard, claimed that of the 646 families in Serei Mongkul commune who were affected by the floods, more than 200 families were evacuated by the authorities. Children, the elderly and the disabled.
According to Senior Minister Kun Kim, about 250 armed forces and local authorities have been working together to rescue people by using about 50 boats to gather and evacuate people as the floodwaters rise and flood their roofs. Because now some houses are half submerged.
As for the safe haven, Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that the authorities have organized security and order for the people and prepared a roof for those who have to be evacuated to safety while some people are at school. At a relative's house.
However, the First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, who was in charge of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, claimed that due to the continuous notification, the vulnerable people in Kon Mom district were also self-reliant. Also, they have prepared daily necessities and some houses have their own boats.
As for the crops, Mr. Kun Kim said that according to the inspection and assessment, the rice field in Serei Mongkul commune, Kon Mom district was flooded about 1,661 hectares and about 263 hectares of farmland, but the extent of the damage could not be determined. It can be concluded yet, that is, until the water recedes.
As for the flood situation, Senior Minister Kun Kim pointed out that the water level in Lumphat district was 3 cm, but the authorities are still monitoring to determine whether the water level will continue to rise to make it easier to evacuate people to the local area. Get safe.
In addition, for the rescue operation, the Senior Minister noted that both the provincial authorities and the provincial disaster management committee, together with the competent authorities, cooperated well and worked hard as servants of the people. Unconditionally.
Monks and villagers in Kampong Reap commune call on philanthropists to help build flood defenses
(Kampong Cham): Monks and villagers in Kampong Reap commune, Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province, called on philanthropists to donate money to help build a dam to prevent flooding.
After receiving the concrete road, the people in Kampong Ream commune are also worried about the flood and the damage to the road. To protect the road from flooding or flooding during the rainy season, monks and residents in the commune have agreed to build a dam to protect the road.
Bhikkhu Sophat Mongkul Van Sophin, the chief abbot of Wat Ratanak Por Rainsy (Kampong Sdey), told Fresh News that the concrete road that Kampong Sang commune is building is very important for the people. Therefore, the people are worried that the water will flow and hit and cause damage, so they decided to build a dam to protect the water.
According to the Venerable, the total length of the road protection dam is about 160 meters, with a construction cost of about 20 million riels. According to the Venerable Preah Chao Athikar Wat Ratanak Por Rainsy, there is no construction budget yet, so the Venerable and the people decided to call for funding from philanthropists.
"I would like to wish all the relatives, Excellencies, Lok Chumteav, all the people near and far, please join in the generous efforts to help build this dam, because it is very important for the monks and the people." "If we do not build a dam, it will damage our roads." Venerable Van Sophin has a priest to confirm.
Ministry of Tourism sets up online technology to manage tourism professional training
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has organized training courses for trainers on E-Certificate technology for tourism vocational training for officials of the Ministry of Tourism and the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism, university staff, vocational schools and tourism vocational training institutes recognized by Ministry of Tourism under the chairmanship of Mr. Nep Samuth, Director General of Tourism Industry Management.
It has the following main functions:
1: Facilitate the issuance of various types of certificates, such as training courses by the Ministry of Tourism or by the Vocational School of Tourism accredited by the Ministry of Tourism.
2: Assist in the management of online tourism vocational training.
3: Confirm the identity of the biography of the students and participants in the training.
4: Keep data and monitor the professional skills of students.
Mr. Nep Samuth said that through the E-Certificate system, it will be easier for universities, tourism vocational training institutes and students to manage and store necessary data and information without fear of loss or fraud. .
He said it was also an important tool to support the human resource development strategy in the tourism sector (2018-2025) towards achieving the goal of "one employee, one skill" by 2025 and lifelong learning by 2030 for Cambodian youth in tourism.
It should be noted that in the future, this system will be a model that can be matched with the automated online tourism license application system, which provides ease of management and provides opportunities for young Cambodians working in the tourism sector. Encouragement from tourism business owners to strengthen professional capacity or in internships.
Please note that the tourism vocational training technology management system is scheduled to be officially announced under the presidency of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism at the end of September 2019.
(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police has launched a campaign to promote helmet wearing nationwide for a full month, and for August 10, 2019, the traffic police force in 19 capitals and provinces inspected a number of motorcyclists. Of the 8,400, 2,603 were forced to wear helmets, accounting for 31 percent. This is according to the report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department, which was obtained by Fresh News.
This measure is implemented nationwide, with the requirement to find a helmet to be worn before being allowed to travel without penalty for one month from July 19, 2019 onwards. Deputy PM Yim Chhay Ly Praises Ministry of Commerce for Two Works to Promote Cambodia's Rice Sector
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, praised the Ministry of Commerce for its efforts to expand the Cambodian rice market and for the election of the President and Board members of the Federation. Cambodian Rice - The third mandate is transparent to lead the development of the national rice sector.
The Deputy Prime Minister made the remarks while presiding over the closing ceremony of the 2019 General Assembly of the Cambodian Rice Federation, which was held on the afternoon of August 9, 2019 at the Phnom Penh Hotel with the participation of Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister. Business, along with senior officials in the Royal Government of Cambodia, representing the private sector and many farmers.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly praised Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, for his efforts to negotiate a comprehensive market for Cambodian rice products in close cooperation with the Cambodian Rice Federation and other relevant institutions.
The Deputy Prime Minister encouraged the leaders of the new mandate of the Cambodian Rice Federation to continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Commerce and agricultural communities in implementing contract farming programs to produce maximum and high quality organic rice in order to boost the rice industry and promote Rice exports in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
To strengthen the sustainable development of the rice sector, the Deputy Prime Minister also gave the following three key recommendations to the Rice Federation:
1. Strengthen and expand cooperation with relevant institutions and development partners, including the private sector, both domestically and abroad, to achieve a national policy to promote rice production.
2. Maintain fair competition in the market to promote efficient, transparent exports and maintain the interests of farmers and agricultural communities by increasing incomes and reducing poverty, as well as maintaining adequate food security and nutrition. For Cambodian children.
3. Encourage and strengthen the participation of farmers and farming communities, as well as protect their interests by creating a favorable and convenient environment for the production and supply of quality rice.
(Phnom Penh): A legal landowner in Prek Talong 2 village, Chak Angre Krom commune, Meanchey district, who was erected a stone fence by Tycoon Chea Bunleng to cover the front of his plot of land and has filed a complaint to the commune authorities for help. For almost two years now, there has been no solution to this case, which has been claimed by the landowners to be a conspiracy between the tycoon and the authorities because they want him to sell the land.
As for the village and sangkat authorities, when he went to inquire, he was always advised to meet with the tycoon, while the tycoon wanted to buy his land to expand to build more flats, but he refused to sell at a cheaper price. The village and commune authorities, while he took the letter to transfer the land ownership to someone else, refused to do so because they intended to sell the land to the tycoon, but at a price far cheaper than the market, which he could not accept.
The landowner's representative would like to appeal to Meanchey District Governor Pich Keo Mony, especially Phnom Penh Governor Khuong Sreng, to help provide justice to his victims, because the tycoon has been fencing off the plot for almost two years and there is no solution.
