It should be noted that on the afternoon of August 9, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, ordered the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, the National Committee for Disaster Management and all relevant authorities to take high measures for flood relief and Avoid harm to the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's order is due to the fact that Cambodia has been experiencing natural disasters due to the continuous flooding these days, which has caused some provinces to be inundated, as was the case in Sihanoukville. And so on.
At the same time, the Ministry of Water Resources also advised people living along the Mekong River in low-lying areas to collect agricultural products on time and take care to avoid any possible accidents.
More than 400 medical team of Mr. Hun Many will visit and treat people in Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province for free tomorrow
(Kampong Cham): On the morning of August 11, 2019, tomorrow, the team of more than 400 volunteer doctors, Mr. HUN Many, will continue to check and treat and distribute free medicine to more than 2 people. Thousands at Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Meanchey High School, Steung Commune, Cheung Prey District, Kampong Cham Province.
Kampong Cham Provincial Governor claims to issue land titles to people in Kbal Teuk resort area, Chamkar Leu district if it is not illegal
(Kampong Cham): More than 23 families who own land around Kbal Teuk resort in Sopor village, Ta Ong commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province, have expressed concern over the loss of their farmland, which they used to enjoy for many years, after officials Land management, urban planning and construction refused to issue title deeds to them.
In a letter of intervention submitted to Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, which was received by Fresh News on August 10, 2019, the villagers claimed that they had enjoyed farming on their ancestral land since their ancestors. The people also claim that in 1997, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had announced to cut off this land for the people to farm according to the regime that the state had distributed.
According to the letter requesting the intervention, the villagers quoted an official from the Office of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Chamkar Leu District stating that the title deed could not be issued to the people because the land was deducted as land ownership. Of the state.
According to some sources from the villagers, officials have been conspiring with investors to turn the land into a resort, so they refused to issue ownership to them, while other nearby residents have already issued title deeds. And. The people support the development of vacant state land in the existing Kbal Tuek resort area, but they do not support the land they have been enjoying for years.
Concerned about losing their land, the villagers asked the provincial governor of Kampong Cham to intervene to solve the problem and issue a title deed to them to be used for subsistence farming.
Mr. Un Chanda confirmed that he had already received the letter requesting the people's intervention. He also assigned the district governor to submit reports and relevant information to find a solution.
The provincial governor also told the people not to worry, he will check if the land is not illegal, he will facilitate the issuance of title deeds to them.
