General Neth Savoeun and Sar Sokha Chair a Meeting to Prepare a Coordinating Mechanism for the Bankruptcy Exam
(Phnom Penh): General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, and Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, on behalf of Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, chaired a meeting on August 9, 2019. High School Diploma Examination Coordinating Mechanism.
Speaking on that occasion, General Dr. Neth Savoeun instructed the authorities, competent forces and all relevant officials to maintain security, safety and order during the high school diploma exam.
The National Police Commissioner General stated that for the protection of security, security and order during the high school diploma exam, the authorities will use only the National Police Force and the Royal Gendarmerie, while the military force is only ready to intervene in case of emergency.
General Neth Savoeun said that the capital-provincial commissioners with private security companies must organize private security forces and people to be a support force in case of insufficient force, and for this protection, all law enforcement forces have the duty to protect only outside the premises. Only the examination center, but the force can enter the examination center only if there is a call for intervention from the center director if necessary.
The General has ordered the Capital-Provincial Administrative Unity Command and the Commissioner of the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie, as well as the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, to set August 15 as a high day to tighten security and order. 19th and 20th, successful operation must be prepared for 3 points:
* First: Protect the transportation of exam subjects * Second: Protect the place to store subjects * Third: Protect the examination center.
The General Commissioner of the National Police also requested the Ministry of Education, which is in charge of organizing the 2019 High School Diploma Examination, to: First, ban the armed forces from entering the examination center, and second: Check the candidates before entering the examination room Also, do not use the armed forces, and thirdly, the storage of electronic materials, requesting the center to self-manage the storage and other records at the examination center directly.
He suggested that young people, teachers, youth scouts or women be used to do this work, except in cases where there is an urgent need to apply for explosives, toxic substances and violence, and the need for competent forces to intervene in a timely manner.
According to the press release of the Ministry of Land Management on the night of August 9, 2019, this morning, the technical working group of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction inspected the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. Construction site of a multi-functional building, 9 storeys high. After inspecting, it was found that the construction did not have a construction permit and did not have a construction permit.
In this announcement, after inspecting the above risks and to ensure the security, safety, protection of property and lives of the people, the Construction Quality Control Committee in Sihanoukville requested the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration to take action to suspend construction sites. Immediately prohibit accommodation, ban the use of construction, suspend all business operations in the building and evacuate all buildings.
The team also required to dismantle this building because this construction is not safe and the quality is suitable according to the construction specifications. Residents living in the vicinity of the building must be on high alert and leave their homes immediately until disposal is completed. Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Celebrate a Dinner for the President of Sri Lanka and His Wife
(Phnom Penh): On the night of August 9, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen held a banquet for the highest honor to Mr. Maitripala Sirisena, President of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Socialist Democratic Republic of Sri Lanka and his wife on a state visit to Cambodia.
At the Family Dinner held at Sofitel Phokitra Phnom Penh, Mr. Maitripala Sirisena and his wife were warmly welcomed by Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit.
The Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit expressed their deepest affection to the presence of the President and his wife, who took the most valuable time to pay a state visit to Cambodia, a country with a history of traditional relations. And religion has been together for a long time.
As mentioned at the bilateral meeting held on August 8, Mr. Maitripala Sirisena informed the Prime Minister that the relationship between Cambodia and Sri Lanka is very long. That is more than a thousand years ago, and this relationship is based on Buddhist philosophy and religious relations as well.
In addition, the President also informed Samdech Techo that his current visit to Cambodia is to expand and strengthen relations between the two countries. He said that the two countries should promote relations between the two countries through education, culture, tourism, trade, civil aviation and especially direct flights to Cambodia or from Cambodia to Sri Lanka. .
As mentioned at the summit on August 8 at the banquet, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit also carefully discussed the cooperation between the two countries. On the economic and trade sectors.
He said the trade volume between the two countries was still small, so the two countries should look at other possibilities to boost trade and investment between the two countries. The same goes for tourism, religion and education.
It should be noted that the President of Sri Lanka and his wife paid a state visit to Cambodia on August 7 and are scheduled to leave Cambodia for Sri Lanka on August 10 tomorrow.
General Sao Sokha tells all military officers not to be involved in forestry crimes
(Preah Vihear): Speaking from Preah Vihear province, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Chairman of the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resources, instructed all military officers and military families to ban Involved in forest crime, whether timber is legal or illegal, and must defend the nation, serve the people, respect the law and crack down on crime.
The above-mentioned reminder of General Sao Sokha was made during a meeting with officers and deputies of the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie and the families of the disabled military personnel who died on the afternoon of August 9, 2019. .
This afternoon, General Sao Sokha also continued to lead a meeting to monitor the prevention and suppression of forest crime in Preah Vihear province after the meeting this morning in Stung Treng.
Yesterday, General Sao Sokha continued to chair a meeting to review the work of preventing and cracking down on natural resource crimes in Ratanakkiri province, while on August 7, 2019, General Sao Sokha chaired a meeting in Mondulkiri province.
