(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a new announcement on the weather in Cambodia from 10 to 16 August 2019, stating that the effects of storms and southwest monsoon caused coastal provinces, especially Preah. Sihanoukville and Koh Kong, as well as provinces bordering Vietnam, continued to receive heavy rains, possibly causing flash floods, while other provincial capitals received more or less rain.
The Ministry of Water Resources confirmed the weather in Cambodia from 10 to 16 August as follows:
1. Coastal provinces, especially Koh Kong and Sihanoukville will continue to receive moderate to heavy rainfall. There will be heavy rain, strong winds, and high waves on the sea.
Kampong Thom, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Mondulkiri, Kratie, Stung Treng and Ratanakkiri provinces will receive moderate to heavy rainfall.
3: Preah Vihear, Siem Reap, Battambang, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey and Oddar Meanchey provinces will have light to moderate rain.
4: Kampong Speu, Takeo, Kandal and Phnom Penh will have light to moderate rain.
At the same time, the ministry called on people to continue to pay more attention to the sea area with heavy rain, strong winds and high waves.
