The final balance of the floods in Sihanoukville: 3 dead, 2 Cambodians, 1 Chinese, water receded, water supply and electricity supply normal
(Preah Sihanouk): As of around 9 pm on August 9, 2019, the flood situation in Sihanoukville has eased. In the final analysis, the floods killed three people, including two Cambodians and a Chinese national, while damaging property. Separately, clean water and electricity are also connected to the people to use normally.
In addition to many problems, including the construction of infrastructure, security, order, aesthetics, as well as solving the problems of people's lives, and the angels seem to put a new problem to test the ability of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, the governor. New of Sihanoukville. Unprecedented rainfall over Sihanoukville from the night of August 8 until 6 pm on August 9 has just subsided.
The heavy rains caused floodwaters to flow into the sea, but did not cause severe flooding in the lowlands of Sihanoukville. Mr. Kouch Chamroeun told Fresh News that the rainfall in Sihanoukville ranged from 272 mm to 224 mm.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun claimed that such a situation had never happened in Sihanoukville. In 2007, the province experienced heavy rain, but not for long, it rained for more than an hour, the water level was only 81 mm.
To solve the flood, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, on behalf of the Provincial Command, led the force to evacuate the people to find a safe place and find a way to release the water, in which all forces in the province have intervened and Samdech Techo Hun Sen The Prime Minister of Cambodia also released a national task force.
Regarding the flood, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun claimed that until the night of August 9, 2019, the water had receded almost completely in a few places, but not as severe as yesterday. A large number of evacuees have returned to their homes. But some have not yet returned to their homes, with some continuing to stay with relatives and friends.
As for the water and electricity network, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun confirmed that until tonight, it has been supplied to the people as usual. There are only a few houses in Sangkat 1 around Khleang Leu Market that have not been supplied yet because the water is still flooded.
The extent of the damage to people's property has not yet been determined. However, the governor was deeply saddened by the flooding, which left two Cambodians and their wives dead when a fence collapsed and a Chinese man was killed by a collapsed fence in Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district. Two Cambodian victims have been sent to their hometowns in Tbong Khmum province.
With the severe damage from the floods, the Governor of Sihanoukville spent many hours cutting water to solve the problem, expressed regret and asked for high understanding from the people in Sihanoukville. Who suffered damage to property.
Senior Health Official: Community and Family Contribute to Advising Drug Addicts to Get Medical Treatment
(Phnom Penh): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, said that the community and the family have played an important role in helping drug addicts to receive medical treatment until they recover.
At the same time, Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, also visited drug addicts who are resting in the Opportunity I Health Center and advised and educated drug patients to be highly committed to stop using drugs. And be in regular treatment with a specialist, and after recovering from treatment, do not return to drug use, despite the pull of friends or drug dealers.
The Secretary of State stated that in the first half of 2019, Opportunity Health Center provided medical services to 1,665 drug patients (97 females) and about 350 to 400 drug patients per day. Receive daily health services, mostly methamphetamine addicts, sent by the I Opportunity Center's Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
During the visit of Teuk Thla Health Center, Ms. O Vandin also met with health officials who are working there and examined the mental health and drug abuse, which has been operating since 2016, with 3 specialized doctors. Provides mental health and drug addiction screening and treatment services.
According to the director of Teuk Thla Health Center, some drug addicts who have recovered from treatment here have advised other drug patients to come to our doctor for further treatment. Recovered from this addiction like him.
As a result, Ms. O Vandin recommended the following recommendations and solutions:
* Data management of drug addicts receiving treatment services should be divided into the number of old patients, the number of new patients and the number of those who drop out of treatment and must be reported regularly with the correct report form.
* Institutions involved in referring patients should have a mechanism for evaluating the effectiveness of treatment when repatriating them to the community to identify factors that lead drug patients to stop using or continue using drugs. Drugs.
Please also note that there are 49 health facilities that operate mental health and drug services in Phnom Penh, including:
1: Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital 2: Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Preah Kosamak 3: Phnom Penh Referral Hospital 4: Meanchey Referral Hospital 5: Samdech Ov Referral Hospital 6: Pochentong Referral Hospital 7: Friendship Referral Hospital Cambodia-China Sen Sok 8: Dangkor Referral Hospital 9: Prek Pnov Referral Hospital and 40 other health centers.
