Ministry of Social Affairs signs MoU with 6 organizations to help educate and care for vulnerable and vulnerable orphans in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with six organizations to assist in the social sector, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, focusing on the education and care of vulnerable orphans and Victims in Cambodia.
The signing ceremony of the MoU was officially held on August 9, 2019 with the participation of Mr. Touch Channy, Director General of the Technical Department of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, representing Mr. Vong Soth, Minister. The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation will be joined by the leaders of the six organizations, as well as relevant government officials of the Ministry of Social Affairs.
In addition, Mr. Touch Channy requested the working group of ministries and organizations that are now cooperating to work as carefully as possible. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs, meanwhile, continues to welcome stakeholders and organizations to assist victims in Cambodia to have a better standard of living.
It should be noted that the six organizations that signed the agreement with the Ministry of Social Affairs now are all organizations that have contributed and acted to help educate and care for vulnerable and vulnerable orphans in Cambodia.
