BERLIN: Germany's refusal to participate in US-initiated efforts to build an international force to patrol the Persian Gulf is a shame for Washington, which wants to show Iran that the West has strong solidarity. This is according to a release by Russian media Sputnik on Friday, August 9, 2019.
German Foreign Minister Heiko Maas has made it clear that Berlin will not join US plans to form a Persian Gulf joint force to counter Iran. However, according to US government officials, Washington is continuing to persuade and pressure Berlin to reconsider its decision.
According to the officials, the refusal of Germany, a major ally of the United States, would make Tehran see that the West is not united. According to Maas, the reason Berlin does not want to be tied to the US plan is because of fears of falling into the flames of war with Iran if tensions continue to escalate.
