Officials from Kampong Chhnang Provincial CamControl continued to inspect goods at Kraing Lvea Market and stalls around the market, but did not find any defective goods
(Kampong Chhnang): For the health of the people as well as food safety, CamControl officials in Stung Treng province on August 9, 2019, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce, local authorities and the market commission, continued to disseminate the quality of food safety and food inspection. And pre-packaged goods at Kraing Lvea market and stalls around the market in Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province, no defective goods were found.
Mr. Yiv Narin, Branch Manager of CamControl in Kampong Chhnang Province, said that the purpose of the inspection was to prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit labels, expiration dates and the presence of banned chemicals that could harm people's health.
Mr. Yiv Narin also advised traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products and services to avoid harm to health, people will be able to face the law.
On the other hand, the team monitored the retail price at 3 stations / depots, and the retail price was in line with the price set by the Ministry.
Defective Orange Juice, Fish Sauce and Butter Found for Sale at Orussey Thmey Market and Kilo 2 Market, Camcontrol Officials in Stung Treng Province
(Stung Treng): For the health of the people as well as food safety, officials of CamControl Stung Treng Branch on August 9, 2019, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce, local authorities and the Market Commission, continued to disseminate the quality of food safety and control of food products. And pre-packaged goods in two markets, Orussey Thmey Market and Kilo 2 Market in Stung Treng City, found some expired goods.
Mr. Kim Pros, President of CamControl Stung Treng Branch, said that the purpose of the inspection was to prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit labels, expiration dates and banned chemicals that could affect people's health.
According to the branch manager, as a result, professional officers found the display of defective and expired goods, including:
* First: Orussey Thmey Market confiscated 48 bottles of orange juice after the expiration date * Second: Market 2 kilos (2 kilos) confiscated expired goods and some quality.
After that, the CamControl officer recorded the confiscation of the goods and stored them at the provincial branch to be destroyed and instructed the traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products, goods and services to avoid any impact. To the health of the people will be able to face the law more.
Ministry of Environment organizes forum on protection and conservation of natural resources
Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, stated that the Ministry of Environment has established a community to protect natural areas to establish a dialogue partnership between the Ministry of Environment and local communities in protecting the environment and natural resources. Currently, there are 168 protected areas under the control of the Ministry of Environment.
"We should move away from the idea of using natural resources by embracing new things without putting pressure on natural resources," he said. Within this framework, the Ministry of Environment, which has the General Department of Local Communities, plays an important role in developing local communities and improving community livelihoods, focusing on community work, establishing ecotourism sites and heritage conservation in protected areas.
At the same time, he said, the Ministry of Environment has set up an environmental fund to support the implementation of local community development plans. Mr. Say Sam Al appealed to communities not only for protected areas under the Ministry of Environment, but also for fishing and forestry communities to request funding from the Ministry of Environment to be used for biodiversity and natural resource conservation.
It should be noted that in the past, the Ministry of Environment has provided funding to some communities and conservationists to protect and manage natural resources, such as the Sang Ruk Vorn community in Oddar Meanchey province, the elephant conservation project in Ratanakkiri province, the conservation project at Phnom Pok-Phnom Tnaot Wildlife Sanctuary. Preah Vihear province and peacock conservation project.
He emphasized that the Royal Government, the Ministry of Environment and other relevant institutions will continue their mission and implement their work plans to increase efficiency in the cause of the environment and natural resources to meet the sacred aspirations of the people of Cambodia and accept the ideas raised to become the goal. Politics for implementation. Su-30 fighter jet crashes in northeast India
