New Sihanoukville Commander-in-Chief, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet: My Will and Principles of Leadership Not to Be Bribed in Appointing Unit Leaders
(Preah Sihanouk): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, stated that his will and principles of leadership should not be bribed in appointing unit leaders for personal gain. No.
He said this on the occasion of presiding over the appointment ceremony to change the position of Commander of Sihanoukville Military Operation Area, which was held on August 8, 2019. According to the decision, Colonel Nou Sam Ol was the Commander of the Sihanoukville Provincial Military Operations Area, replacing Major General Savin Vibol, who was given a new job.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet stated that the correct selection of unit leaders (Commander-in-Chief) is a factor that ensures unity, solidarity and efficiency. The principle of the Army is to select the leaders of the units from the regional level, the military operations and the border forces upwards, to have an Army Commission to review and evaluate in order to ensure transparency and efficiency.
The Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces stated: "The will and principle of my leadership (Commander-in-Chief of the Army) is not to take bribes in appointing unit leaders for personal gain, to select officers who "Willing to serve the nation by assessing the ability, virtue, morality, health experience, because we think of the individual to be fair, transparent, capable, sustainable and effective of the organization.
"This is what we strive for to give to those who work long hours in the unit." This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Hun Manet.
