A spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources said the disaster was caused by rainfall in both Cambodia and Vietnam, but that the situation remained stable while the ministry was monitoring.
According to a report by the Ministry of Water Resources, 3,082 families, equivalent to 13,446 people living along the Srepok River in Lumphat district, in 14 villages in three communes are inundated. . Meanwhile, 1,154 families in Kon Mom district, equivalent to 2,191 people in 6 villages in 2 communes, are also suffering from flooding.
