Next week, the National Assembly will hold a session to elect a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy.
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly will convene an extraordinary session of the 6th legislature on the morning of Monday, August 12, 2019 to elect a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy for a new term to replace the old one who has expired. This is according to the decision of the meeting of the National Assembly Standing Committee on the morning of August 9, 2019.
The meeting of the National Assembly Standing Committee, chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, also approved two draft laws proposed by the Royal Government for review.
The other draft law is the draft law on the social security system. The National Assembly Standing Committee decided to hand over to the National Assembly Committee on Health, Social Affairs, Veterans, Youth Rehabilitation, Vocational Training and Women's Affairs to review and study and report back to the National Assembly Standing Committee.
