CARE Announces Private Construction Contractor for Mondulkiri Student Building
(Phnom Penh): CARE, an international development organization working to combat global poverty, has announced a bid for a private construction contractor to build a school building for students in Busra Village, Busra Commune, Pichreada District, Mondulkiri Province.
If you are interested in any private construction contractor, please go to the office of Care Cambodia in Phnom Penh, located at 216, 4th floor, Norodom Blvd., Sangkat Tonle Bassac 1, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh. And at CARE Cambodia office in Mondulkiri province, located in Ospean village, Sangkat Spean Meanchey, Sen Monorom city from 8:00 am to 12:00 noon and from 2:00 pm to 5:00 pm.
CARE is an international development organization working towards the global fight against poverty, with a particular focus on women and girls to bring about sustainable change in their communities. CARE aims to address the root causes of poverty and social injustice and bring lasting change to the lives of the poor and vulnerable.
CARE was founded in 1945. CARE currently works with more than 90 countries around the world. CARE has been working with the Cambodian people since 1973, with an office in Phnom Penh since 1991.
Today, CARE focuses specifically on disadvantaged and vulnerable women in Cambodia by empowering them. CARE has worked with thousands of people in Cambodia, especially with women who have migrated to cities, women and girls who are ethnic minorities, and rural women who have gone through denial of their rights. Many times.
