The statement of the Chief of the National Defense of Cambodia was made on August 9, 2019, during the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the repatriation of 382 Cambodian peacekeepers. Successfully completed missions in Mali and South Sudan at the Council of Ministers.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said: "I have confirmed and now we will continue to do this work and now our reserve force called mobile reserve force when needed, we will send. "Immediately, despite the shortcomings, I want other countries to have peace like Cambodia."
Since 2006, Cambodia has sent more than 5,000 peacekeepers to UN missions in eight countries around the world, including the Republic of Sudan, South Sudan, Lebanon, Cyprus, Syria and Chad. Mali and early Central Africa. In 2019, Cambodia has more than 800 troops serving overseas missions under the United Nations umbrella.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh continued that the Cambodian people are very proud that the Cambodian peacekeepers have gone on international missions in the past, which have been recognized as a unit and a country that sends The force went to the operation full of ability and made the most important contribution to bring the foreign nations back to peace quickly.
On that occasion, the Cambodian Hat Forces, which had just completed its mission under the United Nations umbrella, also expressed their pride and years of work experience in a country that is not yet fully at peace. They stated that as a Cambodian force, we are very proud to contribute to this important work for humanitarian work.
Constitutional Council elects Plang Chhlam as a member of the Supreme Council of the new mandate
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Plang Chhlam has been elected by the Constitutional Council as a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy for a new term. The election ceremony was held on the morning of August 9, 2019 under the chairmanship of Mr. Im Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council.
Please note that in accordance with Article 4, point 6 of the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy and Letter No. 1357 KYOR / 19 dated 19 July 2019 of the Ministry of Justice requesting the Council Charter for the election of one dignitary as a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy, which shall take place 90 days before the end of each term.
The General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council has publicly announced that the public has 15 days to apply.
According to the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council, from the date of notification until the application deadline of August 7, 2019, the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council has received one candidate, Mr. Plang Chhlam.
This morning, the Constitutional Council meeting elected Mr. Plang Chhlam as a member of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy for the second five-year term, with seven votes in favor of the total number of members of the Constitutional Council.
Mr. Plang Chhlam served as a sub-judge under the Siem Reap and Oddar Meanchey Provincial Courts from 1982 to 1984, Deputy Chief of the Siem Reap-Oddar Meanchey Provincial Court from 1984 to 1988, President of the Siem Reap-Oddar Meanchey Provincial Court from 1988 to 2005, and President of the Provincial Court. Kampong Cham from 2005 to 2010, President of Takeo Provincial Court from 2010 to 2014 and a member of the Supreme Council of Ang Chao Krom from 2014 to present.
Mr. Plang Chhlam graduated with a bachelor's degree in the second year of the Faculty of Law and Economics from 1973-1975, a degree equivalent in Bachelor of Public Administration, and a Master of Public Administration in 2005-2007.
It should be noted that the Supreme Council of the Magistracy was established to assist the King in ensuring the independence of the judiciary. The Supreme Council of the Magistracy has a decision and proposes to the King the appointment, transfer, removal, promotion and promotion of all judges and prosecutors.
Pursuant to the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy, signed by the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, on July 16, 2014, The Supreme Council of the Magistracy shall be under the presidency of the King and shall have 11 members.
The meeting came after the United States threatened to raise tariffs on more than $ 300 billion worth of Chinese goods, with the yuan depreciating by more than 7 yuan to the dollar. US (Thursday exchange rate), the lowest rate ever since April 2008, when the United States was entering a severe economic crisis.
The devaluation of the yuan has been blamed by the United States on Beijing, and the United States has already listed China as a "currency manipulator", leading to a trade war between the two countries. The two economic giants are entering a new serious level as the whole world watches with alarm, including Vietnam.
Vietnamese analysts see the situation as a risk for the Asean country as the depreciation of the yuan will hurt Vietnamese goods trying to export to the Chinese market, especially Vietnamese seafood. Commodities used to have great potential. On the other hand, cheap Chinese goods will easily flow back to Vietnam to compete with Vietnamese domestic goods.
A major Vietnamese seafood exporter, Cafatex, has expressed concern that Vietnamese exporters may lower their seafood prices to make it easier to export to the Chinese market. The sea in the overall market is falling at the same time.
Experts also warned that Vietnam could not allow its currency to fluctuate too much, as the United States could also adjust its currency to counter China. In addition, Vietnam was added to the US currency counterfeiting watch list in May.
