Mr. Ith Sam Heng encouraged the professors in the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia to continue their education and encourage the students to study hard in their fields, making this National Institute a leading institution in all fields. Technical and vocational training of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, including the capacity management system, trainers and quality of students and trainees.
The biggest reason that Mr. Ith Sam Heng appealed to the youth was because the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, has set out a strategy for the existence of human resources that have contributed to the development of the national economy. The need for human resources is really necessary, especially those who have this technical and professional skills.
In addition, Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that the Ministry of Labor will urge the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia (NPIC) to study and set up a laboratory and technology to install 5G internet in the near future. Nine Defective and Expired Goods Exhibited at Stong Market were Found and Confiscated by Kampong Thom CamControl Officials
(Kampong Thom): For the health of the people as well as food safety, Kampong Thom Provincial CamControl Officer on August 8, 2019, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce, local authorities and the Market Commission, continued to disseminate food quality, food safety and control food products. Nine out-of-date items were found in Stong Market, Kampong Chheu Teal Village, Kampong Chen Tbong Commune, Stong District, Kampong Thom Province.
Mr. Leang Sophea, Head of Kampong Thom CamControl Branch, said that the purpose of the inspection was to prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit labels, expiration dates and banned chemicals that could affect people's health.
According to a beverage vendor, CamControl officials said that the Coca-Cola orange juice, which was out of date, had only recently been put on sale by the company, as they were unaware that the company had falsified such inclusions.
CamControl officers then recorded the confiscation of the goods and stored them at the provincial branch for destruction, and put up posters showing the effects of food safety on the stalls and instructed other traders to understand and Adhere to the law on quality control, safety of products and services to avoid harm to health, people will be able to face the law.
