(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, inaugurated the new building of the ASEAN Secretariat in Jakarta, Indonesia on August 08, 2019.
The Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Indonesia, Retno Marsudi, has invited the Head of Mission of Cambodia to join the Foreign Ministers and other representatives of ASEAN Member States at the official inauguration of the new ASEAN Secretariat. The inauguration ceremony marks the 52nd anniversary of the founding of ASEAN.
On the occasion of the inauguration of the new building of the ASEAN Secretariat, a time box will be installed to keep the message of ASEAN leaders outlining the hopes and aspirations of ASEAN on the occasion of the anniversary. 75 years of the founding of ASEAN in 2042.
The inauguration of the new ASEAN Secretariat underscores the growing role of the ASEAN Secretariat and its leadership in responding to emerging global and regional challenges, as well as in building a pillar ASEAN community. Three: political-security community, economic community and socio-cultural community.
A powerful typhoon is expected to make landfall in Taiwan on Thursday, prompting Taiwanese authorities to warn people to be extra vigilant. This is according to the release by CNA on Thursday, August 08, 2019.
According to the Taiwan Meteorological Agency, Typhoon Lekima will make landfall near the northeastern coast of the island as it is moving at 15 kilometers per hour with a maximum wind speed of 227 kilometers per hour. An hour.
Taiwanese authorities have warned people in the northern region, including Taipei, to be extra vigilant. More than 1,500 people, mostly tourists in Taiwan's eastern islands, have been evacuated and troops have been deployed to rescue victims of the floods.
A magnitude 5.9 earthquake shook northeastern Taiwan on Thursday as Taiwan was preparing for a typhoon. The quake cut off electricity to more than 10,000 buildings and killed one person.
