Explanation: The fire is raining and why is it still out? The above was made on the occasion that Mr. Keo Rattanak was invited as a speaker in the press conference on "Questions related to electricity meters" organized by the spokesperson of the Royal Government on the morning of August 8, 2019.
He explained, "First, if the national road is widened by the Ministry of Public Works, the fire department must ask the electrician to remove the light pole and widen the road. The day at this time in this area, so please forgive the road widening.
The President of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) said that the power outage was not due to lack of electricity, but due to the need to widen the road.
"Secondly, due to the addition of electrical infrastructure, for example, we need to install a cabin or a high voltage substation that needs to cut the power line can work for 2 hours 3 hours, in this case, please inform because we know in advance as a work plan." . This is what Mr. Keo Rattanak said.
He continued that, but the plan is not known, suddenly a drunk car hit a light pole, a building, a light pole collapsed, a broken wind or an excavator excavator refused to ask for a law, refused to cooperate with Electricite du Cambodge, touched an underground power line on one side of the city. . He said this was not a power outage due to a lack of supply, but an impact on infrastructure.
At the same time, the President of Electricite du Cambodge, Mr. Keo Rattanak also confirmed that "the current electricity situation, we can use hydropower and full solar power without any problems."
Mr. Keo Rattanak said this on the morning of August 08, 2019, when he attended a press conference on "Questions related to electricity meters" organized by the Government Spokesperson Unit in the building. Land of the Office of the Council of Ministers. The purpose of this conference is to explain and respond to the concerns of the people who are focusing on issues related to electricity meters.
Mr. Keo Rattanak said that in fact, the price of electricity in Cambodia is not cheaper than Vietnam and Thailand, and not the same price due to different factors, in fact, Vietnam has already used a total of more than 40,000 megawatts. Cambodia already has only about 2,000 megawatts of electricity, so it is not possible to bring the price of electricity in a country with more than 40,000 megawatts to the same price as a country with only 2,000 megawatts.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that in the last few years, we have been trying to develop our hydropower plant in the demining forest, both development and protection, and when it is developed, there are still some opposition groups. Protested against the development of hydropower, but fortunately a large number of people support peace and development, we have done so much that has reduced the price of electricity.
The director general of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) added that Thailand has 40,000 megawatts of electricity, and has its own gas and gas to lower electricity prices. No two countries can have the same price of electricity, because each country has a different structure and different development and different favorable, so the price of electricity is also different. In terms of market size, consumption and resources are also local.
He added that the same thing applies with solar, and that Cambodia will have 15 percent solar consumption next year, and that it will also be the cheapest country in ASEAN. The price of solar in Laos is more than 8 cents per kilowatt hour, in Vietnam it is 9.35 cents, in Thailand it is more than 10 cents, while in Cambodia it is only 7.6 cents per kilowatt hour.
Regarding the question from the people who use electricity, they complained that there were power outages many times a day, but the electricity meters were used more than before, Mr. Keo Rattanak asked the question to think about when the power is not off, but Consumer counters are lower than before, why people do not wonder. He explained that the electricity meter problem is caused by three problems, including: weather problems, energy wastage and old electrical equipment problems.
As for the weather, Mr. Keo Rattanak said that this weather rate is very important, that is, the energy consumption in the dry season and the rainy season are different, as in Europe, in the cold and non-cold seasons also use different electricity. In general, the use of electricity in summer is more than the use in winter.
In addition, Mr. Keo Rattanak also explained the problem of old electrical equipment. He claims that according to world studies, the older the device, the more it consumes energy. He said that is why refrigerators, air conditioners, fans are encouraged to use new ones because the older the equipment, the lower the efficiency, and the more efficient it is, the more energy it consumes. Digitally in Cambodia
Dr. In Channy, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, said that once the exchange is completed, local banks and businesses will be highly protected against fraud and will no longer be the target of data theft and abuse. Also. By accepting Visa’s EMV chip, we will be able to strengthen our local operations and through our ATM network, which provides greater security in providing financial services nationwide.
Mr. Kim Ty Komly, First Deputy Technical Director of the National Bank of Cambodia, stated: “We commend Visa and the Banking Association of Cambodia for their cooperation in strengthening payment security in the country. Cambodia. "We are committed to promoting the future of cashless payments for Cambodia based on world-class payment infrastructure, and today's announcement is an important step in achieving this vision."
In addition to assisting local banks with strengthening their use of EMV chip standards, Visa continues to develop strategies designed to manage risk and innovation. It also involves measures to prevent fraud, protect customers from threats, and this partnership allows Visa to develop security systems that are guided by innovative technologies such as the EMV chip.
Visa, along with its financial institutions and business partners, regularly invests in the growth of digital payments in Cambodia, and this includes the production and use of additional education cards for consumers and businesses. On the benefits of electronic payments and the introduction of new payment-related innovations, such as payments via QR code scanning.
