After receiving a courtesy call from the King at the Royal Palace, the President and his wife will lead a delegation to lay flowers at the Independence Monument and pay their respects to His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk. The father of the Khmer nation "Preah Borom Ratanakoth" as well.
During the visit, the President will meet with His Majesty the King at the Royal Palace. The President will also hold bilateral meetings with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during which bilateral cooperation in various fields will be discussed to further strengthen friendly ties between the two countries. The two are deeply connected through Buddhism.
The two leaders will also exchange views on regional and international issues of common concern and interest. After the meeting, the President and the Prime Minister will witness the signing ceremony of a number of cooperation documents.
During his stay in Cambodia, the President of Sri Lanka will visit Wat Langka and present Samdech Preah Moha Areyvong Saturday Chanthol, the Chief Bishop of Wat Lanka, the son of the Po of Maha Bodhisattva from Anuradhapura. He will then attend a tree planting ceremony representing Sri Lanka at the Phnom Udong Vipassana Center, which received 10 gifts from the President.
Mr. Maitripala Srisena and members of the delegation will also visit the temples in Angkor Park in Siem Reap.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs emphasized that the current visit to Cambodia by President Maitripala Srisena will make a significant contribution to strengthening ties and expanding cooperation in the fields of economy, trade and culture between Cambodia and Cambodia. Sri Lanka.
Cambodia and Sri Lanka formally established diplomatic relations on May 18, 1952, but were severed in 1975. By August 6, 1996, diplomatic relations were re-established. Currently, Cambodia does not have an embassy in Sri Lanka, and Sri Lanka does not have an embassy in Cambodia.
Currently, trade relations between Cambodia and Sri Lanka are still small. The trade volume between the two countries in the first six years of 2018 was nearly 2 million dollars. Of that, Cambodia imported more than 1 million US dollars from Sri Lanka and exported more than 610,000 US dollars to Sri Lanka.
Cambodia received nearly 4,000 tourists from Sri Lanka in 2018. Sri Lanka has provided some assistance to Cambodia for education, and Cambodia has provided a total of about $ 200,000 to help flood victims in 2016 and 2017.
Kashmir dispute: Pakistan expels Indian diplomats, recalls ambassadors
ISLAMABAD: The Pakistani government has decided to expel a senior Indian diplomat and recall its ambassador to New Delhi in protest of India's withdrawal of autonomy from Kashmir. . This is according to the release by RT on Thursday, August 08, 2019.
The decision was made on Wednesday after a meeting of the Pakistan National Security Committee. The committee also decided to cut diplomatic ties as well as suspend trade with India as people in Kashmir fear an armed conflict between the two countries.
Indian-administered Kashmir has been closed since Monday after the New Delhi government lifted a special provision that gave some autonomy to the region. In addition, telephone and internet services have been cut off since Sunday evening, and hundreds of Indian troops have been deployed on the streets.
