Effective rescue operation rescues man in stone
Bora has been trapped in the rocks for several days, since August 4, only on August 7, when people and his family found him trapped in the rocks. Bora could be in danger if the rescue operation is delayed.
After finding Mr. Pora trapped in a rock, both the authorities and the police and the military police in the province sought to find a way to rescue the victim. However, due to the difficulty of the scene, the rescue was not effective.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, despite the busy schedule of organizing the Cambodia-Sri Lanka Business Forum with the President of Sri Lanka, also took part in the rescue operation. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, immediately assigned Senior Minister Kun Kim, the First Vice President of the National Committee for Management to address this issue.
Seeing that the rescue situation was difficult and the authorities and law enforcement forces in the province lacked the rescue equipment, Senior Minister Kun Kim immediately acted by transporting the rescue team from Unit 711 of the 70th Brigade, which specializes in rescue. From Phnom Penh by plane to the scene.
A team of 12 711 rescuers arrived at the scene and worked hard to rescue the victims from the cave. After the efforts of the rescue team and using various methods, finally, at around 6 pm, the victim was safely removed from the cave.
Both the family, the people and the rescue team expressed their excitement and joy when one person's life was saved. This rescue will not be successful without the prompt management of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the command of the rescue operation force carefully by Senior Minister Kun Kim at the scene and the cooperation of all You are not a rescuer.
The public highly appreciated this effective rescue operation. The public also expressed their appreciation and gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and all the rescue workers who worked hard to save Bora from danger to life.
(Kampot): Major General Mao Chanthurith, Kampot Provincial Police Commissioner, told Fresh News that as of 10:30 pm on August 7, 2019, the police had controlled the fire at Samaki Trapeang Ropov Market in Teuk Chhouk District. In Kampot province, the fire did not spread to nearby houses, but the entire Samaki Trapeang Ropov market was completely engulfed in flames.
The General Commissioner confirmed that until now, the police are continuing to put out this terrible fire until it is completely extinguished, and this firefighting operation uses 4 fire trucks, including 3 vehicles belonging to the Kampot Provincial Police Commissioner and 1 The other unit received cooperation from the fire truck of the Police Inspectorate of Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to local officials, more than 200 stalls in Samaki Trapeang Ropov market were completely destroyed by fire on the night of August 7. The cause of the fire and the extent of the damage are not yet known.
