The Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia organizes an international conference on "Cambodia and ASEAN Regionalism in the Indo-Pacific Context"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 08, 2019, the Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, in cooperation with the Konrad Adenauer Foundation in Cambodia, organized an international conference on "Cambodia and ASEAN Regionalism in the Indo-Pacific Context".
It should be reminded that Cambodia has been a member of ASEAN for 20 years. This membership has benefited Cambodia greatly in terms of economic opportunities, prestige and interests, as well as its international role through adherence to ASEAN norms and diplomacy. Cambodians now have more opportunities to learn and understand their neighbors.
In the past, Prime Minister Hun Sen has said, "As a small country, Cambodia cannot hope to live without connections to the outside world. "The growth and prosperity of all Cambodians depends on how we work with ASEAN to deepen regional integration, as well as strengthen the importance and resilience of the nation."
Dr. Kith Phea said that ASEAN seems to be becoming a strategic area facing competition from superpowers. The emergence of the Indo-Pacific has created some uncertainty in Southeast Asia, prompting ASEAN and its member states to rethink their strategic options and foreign policy.
