Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of attending the Cambodia-Sri Lanka Business Forum
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen extended a warm welcome to the presence of Sri Lankan President Mao Tri Pallasirisena on his state visit and a delegation of Sri Lankan businessmen and investors who accompanied him to study first-hand the progress of Sri Lanka. Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo stated that the Cambodia-Sri Lanka Business Forum provides an opportunity for Samdech to share information on important developments in Cambodia related to business and investment opportunities and potential, as well as the introduction of new measures of the current Royal Government of Cambodia. Improving the business and investment environment in Cambodia.
* The Prime Minister stated that Cambodia and Sri Lanka had established diplomatic relations more than six decades ago, in 1952, but that diplomatic ties had been temporarily suspended due to the Cambodian civil war since 1975.
* Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia-Sri Lanka officially re-established diplomatic relations on August 6, 1996, and the two countries' relations became more friendly through the exchange of visits of the leaders of our two countries.
* Samdech Techo stated that in 1979, when he was Minister of Foreign Affairs, he led a delegation to attend the Non-Aligned Movement meeting in Colombo, which was his first visit to Sri Lanka.
Samdech stated that the current visit of the Sri Lankan President shows the strengthening of relations between the two countries, especially in the fields of diplomacy, trade and tourism.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that to testify through this visit, tomorrow will be the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on Political Consultation between the Foreign Ministries of the two countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that over the last two decades, Cambodia has achieved an average annual economic growth of around 7.7% and has moved from being a low-income country to a middle-income country. Low in 2015. In 2018, the Cambodian economy will grow at a rate of 7.5%, which is the basis for continued strength in 2019.
* The Prime Minister stated that this indicator shows that Cambodia is on the path to achieve the status of a high middle-income country by 2030, as set in the national policy agenda.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that within the framework of investment, Cambodia is still a potential destination country for both local and foreign investors. In fact, according to the record of the Council for the Development of Cambodia for the past 5 years (2014-2018), the investment situation of Cambodia has improved, with Cambodia having approved 959 investment projects with a total investment of about 23 billion US dollars. Which can create 1 million jobs.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that the investment figures in the first half of 2019 were 153 investment projects approved with an investment capital of approximately 5.2 billion US dollars, compared to the same period in the first half of 2018 The number of projects increased by 48 while the investment capital increased by about 2 billion US dollars.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has introduced the Cambodia Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025, which is a new economic growth strategy aimed at diversifying the economy and restructuring Cambodia's industry from a labor-intensive industry to a skills-based industry. By 2025.
* Samdech Techo stated that the Royal Government considers the private sector as the engine of economic growth and a real partner in the development of the country.
* Samdech Techo confirmed that on March 29, 2019, Samdech led the Royal Government Forum. The 18th Private Sector, on that occasion, I set out a number of sharp measures aimed at 1) increasing the competitiveness of the Cambodian economy, 2) improving and further enhancing the investment and business environment, and 3) diversifying the national economy and creating jobs. More quality for the Cambodian people.
* Samdech Techo stated that these measures are currently being thoroughly implemented by the relevant ministries and institutions, and the Royal Government has established a clear mechanism for reviewing and monitoring the implementation of these measures to ensure the effectiveness of the decision. The above three goals.
* Samdech Techo welcomed the wise decisions of all foreign investors, especially Sri Lankan investors who wish to select Cambodia as a potential investment destination to start or expand their business.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also encouraged Cambodian investors who wish to expand their business abroad to consider Sri Lanka as their target country. Samdech Techo reminded that in recent years, Cambodia has always called for foreign investors to come to Cambodia, but in recent years, Cambodian investors have also gone out to invest in Laos, Myanmar, Timor-Leste and other countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen briefed Sri Lankan businessmen and investors on Cambodia's investment potential and key advantages over five areas, including:
Fourth, Cambodia is in a strategic position in the ASEAN region, which has been becoming a "factory of Asia". Cambodian-made goods can supply local markets, the Mekong sub-region, ASEAN markets and other major markets in the world.
Fifth, Cambodia has the potential for the development of "cultural and natural" tourism, including cultural treasures, natural resources, historical heritage, as well as beautiful scenery of beaches, rivers, lakes and national forests, which are attractive for both domestic and foreign tourism markets. And international.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that foreign investors receive the same benefits and protections as domestic investors and are able to invest 100% without the need for the participation of investors in the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that foreign investors in Cambodia are not only for the Cambodian market, but can distribute to other markets with a population of about 3 billion with ASEAN member countries and other trading partners such as China, India and other countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encouraged Sri Lankan investors who are here to hold further discussions with Cambodian businessmen and representatives of relevant ministries and institutions to learn about investment potential and opportunities in Cambodia and to make investment decisions in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo announced that on behalf of the Royal Government, Samdech guarantees to all investors all kinds of environment that favors and promotes investment, especially peace, security and political stability, as well as macroeconomic stability, legal framework and effective institutions. Transparency, accountability and predictability.
