The state visit, which is an important visit to strengthen cooperation between the two countries, is also part of the consideration for expanding trade volume, with both countries holding business forums to allow you to Businesses can meet to reach business cooperation with each other.
The establishment of the Cambodia-Sri Lanka Business Forum aims to boost the trade volume of the two countries, while the trade volume is still small, at about $ 4 million each.
According to official figures obtained by Fresh News from the Ministry of Commerce, in 2015, the trade volume between the two countries was more than 6 million dollars, of which Cambodia imported from Sri Lanka nearly 6 million dollars, while Cambodia exported to Sri Lanka has nearly $ 360,000.
In 2016, the trade volume increased to nearly 10 million dollars, of which Cambodia imported from Sri Lanka nearly 4 million dollars, while Cambodia exported to Sri Lanka more than 5 million dollars.
In 2017, the trade volume between the two countries dropped back to just nearly $ 5 million, of which Cambodia imported more than $ 4 million from Sri Lanka, while Cambodia exported to Sri Lanka only $ 570,000.
Meanwhile, in 2018, the trade volume of the two countries continued to decline to only nearly 4 million dollars, of which Cambodia imported from Sri Lanka nearly 3 million dollars and Cambodia exported to Sri Lanka nearly 1 million dollars.
