Philippines declares nationwide dengue outbreak as 'alarming' increase
MANILA: Dengue cases and deaths continue to rise alarmingly in the Philippines, prompting the Philippine Ministry of Health on Tuesday to announce a nationwide dengue outbreak. According to Xinhua reported on the night of August 6.
From January to July 20 this year, the Philippine Ministry of Health detected about 146,000 cases of dengue fever nationwide, up 98 percent from the same period in 2018. The outbreak killed 622 people.
Dengue cases in the Philippines are observed to erupt every three to four years. The previous major eruption occurred in 2016.
