(Phnom Penh): The spokesman for the Office of the Council of Ministers, Mr. Ek Tha, said that reducing the holiday from 28 days to 22 days for 2020 will make Cambodia more attractive to national and international investors to contribute to the construction. And develop the country to become more dynamic.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has recently decided to reduce the number of public holidays by six days, from 28 days to 22 days per year, from 2020 onwards.
In 2020, the Royal Birthday of the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, was reduced to two days, with only one day left.
Five other national and international festivals will not be allowed to be closed from 2020, including: Meak Bochea, National Day of Remembrance, International Children's Day, and the anniversary of the Urban Peace Agreement. Paris and Human Rights Day, December 10.
Separately, the holiday for Khmer New Year, which has been 3 days ago, has been added 1 day to make it 4 days.
