(Central): Traffic accidents are a major obstacle that destroys the national budget of more than $ 300 million per year. This was confirmed by Mr. Moeung Yuleng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province on the occasion of his visit to educate and disseminate the road traffic law and provide helmets to motorcyclists on the morning of August 6, 2019.
Mr. Ming Yuleng said that in 2018, the number of deaths due to traffic accidents in Cambodia was 1,761, an average of 5 people per day, caused by negligence in driving vehicles on public roads, cleaner roads. The danger is increasing.
"In Kandal province, the number of traffic accidents in July 2019 has increased five times, killing 12 people, including three women, with serious injuries and several minor injuries," he said.
He added that most of the victims were motorcyclists who did not have a clear understanding of the vehicle, did not know the traffic signs placed on the road, careless driving, especially not wearing a helmet.
