This is the third census in the history of Cambodia, which is usually conducted every 10 years to obtain specific demographic data for use in the formulation of appropriate policies and to serve as an indicator in monitoring national strategic development plans. And Cambodia's Sustainable Development Goals 2016-2030, leaving no one alone.
The Cambodian government considers the census very important and the only source that can provide complete and accurate data as well as characterize the actual living conditions of people across the country.
The Cambodian census gives us accurate data on the country's demographics and helps the government to formulate policies and implement programs to balance development for people across the country.
