General Department of CamControl, Ministry of Commerce Holds a Training Workshop on "Competition Law and the Basics of the Cambodian Legal System"
The purpose of the draft competition law is to encourage fair and honest business relations, increase economic efficiency, encourage the creation of new businesses, protect the national economy from the effects of competition activities, violate the law and help consumers get High quality goods and services, low prices, rich and wide selection.
The Deputy Director General said that the competition law will solve issues related to business conspiracy, pricing, quantity of goods for sale, geographical location for sale of products and services, arbitrary use of business power by market power, and Prevent business mergers that undermine the competitive process and can lead to monopolies.
Cambodia has prepared its competition law with great care and caution, as in the process of drafting, the Ministry of Commerce has consulted several times with stakeholders and with the participation of experts. Many internationals, too.
The Deputy Director General added, "The purpose of today's training workshop is to raise awareness of the importance of fair competition in doing business as well as strengthen the legal knowledge of the officers of the General Department of CamControl. "Furthermore, in the future, they will have to become judicial police officers to enforce this competitive law more effectively."
Mr. Kim Meas Sok Seiha announced the opening of the training workshop and instructed all participants to make efforts to receive new knowledge from international experts and national trainers for the purpose of additional wisdom for self-development as well as for Strengthen the implementation of the competition law of the institution in the future.
Murder! Angry wife filed for divorce, husband abducted on the street and died in Kratie City
(Kratie): A murder case occurred when a husband cut his wife to death and escaped, but the police are arresting. The murder happened on the night of August 5 in Orussey 2 village, Orussey commune, Kratie city.
According to the Orussey Sangkat Police Station, the victim was Kong Srey Touch, 27 years old, and the assailant was Sam Sopheaktra, a resident of the above-mentioned village-commune.
According to local police officers, the victim and the victim had a dispute until the victim decided to file for divorce, but the perpetrator did not agree. On the day of the incident, at more than 7 pm, the victim was riding a motorbike to buy sweets when he returned home at the entrance of the house. The neck was dropped into a sewer, causing a sudden death.
After cutting his wife, the assailant escaped. Currently, law enforcement forces are looking to arrest the suspects to deal with legal procedures.
