National Road Safety Committee Holds Press Conference on Working Together to Save Lives
(Phnom Penh): The General Secretariat of the National Road Safety Committee, the Road Safety Network in Cambodia, co-chaired by the Asia Injury Prevention Foundation and the Coalition for Road Safety, organized a press conference on "Working Together for "Life-saving: Measures that could save more lives now and during the next decade."
The conference aims to create opportunities for meetings of policy makers and implementers of government institutions, stakeholders on road safety, as well as private sector advocates, the media, civil society organizations and NGO networks. Various to exchange knowledge, information and experiences.
The conference discussed practical strategies and actions to contribute to accelerating progress towards achieving the life-saving goals that Cambodia is committed to supporting the United Nations Road Safety Decade 2011-2020 and its goals. Sustainable Development (SDG).
The conference also aims to promote discussions on preparations for road safety activities during the next decade (2021-2030).
The Asia Injury Prevention Foundation Asia The Injury Prevention Foundation Asia is a non-profit, non-profit organization with a strong commitment to preventing traffic accidents and deaths in high-income countries. Low and medium.
