About 10,000 pieces of Shiva dance statues have been reassembled
(Siem Reap): The statue of Shiva (Indra, Preah Iso Preah Hari), which is in a state of disrepair, about 10,000 pieces, is currently being examined by experts from the Angkor Conservation in collaboration with the National Authority of Preah Vihear, Apsara Authority, National Museum, Phnom Penh and French School. The Far East opens a remodel to its original form.
The original form of the broken Shiva statue above is a dance gesture, about 5 meters high, with a double head, 5 faces, 10 hands. This statue of the deity originated from Prasat Krahorm in the archipelago of Koh Kerna in the 10th century AD.
The devastation of tens of thousands of pieces of this deity was caused by the natural factors of age, the chaos of the civil war, and some unscrupulous merchants took advantage of the unhealthy countryside, cut off their heads, traded and smashed their bodies. Which is broken to pieces.
In 2012, the French School of the Far East, in collaboration with the National Authority of Preah Vihear, the Apsara Authority and the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, conducted a joint excavation to collect fragments of Shiva dancing from the destruction of some of the soil and piles of soil mixed with Some of the bricks were kept at the Norodom Sihanouk-Angkor Museum, but due to the difficulty of repairing them, they were transferred back to the Angkor Preservation.
During the renovation, five pieces of hand and two faces were taken from the National Museum of Phnom Penh, which the French kept in 1960 to reassemble them.
Regarding the renovation process, Mr. Chan Chamroeun, Deputy Director of the Department of Protection and Preservation of Ancient Buildings of the Ministry of Culture, said that so far, the repair and assembly of Shivaram statues has been going on for more than two months. As a result, the team assembled the chest, some of the brittle stone treatment, as well as other parts. Three more faces were lost, and the team is considering how much new batteries should be added to fill in the gaps.
This expert is determined that no matter how difficult it is, he will fulfill this task and request that all Cambodian children work together to protect and understand our jewels without relying on experts. One face.
As for the efforts to assemble the statue of Lord Shiva in such a state of ruin, because he wanted to preserve what is ancient and the works and techniques of Khmer ancestors from the 10th century AD that are invaluable for the next generation of researchers. Saw.
