Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: 13 days of the campaign to wear helmets, the death rate in traffic accidents while driving a bicycle has decreased
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, said on August 5, 2019 that during the 13 days of the helmet-wearing campaign, the death toll in traffic accidents using bicycles was A decrease of 9 people, including 5 people who did not wear a helmet, compared to 13 days before the campaign.
In anticipation of the death toll, Prince Sar Kheng continues to call on all citizens to implement the road traffic law consistently with a high vigilance to protect the safety and lives of families and all road users.
"Dear compatriots! Once again, today, Your Majesty, I would like to express my appreciation and appreciation for the results of the nationwide campaign to restrict the use of helmets by motorcyclists across the country, which has reduced the death rate.
According to a report on the results of the 13-day helmet tightening campaign (July 19-31, 2019), the death toll for motorcyclists has dropped by nine, including nine. The number of people not wearing helmets decreased by 5 compared to 13 days before the campaign.
I would also like to thank all the people who participated in respecting and implementing the land traffic law vigorously, with ownership and a high alert to maintain safety on the road in accordance with the law.
Although the implementation of the temporary helmet restriction campaign has yielded positive results, the death toll remains high and the number of injuries continues to rise with no signs of abating.
On behalf of the President of the National Road Safety Committee, I, Your Majesty, would like to call on all citizens to implement the Road Traffic Law consistently with a high awareness to protect the safety and lives of families and road users. Everyone.
I wish all my compatriots happiness and prosperity in all things. "
