This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen handed over diplomas and certificates to more than 1,000 police
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, August 5, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the awarding ceremony of Police Science Degree at the Bachelor of Science Degree. And certificates to 1,465 student police officers and trainees at the Police Academy of Cambodia.
Students and trainees are police officers who will receive diplomas and certificates today, including: 180 master's degree students, 7 females, 319 bachelor degrees, 40 females, 966 certificate trainees, 55 females.
It should be noted that the Police Academy of Cambodia is an institution under the Ministry of Interior that has been active in training police and prison officers to improve the quality and professional capacity of national police officers and prison officers throughout the country in accordance with the needs of society and Defined quality standards.
From 2007 to the first half of 2019, a total of 44,920 police officers, trainees and police students graduated from the Police Academy of Cambodia, including 2,441 women.
The report shows that, on average, the Police Academy of Cambodia trains nearly 4,000 long-term and short-term national police forces and prison officers each year. From 2007 to the first half of 2019, a total of 14,491 students, including 1 female, graduated from the first part of the new professional police force and police officers graduated from the six regional police schools. , 778 people.
The Prime Minister's strict order was issued on the occasion of handing over diplomas and certificates to more than 1,000 police officers at the Police Academy of Cambodia in Dei Edth Commune, Kien Svay District, Kandal Province on the morning of August 5. 2019.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in addition to the study of public order, security, border police, immigration, identification, management and command of prison management, information technology and foreign languages should also be examined more closely, "What other skills? Which needs to be included in the additional training curriculum for the National Police trainees in this Cambodian Police Academy. ”
There are a number of points that Samdech Techo wants more training, such as terrorism, war, sectarian conflict, etc. He expressed concern about the security situation in the world, which is still under threat recently. There have been shootings in Texas, Ohio, in the United States, in New Zealand, in Sri Lanka, and many people have been killed and injured.
The Prime Minister stressed that all these issues should be considered carefully if there are any other points that can be included in the training curriculum for the National Police Force.
Another important point that Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants to include in the curriculum for the National Police is that the experience gained from the relationship between Cambodia and the international community within the framework of the Ministry of Interior, the National Police and the Armed Forces should also be documented. For training of National Police trainees as well.
All these important points were introduced by Samdech Techo Prime Minister to General Seng Phally, as the President of the Police Academy of Cambodia, should prepare a comprehensive document to be included in the training program for police officers outside the field of study. At present.
