(Phnom Penh): At the Mekong Cooperation Meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, stated that Cambodia has benefited from a number of activities under the Lower Mekong Initiative. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which was received by Fresh News on August 5.
The press release on the 12th Lower Mekong Initiative (LMI) Foreign Ministers' Meeting as part of the Mekong Cooperation Meeting was held on 1-3 August 2019 in Bangkok. The meeting welcomed the ongoing progress of the Mekong Water Data Initiative, including the launch of a data center and "Mekong Water" in order to strengthen the coordination role of the Mekong River Commission.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated: "Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon has stated that Cambodia has benefited from the many activities under this initiative and is pleased to co-chair with the United States. Meeting on "Human Development and Pillar Connections" on the occasion of the first LMI Political Dialogue in April in Bangkok. He also welcomed the establishment of LMI's public benefit program.
The 10th Meeting of the Ministers of Foreign Affairs of the Mekong-Gangetic Cooperation (MGC) has the following results:
The meeting approved the MGC Action Plan 2019-2022 and the Joint Declaration of the 10th Meeting of the Ministers of Foreign Affairs of the Mekong-Mekong Cooperation. The meeting also agreed that Cambodia should co-chair the Mekong-Mekong Cooperation in 2020, the year of the 20th anniversary of the Mekong-Mekong Cooperation.
In particular, the 9th Mekong-Republic of Korea Foreign Ministers' Meeting has the following results:
The meeting agreed to hold the first Mekong-ROK Summit on November 27, 2019 in Busan, coinciding with the ASEAN-ROK Dialogue Summit. Held the 7th Mekong-Republic of Korea Business Forum in September 2019 in Thailand. The meeting approved the 9th Joint Statement of the 9th Mekong-ROK Foreign Ministers' Meeting.
In addition, the 12th Mekong-Japan Foreign Ministers' Meeting had the following results:
The meeting decided to adopt the Mekong-Japan Cooperation Initiative for Sustainable Development 2030 to be adopted at the Mekong-Japan Cooperation Summit to be held in November 2019 in Bangkok, Thailand. Priority areas under the initiative will cover environmental and urban issues, agriculture and the environment.
