For this week, we will cover the topic of "Copyright (Part 2)", which explains the scope of rights, conditions and procedures for legal protection on copyright as follows:
Authors receive exclusive rights to the work. This right is recognized by national law. There are two types of copyright: heritage rights and moral rights.
1. Heritage rights
Inheritance rights are the author's right to conduct business on his own works through reproduction, publicity, and reproduction. Authors have the exclusive right to do it themselves or allow them to do the following:
2. Moral rights
The author's moral rights are as follows:
The Law on Authors establishes a number of conditions for the work that has already been created to be protected by law, or in other words, to be able to create rights for those who strive to create the work. In the intellectual property system of Cambodia, copyrighted works are automatically protected, meaning that works can be protected through copyright, whether registered or unregistered.
That is, registration to protect the work of the author is the right of the author, not a legal obligation like other intellectual property. However, in case the author or copyright holder wants to register for protection of his / her work, he / she must apply for registration of the copyrighted work at the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts.
A. Original conditions of the author's work
Works that can be protected by copyright must meet the "original works" condition. An original work is a work that was created based on the personal wisdom of the author of that work. Original works are works that are not copied from third-party works.
However, the originality of a work does not require that a work be absolutely new or the original creation of a work, meaning that a new work, even if it is identical or similar to a previous work, must not be completely copied. Previous works can be protected through copyright. Originality may also vary depending on the nature of an author's use of ideas to create a work.
B. Legal conditions of the work
The author's work that can be protected must be of the type specified in the copyright law. This law defines the types of works that can be protected and non-protected in Cambodia. In addition, copyright law provides protection for works created in Cambodia and abroad, subject to other special conditions.
Works to be made in Cambodia are works created in accordance with the laws of Cambodia by a person of Khmer nationality or by a foreigner residing in Cambodia or by a legal entity with a registered location. Law in Cambodia.
Works created abroad by Cambodians or foreigners are considered foreign works and are not subject to the laws of Cambodia. However, this foreign work will also receive legal protection in Cambodia if it is first published in Cambodia or is published within 30 days in Cambodia from the date of publication. For the first time in the country of origin.
Although the author is given the right to defend his work through the law, the law also provides for restrictions on copyright, which the author can not prohibit:
A. Private performances, free of charge, are performed with family or friends. Arranging in the library any manuscript for preservation or for research. Use of works for unpaid study d. Translation of works from Khmer into ethnic languages or translation from ethnic languages into Khmer.
IV. Period of protection of heritage rights:
Heritage rights are protected from the date of creation. This period of protection shall last for the life of the author as well as 50 years after the date of the author's death. The protection of heritage rights on collaborative works takes place throughout the life of the last living author, as well as 50 (fifty) years after the last author's death. (Article 30)
Inheritance rights over a work published as an anonymous or a pseudonym shall be protected by this law for 75 years from the end of the calendar year of the year in which it was first published. Permission from the owner. (Article 31, paragraph 1)
Inheritance rights over collective works or audiovisual works or past works shall be protected for a period of 75 years from the end of the calendar year of the year in which they were first legally published. (Article 31, paragraph 4)
In general, all works are automatically protected by copyright and related rights. Authors or owners can submit works to the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts. On the other hand, this law recognizes the person who creates the cultural work and that person has the exclusive right to the work and guarantees the benefit whenever someone else does business on the work.
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, confirmed that there is no African swine fever in Kampong Cham Province.
The provincial governor confirmed this while celebrating my school, my future on the morning of August 4, 2019 in the camp of Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province.
The provincial governor said that recently, after the media reports about African swine fever, people in Kampong Cham province were so scared that they did not dare to eat pork.
According to the provincial governor, after the incident, the Kampong Cham provincial authorities launched a large-scale campaign with veterinary officers of the Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to inspect the health of pigs in some pig farms in the province and animals. Pigs transported through Kampong Cham province, that is, professional officers properly inspected and even sprayed pesticides on the trucks.
The provincial governor confirmed that if any pigs were found to be suspected of having the disease, the authorities would immediately detain them and not allow them to transport pigs through Kampong Cham province. So people should not be afraid of this African swine fever and turn to eating pork together. In addition, this is the spawning season, fishing is banned, so if you do not eat pork, chicken and beef may go up in price.
The governor said the African swine fever was contagious and could not be transmitted to humans. At the end of my school program, my future, I also organized a bread party with pork.
