A police officer was accused of threatening a neighbor with a gun in Kampong Cham City, but relatives came out and denied it, claiming it was a misunderstanding
(Phnom Penh): A competent police officer working for the Ministry of Interior is accused of threatening a neighbor with a gun due to a minor dispute in Sangkat Kampong Cham, Kampong Cham City, Kampong Cham Province, but his wife and relatives came out. He categorically denied the allegations and argued that the incident was just a misunderstanding.
Ms. An Thida claims that the accusation by Ms. Tat Sineth that her husband used a gun to threaten in a minor dispute is an exaggeration because her husband does not have a gun in the house.
The wife of the police officer confirmed that the dispute started from the construction of the wall of the house, with her family asking the side of Ms. Tat Sineth, who lives next door, to build the wall of the house, and she agreed to build the wall next to the house. On the other hand, Ms. Tan Sineth refused to build and forbade the construction to touch the walls of her house.
The wife of the police claimed that the complaint was exaggerated and that Tat Sineth was not a widow. She considers that filing a complaint over and over again is a disgrace to her family, so her family came forward to explain the truth and want to end the conflict between the two parties.
At the same time, Ms. An Thida also called on the public and the media not to be confused, and for some media outlets that have published in the past, which quoted only the words of one party to publish completely wrong.
