(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Prak Poly, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Banteay Meanchey Province, stated that he did not oppose the Royal Government's sub-decree not to cut land for the people, as advertised on some media and social media.
Mr. Prak Poly's statement came after some media outlets and social media outlets reported that he had opposed the Royal Government's sub-decree not to cut land for the people as instructed by the Royal Government.
On March 27, 2018, the Royal Government of Cambodia issued a sub-decree to cut an area of 20 meters by 56 meters west of O'Chrov Thmey Primary School from the inventory of assets of O'Chrov Thmey Primary School and reclassify it as private land. The state for the gift belongs to 5 families in Kbal Spean 1 village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
But so far, the land has not been given to the five families yet, leading to accusations that Mr. Prak Poly refused to comply with the sub-decree.
Mr. Prak Poly told the media on August 4, 2019 that he did not oppose the Royal Government's sub-decree. The reason for not cutting the land for the five families is because the five families went to point out the land differently from when the sub-decree was issued.
The Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Banteay Meanchey Province said that due to the land in the sub-decree and the location of the land that the five families point to is different, he has not yet decided to cut to the people and made a letter. Decided by the Ministry. So far, the ministry has not decided yet.
Mr. Prak Poly asked for understanding from the five families.
