For example, on Sunday, July 7, Iran publicly announced that it would increase uranium enrichment to more than 3.6 percent in the short term, a level restricted under the Iran Nuclear Agreement. 2015.
This time, through Zarif, Iran announced that "the third step in reducing the commitment to the nuclear deal will be implemented in the current situation." "If this agreement is not implemented by others, we will not be able to implement it 100 percent, and of course all our actions in the past are within the framework of the agreement," he added. Agree this. ”
US President Donald Trump pulled the United States out of the 2015 Iran nuclear deal in May 2018 to reopen sanctions on Iran. But other signatories, including Britain, France, China, Germany and Russia, have stated they will not withdraw from the deal, while Tehran has warned that if the nuclear deal is destroyed it could endanger the world. Round.
