Spokesman Jin Malin: Kep Provincial Court may be established in 2020 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Chin Malin, Spokesman of the Ministry of Justice on August 3, 2019, confirmed that the Kep Provincial Court may Must be established in 2020 if the financial project, human resources and some legal standards are going well as planned by the Ministry.
In an interview with Fresh News, Mr. Chin Malin said that the Ministry of Justice is preparing financial projects, human resources such as judges, prosecutors and administrative officials, and if both projects go smoothly, Kep Provincial Court may To be established in early 2020. Regarding legal norms, he said that the establishment of the court of any province must be done as stated in the law on the establishment of the judiciary.
According to a senior official of the Ministry of Justice, he confirmed in a conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit, stating that in Cambodia today we have 24 courts throughout the capital-province. Separately, Kep province does not have a court yet and cases have been sent to the Kampot Provincial Court.
Please note that in Cambodia today, there is only one Court of Appeal, the Court of Appeal of Phnom Penh, which handles all cases that are sent from all capitals and provinces. As of 2019, the Ministry of Justice has trained nine human resources, with a total of nearly 500 judges and prosecutors on duty across the country.
