Cardiac Surgery Room, Kantha Bopha Sihamoni-Monineath Hospital Building, Succeeded for the First Time in Surgery for Girls with Congenital Open Heart Disease
(Phnom Penh): On August 2, 2019, this is the first day of the operation of the operating room of Kantha Bopha-Sihamoni Monineath building of the new Kantha Bopha 1 Hospital. Doctors successfully operated on the first 11-year-old girl. People with congenital heart disease and all treatments are free for everyone.
In this successful operation, the family, relatives and all the doctors would like to thank His Majesty the Prince of Life on the Stone, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia and Queen Monineath. Sihanouk is the most revered deity.
Please be informed that the operating room of Kantha Bopha Sihamoni-Monineath Building of Kantha Bopha Hospital was inaugurated under the presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia and Queen Monineath Sihanouk on the morning of the 1st. August 2019 yesterday.
On that occasion, the King said that in 2018, Samdech Mey and His Majesty the King donated 1 million US dollars for the construction of a surgical building, which was inaugurated today. On this occasion, Samdech Mey and His Majesty also agreed to donate an additional 200,000 USD to the Kantha Bopha Hospital Foundation.
The first cardiac surgery room in Phnom Penh of Kantha Bopha-Sihamoni Monineath will be operational from August 2, 2019, which can increase the number of surgeries by about 1,000 per year together with the first cardiac surgery center. Has been operating at Jayavarman VII Hospital in Siem Reap since 2011.
With our team of Cambodian specialists with 8 years of experience, we hope that this Second Heart Center will be able to meet the needs of treating more than 4,000 young children with congenital heart disease who are awaiting surgery. Corrected every year, more than 80 percent of these cases, they will be able to live like a normal child after successful surgery.
