Mr. Samleang Try pointed out that in order to repair the red gravel road damaged by the flood for the people to cross temporarily, the professional officer dug a drainage road by installing 6 bicycles temporarily and Pour rocks, pour soil, grind and compact to make people travel first. The construction of this road in accordance with the technical standards of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, we will prepare in the dry season.
Japan Provides Over $ 300,000 to Cambodian Civil Society for Education Promotion Project in Kandal Province
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, has provided US $ 310,777 to the Association for Relief and Rescue of Japan (AAR Japan) under a grant scheme for a Japanese NGO project. On the project to improve environmental education in Kandal province.
In this project, AAA Japan will establish a system to evaluate the implementation of environmental education and implement activities to support the capacity building of the Disability Support Committee at the commune administration level. Through this project, the learning environment and quality of education for children with disabilities will be improved.
The Japan NGO Grant Program has been in Cambodia since 2002 to support the activities of Japanese NGOs in their efforts to support the development and reconstruction of Cambodia at the grassroots level.
Since 2002, the Japanese government has provided more than $ 36 million for 118 projects focusing on basic education, health, agriculture and demining activities in Cambodia.
