(Takeo): On the afternoon of August 2, 2019, Takeo Provincial Authority organized a pork eating ceremony in front of Takeo Market under the theme "Safe Pork Eating Program in Takeo Province" in the presence and led by Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor and Officials around the province, along with residents and traders selling pork in Takeo market.
Mr. Ouch Phea said that after the outbreak of African swine fever came to Cambodia, especially in Ampil village, Ponley commune, Ang Borei district, Takeo province, people in the country as well as in Takeo province stopped eating pork and buying Pork in the market to eat for fear of this disease.
The governor of Takeo province continued, "The African swine fever epidemic is not contagious to humans, only to pigs." Therefore, people in Takeo province should eat pork normally because it is not contagious to humans. "On the other hand, re-eating pork to encourage local farmers and pork traders."
Mr. Ouch Phea added that the pork sold in the market must be inspected by the provincial veterinarian before being allowed to be exported to other markets, so please do not worry. However, the pork sold as a shelter is sick, veterinary officials have examined very carefully.
