Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Continues Inspection of Chicken Nest Road in the City
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, accompanied by the Provincial Public Works Officer, inspected the process of clearing the chicken nest road in Kampong Cham City. Meanwhile, the Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Cham Province said on the afternoon of August 2, 2019 that the removal of chicken nests in the city throughout Kampong Cham can be completed in two weeks.
Director of the Department of Public Works, Mr. Sok Srun, said that last year, the maintenance of special roads, chicken nests on the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport used funds from the Ministry of Public Works. However, in 2018, the Ministry of Public Works did not have the budget to provide, so the provincial public works department did not have the budget to use in the campaign to clear the chicken nest road.
However, after Mr. Un Chanda took office, he instructed the Department of Public Works to launch a campaign to clear chicken nests in the city throughout Kampong Cham province, and this operation was funded by the Kampong Cham Provincial Hall.
Mr. Sakh Srun confirmed that the removal of chicken nests in the city throughout Kampong Cham province started the campaign on July 22, 2019, which so far has achieved about 50 percent. The campaign will also be completed in the next two weeks.
