Senior Ministry of Labor official: Union law ensures harmony in industrial relations, promotes freedom of association
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Vannak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, affirmed that after the entry into force of the Law on Trade Unions, it has made a significant contribution to ensuring harmony in industrial relations and contributing to the promotion of freedom of association. .
The Secretary of State made the remarks at the opening of the second National Tripartite Consultation Workshop on the Draft Amendments to the Law on Trade Unions on the morning of August 2, 2019 at the Sunway Hotel.
Mr. Mam Vannak pointed out that the number of unions registered with the Ministry of Labor is increasing every year at all levels, including local unions, federations, unions and trade unions. In fact, as of the first half of 2019, there are 5,045 professional organizations registered with the Ministry of Labor, of which 4,811 local unions, 195 trade unions, 29 unions, and 10 employers' associations.
In addition, the number of collective labor disputes and strikes has also declined significantly due to the effectiveness of the implementation of trade union law and the strengthening of the labor inspection system.
Mr. Mam Vannak said that along with these progresses, there are still some unions and international institutions that do not have a clear understanding of the content of the provisions of the Law on Trade Unions, continuing to raise some concerns in the registration of unions and certification. The most representative of the union.
The Secretary of State further stated that this draft amendment is a draft that was revised by the Legal Technical Working Group of the Ministry of Labor after receiving input from stakeholders in the tripartite workshop on April 25, 2019. And some comments sent by relevant parties to the Ministry through official written letters.
These are the results of the input provided by all stakeholders to the Ministry as a basis for the Ministry to consider, weigh and verify all aspects of this draft amendment for submission to all participants for further review. This.
The Law on Trade Unions is a legal framework that aims to 1-Protect the rights and legitimate interests of workers 2-Ensure the right to freedom of collective bargaining between workers and employers 3-Promote harmony in academic relations Bio and 4- Contribute to the development of decent work, increase productivity and investment.
