Authorities cut down and burn many marijuana trees that people illegally planted in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): Many marijuana trees that people illegally planted were confiscated by the police force of Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province and burned on the spot.
Lt. Col. Rith Sona, Tbeng Meanchey District Police Inspector, told Fresh News on August 1, 2019 that by following the instructions of Major General Sous Sok Dara, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner, Tbeng Meanchey District Police Force cooperated with The Pramer Administration Police Station inspected and burned some fresh marijuana trees that farmers were secretly planting.
