General Department of Taxation and Administration of Preah Sihanouk Province held a meeting on strengthening tax collection management, in the first 6 months of this year, Preah Sihanouk Province collected 104% of tax revenue!
(Preah Sihanouk): The General Department of Taxation and Administration of Preah Sihanouk Province this afternoon, August 1, 2019, held a meeting on strengthening tax collection management in Preah Sihanouk Province under the chairmanship of Mr. Kong Vibol, Royal Government Delegate in charge. Director General of the General Department of Taxation and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to the results of tax revenue collection of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Tax Branch, as of the first 6 months of 2019, the results of tax collection in Preah Sihanouk Province reached 104% of the legal plan, which is the result.
This result has been applauded and appreciated by the provincial governor and the Royal Government delegates, in which the most significant type of income is the stamp duty on the transfer of ownership and ownership of real estate.
The meeting focused on strengthening tax collection management in Sihanoukville by examining the potential of tax revenue management, although the current tax revenue has increased significantly, but does not reflect In line with the growth of economic activity in the province, the tax collection has not yet reached its full potential.
It should also be noted that taxes are an important source of development, especially development in Sihanoukville is dependent on the sub-national budget.
In the past, the General Department of Taxation has observed that there are still problems in promoting the registration of taxes on rents and land, noting that the contract seems to have been made for the purpose of declaring tax at a lower rent than the actual price, and some properties are required. Rented several generations:
* Updating and registering real estate, which aims to strengthen the provision of services and make it easier for people to pay property taxes * Tax registration by the business owner does not clearly understand the tax obligations * Risk of loss of income Taxes from businesses that take refuge under the casino brand and strengthen the management of tax collection on the construction sector.
On the contrary, the General Department of Taxation will take strict legal measures against tax evasion and obstruction of tax regulations and take action on tax offenses on enterprises with high risk of tax revenue, which makes business competition unequal. Weak tax system and affect economic growth through cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions as a precautionary measure to revoke licenses.
The Royal Government delegates highly appreciated and thanked the leaders and tax officials at all levels, as well as local officials at all levels who have been actively involved in efforts to collect revenue to achieve results. Better.
