Indigenous peoples have a history closely related to the ancient Khmer government.
(Siem Reap): According to the presentation of Professor Ang Chulan, an anthropologist based on historical, literary and anthropological evidence, indigenous peoples have a deep history with ancient Khmer government.
He mentioned in a lecture on "Indigenous Peoples in the History of Cambodia" organized on July 30 by the Angkor Training Center and more than 300 participants.
Given the above evidence, indigenous peoples are closely related to the government, customs, traditions, culture and ancient Khmer society. These relationships can be seen in the various ceremonies organized in daily life from birth to death.
Mr. Ang Chulan explained that it is difficult to determine the number of indigenous peoples in Cambodia, both ancient and modern, because it needs to be studied and it is the work of linguists because some languages are lost. Gradually.
There is one ethnic group that Aung Chulan mentioned and seems to have a strong connection to the ancient Khmer government, the Kuy people. This ethnic group is most prominent because the French period has a lot of documents about this ethnic group. France exalted this nation with its skillful and skilled metalworking skills.
Although there is evidence that the Kui are good at steelmaking, Professor Ang Chulan states that it is not that Cambodians are ignorant. If you do not know, how can you build such a wonderful Angkor Wat? Mr. Ang Chulan only raised his personal suspicion that the Kuay people may have played a part in the ancient Khmer government in terms of weapons, military parts and so on. However, Ang Chulan stated that this is a topic that researchers need to study further to be 100 percent clear.
