(Phnom Penh): Only one month left is the one-year anniversary of the Royal Government of the sixth mandate, which was established on September 6, 2018, after the election was transparent, fair and just, and more people went to the polls. 83% of the total registered voters
It is observed that after the election of the sixth mandate, the Royal Government was formed smoothly under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, despite the absence of the former CNRP. This situation seems to be in stark contrast to the situation after the 2013 election in which the former opposition party participated.
After the election was over and the new locomotive was formed, a number of achievements emerged under the shadow of the CPP-led peace process after a landslide victory in the election. Elections.
In fact, on the morning of August 1, 2019, the Spokesperson Unit of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by Mr. Phay Siphan organized a press conference on "Achievements one year after the election" with the participation of Mr. Phay Siphan and Mr. Chin Malin. Spokesperson of the Ministry of Justice. This conference aims to show the public the achievements of the Royal Government of the sixth mandate in the past year.
Through this conference, Mr. Phay Siphan also emphasized that after this one year election, Cambodia has achieved great success by maintaining peace, maintaining political stability and maintaining real economic growth, gross domestic product (GDP) is growing within 7 percent per year, which is a good number.
Mr. Phay Siphan also presented the work of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, which emerged from the election for the past six months, as he went abroad to work as well as finding 18 business partners. Lift. Of these 18 visits, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has participated in major forums such as the United Nations.
In terms of investment, in the first six months of 2019, Cambodia allowed the establishment of 153 new investment projects under the investment capital of 5,181 million US dollars, which created 167,330 jobs. Compared to the same period in 2018, there are 105 projects, including 74 projects outside the special economic zone and 31 projects in the special economic zone. In the first half of 2018, the total investment was more than 3,500 million US dollars.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also changed a tax system that is better for Cambodia, as in the history of Cambodia, there has never been a tax system like now, and those who are obliged to pay taxes have participated in fulfilling their duties properly. This was confirmed by a spokesman for the Royal Government of Cambodia.
According to Mr. Phay Siphan, through this tax collection, it is an opportunity for the Royal Government to have some reserves to be ready to use in case of emergency or any need. All of that money can be used to pay the salaries of civil servants in the armed forces for at least a year.
If we look at the tourism sector, in the first seven months of 2019, nearly 1.4 million foreign tourists bought tickets to Angkor and earned more than $ 62 million. In the whole period of July 1, 2019, more than 140,000 foreign tourists bought tickets to visit Angkor and earned more than 6 million dollars.
From the achievements briefed by the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit this morning, it can be assessed that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which emerged from a fair and transparent election, has done its job. Smoothly, there is no cause for obstruction.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth chairs a meeting of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee to review and discuss two main agendas
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Chairman of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee (CSEC), chaired a meeting of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee. The meeting was held at the Ministry of Economy and Finance on July 31, 2019.
The meeting was attended by Mr. and Mrs. Senior Ministers and Ministers as well as senior leaders of relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government to review and discuss two main agendas:
1: Progress of the implementation of the reform measures package introduced by Samdech Techo Prime Minister at the 18th Royal Government-Private Forum 2: Preparation of the Performance Monitoring Framework for the Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Economy and Finance, obtained by Fresh News today, the progress of the implementation of the package of reform measures:
The package of reform measures introduced by Samdech Techo Prime Minister at the 18th Royal Government-Private Forum on March 29, 2019 aims to improve the investment climate, and enhance trade facilitation and competitiveness. Cambodia through addressing a number of major challenges, including:
* Reduction of logistics and port services, reduction of electricity prices, reduction of holidays, strengthening of public services and development of small and medium enterprises, etc. * As of the first half of 2019, the Ministry - The institution in charge has implemented those measures with remarkable results. * Most of the measures have been implemented and monitored, while a small number of measures need to be accelerated to achieve the planned time.
In addition, the meeting encouraged and encouraged the relevant ministries and institutions to continue their efforts to achieve the measures that have not yet been fully achieved by completing the plan by the end of 2019.
2: Achievement Monitoring Framework for Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4:
The Achievement Monitoring Framework for the Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4 is a new initiative to develop mechanisms and tools for monitoring and evaluating the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4, and the results will be used to strengthen the effectiveness of the Royal Government to support To achieve the vision of 2030.
In addition, the achievement monitoring framework also submitted technical consultations with relevant ministries and institutions, receiving a lot of input and improvements before submitting to the discussion meeting today.
Overall, the Meeting expressed support for the initiative to establish this monitoring framework and pledged to continue to work together to improve those key performance indicators so that the monitoring framework evaluates the implementation of the Rectangular-Phase 4 strategy. All angles and high reliability.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Meeting, thanked and commended the relevant ministries and institutions and the working group of the General Secretariat of the NCDD for their hard work and active participation in the implementation of these important tasks. Request all relevant ministries and institutions to continue to cooperate with a high sense of responsibility. Cambodia sends 73 more troops to South Sudan on humanitarian mission
(Kampong Speu): On August 1, 2019, Cambodia sent an additional 73 military police to complete a mission in South Sudan under the United Nations umbrella.
The handover ceremony of Cambodian troops to South Sudan was presided over by General Pol Saroeun, Senior Minister in charge of sending troops to the UN mission, along with Pauline Tamesis, UN Resident Coordinator. Cambodia at the Peacekeeping Forces Training Institute for Mine and War Remnants in Kampong Speu Province.
Of the 73 861th Infantry Division, 11 were women on UN peacekeeping missions in the Republic of South Sudan.
General Pol Saroeun, Senior Minister in Charge of Deploying Troops to the UN Mission, Brings Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Four-Point Recommendations to All Officers, Officers and Soldiers Who Will Go on Joint UN Peacekeeping Missions Contains:
First, to strictly implement the recommendations, which are the four points of the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, which was mentioned in the meeting to send the 135th Squadron to go on a mission to Sudan on the 12th. April 2006 ago.
Second, stand as a center of solidarity, unity, respect for rules, laws, regulations and maintain the dignity of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the nation. Study, experiment, learn more foreign languages and develop the ability to respond to its mission to accomplish tasks.
Third: Study clearly the geopolitical situation and the challenges of the mission. Always be vigilant and alert to any dangers that may result from clashes between armed groups, ambushes, natural disasters, and infectious diseases.
Fourth, respect the tradition of good relations with the country and the people in the areas where our forces carry out their missions and support the sharing of food, relief, medical treatment and protection of the people there. This is a humane, virtuous gesture worthy of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces born of the people doing things for the people.
(Phnom Penh): Spokesman of the Royal Government of Cambodia held a press conference on "Achievements one year after the election" this morning, August 1, 2019, the spokesman of the Ministry of Justice, Mr. Chin Malin confirmed that. Three major tasks that the Ministry of Justice achieved in the first year of this sixth mandate.
The spokesman claimed that the Ministry of Justice achieved three important tasks in the first year of the sixth mandate, including:
This year, the Ministry has built an appeal in three provinces: Tbong Khmum, Battambang and Sihanoukville. 3. Launch of specialized courts: Under Cambodian law, there are four specialized courts: criminal courts, civil courts, commercial courts, and labor courts. Currently, the Ministry has launched only two specialized courts, the Criminal Court and the Civil Court, and the Ministry has prepared the legal framework and human resources to be fully operational by 2020.
* Job 2: Human Resource Management: Organizing human resources through recruitment and training of judges and prosecutors. So far, the ministry has conducted nine training sessions, with a total of nearly 500 judges and prosecutors serving across the country.
* Third job: the most important is legal aid work: This legal aid work includes education, dissemination of legal aid to the people, legal counseling to the people, extracurricular mediation work, and legal work to the people. The poor who could not afford to have a case in court. Samdech Techo's volunteer lawyer is also considered as an important legal aid job.
On that occasion, Mr. Jean Malin spoke about human rights issues, explaining the procedures for assessing human rights in a country. The spokesman confirmed that human rights in Cambodia have made significant progress.
A senior official of the Ministry of Justice stated: "I would like to briefly participate in issues related to democracy, the rule of law, as well as human rights in the reform of the judiciary in promoting the people's right to justice. "If we talk about human rights, we see that Cambodia is making remarkable progress as a whole, because if we evaluate human rights, we are not just looking at one part."
He continued, "They do not look at it as a group that has a tendency to oppose or a group that hates the government, they look at it from one side, linked to political issues." "But for technicians, researchers on human rights issues, they evaluate every aspect."
When it comes to human rights, Jean Malin says there are many things, not just demonstrations. In order to assess whether a country's human rights are progressive, it is necessary to look at all aspects, including: economic rights, social affairs, culture, citizenship, politics, the rights of specific groups, such as women's rights, children's rights, indigenous peoples' rights, minority rights, and the rights of persons with disabilities. Homosexual, too.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Justice added that in Cambodia, when it comes to political rights in terms of rallies, demonstrations, demonstrations, etc., it is observed that there is protection and promotion, but why? Legal action is being taken against a small group of people exercising all these rights. Law enforcement on them because they practice in a wrong way that violates the law.
"Therefore, the competent authorities of the sovereign state must enforce the law to prevent any acts that are offensive and cause social unrest, and the implementation of these laws is not a violation of the rights and freedoms of the people, it is a necessary measure. "Only to prevent and maintain peace and social order." This is a claim from a senior official of the Ministry of Justice.
According to Mr. Chin Malin, in relation to the right to justice, people have been promoted to the right to justice through judicial reform. In principle, the goal of the reform of the Cambodian judiciary is to give the people the right to the promotion of justice, and to increase the right to justice through the provision of justice mechanisms.
He stated that in principle, there are two justice mechanisms. He said that the first: services are provided by the court through the case process and second: the actors to be provided out of court through the provision of legal assistance and out-of-court dispute resolution.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: The biggest enemies of road damage are water and overweight trucks
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the first enemy that causes the most road damage is water, and the next enemy that causes the road to damage is the truck. Exceeding the legal limit.
In this ceremony, Mr. Sun Chanthol emphasized that water is the first source that leads to road damage. He advised that when building the road, there must be proper drainage according to the standard and must be careful to pour the soil to build people's houses to avoid being higher than the road, because it causes water to flow on the road. May damage roads.
In addition to water, overloading is also a major cause of road damage. The Minister of Public Works said that overweight trucks could easily damage the road, even if the road was built to the required standard.
According to the World Bank's formula for overweight cargo, a truck over 10 tons equals 10,000 vehicles on the road, and if a truck over 30 tons. Equivalent to 810,000 cars driving on the road.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol asserted that AC level roads that meet the quality standards, with no inflow of water and no overweight trucks, can last up to 18 years if properly serviced and repaired. Time.
The minister urged transport companies not to carry more than the legal limit, which would damage the roads and cause hundreds of millions of dollars a year to repair and maintain the roads. Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An Visits Five Traffic Accident Victims at Calmette Hospital
