After two consecutive days of traffic accidents that caused 2 deaths and more than 70 injuries, Svay Rieng Provincial Police Disseminated Advice to Drivers of Workers
(Svay Rieng): Major General Koeng Khorn, Svay Rieng Provincial Police Commissioner, has issued an order to all municipal and district inspectors of the administrative police force to disseminate instructions to car owners and truck drivers in their locality. To reduce accidents that may occur eventually.
General Koeng Khorn said that with the regular guidance of Mr. Men Vibol, the provincial governor, he led the police officers to educate the traffic law to the owners of trucks carrying workers and submitted a certificate to the actual force today. Some plans to make the local police force work more effectively.
It should be noted that the above police campaign was carried out after two consecutive days of traffic accidents in Svay Teap district and Svay Rieng city, resulting in two deaths and more than 70 minor injuries. The first case occurred when a truck carrying workers overturned, killing two people and injuring 31, and in the second case, a truck collided with a truck, injuring 43 people.
While advertising to the drivers, the police officers set out a number of measures, including:
* First: Make a contract with the owner and driver of the truck carrying workers to provide seats for workers to sit * Second: Guide all truck drivers to respect all traffic laws * Third: Drivers must be understanding and tolerant Let's drive at the speed set by law * Fourth: Check the driver's license * Fifth: Take the car to check the technical characteristics often at the inspectorate.
