The following is the decision of the Ministry of Land Management: The Ministry of Interior issued an official press release on the results of the visit of Prince Sar Kheng to Turkey (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior on the afternoon of the 1st In August 2019, an official press release was issued on the results of the visit of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, to the Republic of Turkey from July 28 to August 1.
It should be informed that in the spirit of the agreement between the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Head of the Government of Turkey in the past, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, led a high-level delegation of the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia to pay an official visit to the Republic of Turkey from July 28 to August 1, 2019 to attend a bilateral meeting with Mr. Sule Mansolu, Minister of Interior of the Republic of Turkey.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed and exchanged views on global changes in the context of international security, in particular, focusing on new forms and forms of crime that could affect and Risks to the peace, stability, security, public order and social security of both countries.
After fruitful close discussions, the two sides signed the "Agreement on Security Cooperation between the Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Republic of Turkey".
In addition to key discussions and issues within the scope of the Security Cooperation Agreement, the two sides also agreed to identify four additional areas of cooperation, including:
* First: Exchange of experiences on traffic safety management and control in urban areas * Second: Exchange of experiences on strengthening and expanding partnerships between the government and civil society and non-governmental organizations to participate in social development Nation * Third: Cooperation, training and capacity building of the Water Border Police Force * Fourth: Exchange and sharing of experiences on the leadership and management of sub-national administrations.
In addition to attending bilateral meetings with his Turkish counterpart, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also visited a number of units under the Ministry of Interior of the Republic of Turkey, including the Department of Anti-Trafficking and Crime, organized organizations, security camera surveillance centers. Traffic Support and Planning Department and Special Operations Forces.
Finally, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng invited the Minister of Interior of the Republic of Turkey, Mr. Soulomansulou, to lead a delegation to visit the Kingdom of Cambodia at an appropriate time, and he gladly accepted the invitation.
During the visit, Prince Sar Kheng met with the Minister of Interior of the Republic of Turkey and signed an agreement on security cooperation between the two governments.
It should be noted that the agreement on security cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Turkey, which the two sides signed today, is the result of an agreement between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Rejib Thayer. The President of the Republic of Turkey on the occasion of the Prince's visit to the Republic of Turkey at the end of October 2018.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng led a delegation from the Ministry of Interior to leave Cambodia on July 28, 2019 to pay a visit to Turkey at the invitation of Mr. SULEYMAN SOLU, Minister of Interior of the Republic of Turkey.
