According to a press release obtained by Fresh News today, the MoU will contribute to the implementation of the fourth phase of the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy: Environment, Society and Economy.
According to the 18th Public and Private Forum, chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the past position of the Royal Government on the importance of working in partnership with the private sector to achieve effective results. Sustainability and equity.
Banks and microfinance institutions can choose to finance or contribute to projects that are positive for the environment, gender equality, economic equality, and contribute to the elimination of financing that has a negative impact, such as deforestation, air pollution, and waste. And destruction of natural resources.
Mr. Sao Sopheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, emphasized that the current engagement with the Banking Association of Cambodia is an example of the cooperation between the Royal Government and the private sector to implement the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy for Cambodia and Planetary Protection. Earth and for the benefit of member banks in attracting international funds with low interest rates.
According to Dr. In Channy, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, the Banking Association of Cambodia, through the Sustainable Finance Commission, has been continuing its main mission:
First, build management systems and necessary tools to help member banks implement sustainable financial principles. Second: Continue to build the capacity of bankers involved in environmental and social risks. Third: Continue to expand cooperation with all relevant partners to promote implementation. Sustainable and Effective Financial Principles Fourth: Promote public awareness of the Banking Association's activities related to the environment and society.
Dr. In Channy continued that in addition to the long-term vision, the Banking Association aims to promote the implementation of sustainable financial policies to other sectors, promote the modification of sustainable financial policies into rules for everyone to apply. And want Cambodia to be a leader in implementing sustainable financial principles in the Mekong region.
