Phnom Penh Newspaper Vendor Wins 100 Million Riels from Carabao Energy Drink
(Phnom Penh): A young woman who sells newspapers and school supplies behind the fence of Preah Yukanthor High School in Phnom Penh is lucky to win a grand prize of 100 million Riels from Carabao Energy Drink.
Speaking to the team that handed over the prize to the place of business, Ms. Ny Makara, 36 years old, currently lives in a rented house upstairs in Sangkat Or Russey 4, Khan 7 Makara, Phnom Penh.
She added that almost every week she looks up at them to receive a million dollars from Carabao and imagines that one day they will be as lucky as him and try to eat almost every day.
Last weekend, after setting up the stall, he was tired and bought a can of carabao drink from a nearby vendor to eat, but when he saw it, he saw a prize of 100 million riels. Suddenly, she felt very excited and shouted to the people around her to help check and call the company.
She added that after receiving the 100 million riel prize money, she will buy some upstairs houses for accommodation and leave some to buy additional study materials for sale to make life easier for the family.
