He said that the important day will contribute to cultivating the spirit of people who love to protect the precious forest to maintain the balance of climate to support the lives of people, animals, biodiversity, not only the forest reduces the vulnerability. Due to the impact of climate change, aiming to achieve improved food security of local communities.
Finally, he asked all people to participate in protecting and preserving natural resources to survive forever.
ABA Bank is the eighth company and the first commercial bank to list on the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
Mr. Hong Sohour “ABA Bank is the eighth company and the first commercial bank to be listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange. The existing listed companies include five listed companies and two listed As a bond. "These seven companies have already raised a total of 140 million US dollars from the market, which is small compared to foreign markets, but for the Cambodian market is a big starting point."
He added that the company not only received long-term capital for investment, but also received tax incentives, which are currently equal to 50% of the income tax payable, and gained reputation and trust. From the public as well.
He said that with the increase in the number of listed companies, the number of trading accounts in the market has increased significantly. In fact, the market capitalization increased from 1.77 trillion riels to about 442 million US dollars, the total market value of all listed companies in 2018 increased by about 2.28 trillion riels, about 570 million US dollars by the end of the semester. First, in 2019, an increase of about 28.75%.
Mr. Heng Bo Makara said that the listing of ABA bonds on the Cambodia Securities Exchange at this time is part of the promotion of the operation of the Cambodian capital market in line with the financial sector development strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He added that on behalf of the supervisory authority of the National Bank of Cambodia, it will continue to strengthen the regulatory framework and strengthen the effectiveness of inspections on banking and financial institutions with the implementation of gentle and prudent policies and openness to the provision of financial services. To be richer.
"I am confident that our bonds will contribute to the development of the capital markets, as well as the promotion of the national currency," he said.
