It is true that Angkor Wat, the national soul, is an important foundation in supporting the development of tourism in Cambodia, and cultural tourism is an important backbone of Cambodia's tourism, while Siem Reap is a priority tourist destination for Cambodia. Also.
"We have a lot of issues to discuss, but the first major issue is that Siem Reap needs to develop more new tourism products to attract tourists and extend their stay," he said.
In 2018, in order to support the growth of tourists visiting Siem Reap, the Royal Government decided to set up an inter-ministerial working group to study the planning of the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master, chaired by the Ministry of Tourism, and currently the working group is studying planning. The master is very active.
The master plan will focus on the development of Siem Reap, especially Siem Reap as a tourist city, a heritage city and an eco-city that needs to be integrated in terms of economy, society, culture, environment and architecture. Integration with the Angkor Area Management Plan (TMP) of the APSARA Authority.
Meanwhile, the Ministry of Tourism has been cooperating with stakeholders to organize some work to promote the development of tourism in Siem Reap, including:
* Promoting the development of tourist areas around Siem Reap, especially Prek Toal, Tonle Sap Lake, Phnom Kulen and tourism communities to create new tourism products and extend the stay of tourists.
* Encourage the development of infrastructure in the province by repairing roads, preparing adequate water and electricity supply systems, and setting up solid and liquid waste management systems in accordance with environmental standards, parking lots, public toilets, and managing transportation. Public order in the city, etc.
* Improving the quality of tourism services and human resources in the tourism sector in response to the growth of tourists by strengthening the quality of tourism vocational training schools, internal training and promoting the implementation of ASEAN standards in tourism.
