Rice Federation of Cambodia Holds Consultative Meeting on General Assembly and Election of the 3rd Mandate Rice Federation of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Rice Federation has organized a meeting chaired by Mr. Sok Puthivuth, Chairman of the Board of Directors to discuss the organization of the General Assembly and the upcoming third election of the Cambodian Rice Federation. The meeting was held on the morning of July 30, 2019.
After much deliberation, the meeting decided to restructure the new Cambodian rice for the third mandate and the election procedure of the third mandate of the Cambodian Rice Federation with 100% approval.
In the afternoon of the same day, the Rice Federation of Cambodia organized a consultation program with members and elders who have experience in the field of rice in Cambodia on the new structure and election procedures of the Rice Federation of Cambodia of the third mandate.
As a result, the entire session was enthusiastic and fully agreed on the new structure proposed by the Board and agreed on unification through the one-voice principle, with federal members adhering to Solidarity to continue to work to help the entire Cambodian rice sector in the upcoming third mandate.
Mr. Sok Puthivuth talked with the candidates of the Board of Directors of the Rice Federation of Cambodia of the third mandate and agreed on the principle of one voice, and the President gave the recommendations and the principle of the one voice to continue the operation of the Rice Federation of Cambodia of the third mandate. Moving forward sustainably and able to compete internationally, avoiding domestic competition.
The meeting and consultation program was held with good results and was highly appreciated by all members on the new coalition structure and the past achievements of the federation with great friendliness.
