(Phnom Penh): Mr. Son Kunthor, Senior Minister, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister in charge of Small and Medium Enterprises and Microfinance Institutions and President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Industry, said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, did not want to see or hear. No enterprise fails or collapses.
He said this on Wednesday morning, July 31, 2019, on the occasion of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprises held a meeting to review the results of the first half and plans for 2019-2020.
Mr. Son Kunthor said that what Samdech was most happy to see was that the business people were making a profit and growing and the lives of the Cambodian people were prosperous. Therefore, the establishment of clusters and collective units to develop micro and small and medium enterprises in Cambodia is the right decision.
He continued that the leadership of the Royal Government, which has Samdech Prime Minister Hun Sen, always pays attention and supports small and medium enterprises, by setting out favorable policies and various subsidies to make small enterprises profitable. Gain sustainability in the market.
