Authorities in Svay Rieng province said that before the incident, a truck carrying workers was driving from west to east towards Shandong Special Economic Zone "Bavet City". The steering wheel hit a truck full of workers, causing workers to throw on the road, causing serious and minor injuries all over the road.
Immediately after the incident, local authorities arrived at the scene, led by Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng and Deputy Governor, Provincial Police Commissioner, all forces intervened to help lift the victim to Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital. To the rescue. The perpetrator, who was driving a chicken truck, was immediately arrested and brought to the provincial land traffic office for legal action.
Authorities confirmed that Mr. Men Vibol and Svay Rieng Provincial Red Cross MPs were present at the provincial hospital, while the seriously injured were sent to Calmette Hospital in Phnom Penh. Pregnant women too.
Sources from the authorities confirmed that the workers were from Ang Taso and Svay Ang communes, Svay Chrum district, and every morning a truck carrying workers always drove to take workers home to work in Bavet City.
However, as of 11:00 a.m. on the same day, the number of injured was still 43, with 15 seriously injured and 28 lightly injured, and the authorities and medical teams in the rescue sent. Three people were seriously injured at Calmette Hospital.
