(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, met with Ms. Maria Sargren, Ambassador of Sweden to Cambodia as she concluded her diplomatic mission in Cambodia, as well as discussed further strengthening. More on Cambodia-Sweden Bilateral Cooperation.
The above meeting was held at the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the morning of July 30, 2019.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth expressed his deep gratitude and appreciation to the people and the Royal Government of Sweden, which Sweden is an important partner in actively contributing to the socio-economic development of Cambodia in the past.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth said that Cambodia's achievements are inseparable from the support of the Swedish government as well as the ambassador herself during her diplomatic mission in Cambodia.
In fact, Sweden has actively contributed to the reform program that the Royal Government of Cambodia is implementing by providing both financial and technical support, including the Public Financial Management Reform (PFM) program since its inception. January 1, especially tax reform.
He also thanked the friendly side for providing technical assistance as well as sharing work experience in the field of taxation by providing study tours directly to Sweden.
Ms. Maria Sargren expressed her deep gratitude for the excellent cooperation provided by relevant Cambodian institutions during her three years of diplomatic missions in Cambodia, which led to the glorious success of her diplomatic mission. To this day.
She personally witnessed Cambodia's steady growth today with strong economic growth, which is the result of the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts, especially the launch and implementation of in-depth reforms in all areas.
Discussions also focused on further deepening the reform of public financial management as the information technology public financial management program (FMIS) was implemented and expanded to ministries and institutions. Other, transparency and accountability and the establishment of a single center for all data and statistics (Data Center).
