The embassies of countries that like to work without knowing their jurisdiction and interfering in Cambodia's sovereignty have called last year's election the elimination of Cambodia's largest opposition party, further undermining it. Cambodia's achievements in promoting political reconciliation and promoting economic growth since the 1991 Paris Peace Accords.
Do the embassies of the American superpowers not know about the diplomatic law or do they know and pretend not to know? Embassy of the United States, do not act as more Cambodian, more Cambodian, more Cambodian people, more voters who went to the polls with confidence!
The Cambodian people have no one to believe you anymore. The Cambodian people, the masters of the country's destiny, know and see very clearly that Cambodia has always adhered to multi-party democracy as stated in the Cambodian Constitution. Political competition has expanded and elections have been held regularly since 1993.
Cambodia recently held a successful Commune / Sangkat Council Election on June 4, 2017, with 12 parties participating and 7.8 million registered voters. On July 29, 2018, Cambodia also successfully held the 6th National Assembly election in a free, fair and successful manner.
Twenty political parties participated in the election. In comparison, turnout rose to a new high of 83.2%, compared to 55% for the 2016 US presidential election. It is a true reflection of the will of the people.
In fact, in every election in Cambodia, there are always international observers, including observers from the United States.
Observers agreed that the election was peaceful, free and fair because they had come to observe, not sit and criticize like the US Embassy.
A simple question here, who is most appropriate to judge a free and fair election in Cambodia? International observers who participated in the actual observation or do you remember not watching?
Stop, stop, do not interfere in the internal affairs of Cambodia for Cambodia to live happily. Assessing the July National Election in Cambodia is a flawed election and only one great power can do so without shame.
The history of Cambodia is really fed up with the actions of the United States! Because of these untrue allegations, the United States dropped more than 3 million tons of bombs on the heads of Cambodians without a word of apology, and now they are pursuing to prevent Cambodians from living in peace. History knows very well that the United States was never happy when Cambodia prospered.
Cambodia is committed to building good relations with the United States based on the principles of international relations, including non-interference, mutual respect and mutual benefit. We must also uphold the universal values of fairness, environment and openness.
