It should be noted that on July 30, 2019, at the invitation of Thai Foreign Minister Daun Pram Mod Vinay, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon led a delegation to attend the 52nd ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings. It will take place from July 30 to August 3, 2019 in Bangkok, Thailand.
Mr. Prak Sokhon, along with other ASEAN Foreign Ministers, will pay a courtesy call on Thai Prime Minister HE Prayuth Chan-o-cha.
Under the theme "Promoting Partnership for Sustainability", the 52nd ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings will focus on enhancing cooperation to further promote the ASEAN Community Building Process and strengthen regional convention. Focus on the ASEAN Center as well as expanding partnerships with ASEAN Dialogue Partners and external parties.
As the facilitator for the ASEAN-New Zealand Dialogue Partnership (2018-2021), Prak Sokhon will co-chair with Mr. Winston Peters, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade of New Zealand. "With New Zealand."
Coinciding with the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting, Mr. Prak Sokhon, along with other ASEAN Foreign Ministers, will witness the signing ceremony of the instrument of accession to the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia by the Republic of Peru. And the Republic of South Africa.
The Cambodian Ambassador will also attend the inauguration of the ASEAN-China Young Leaders Scholarship Program and the ASEAN-Australia Anti-Trafficking Initiative.
In addition to the ASEAN Foreign Ministers 'Meeting, Mr. Prak Sokhon will attend the following other meetings: - The 12th Lower Mekong Initiative Foreign Ministers' Meeting - The 10th Ministerial Meeting of the Mekong-Mekong Cooperation The 9th Mekong-Republic of Korea Foreign Ministers 'Meeting and the 12th Mekong-Japan Foreign Ministers' Meeting
