Mr. Net Pheaktra confirmed in a statement on July 30, 2019: "The countries that are the source of this plastic waste, including the authorities of Canada and the United States have contacted the Royal Government of Cambodia to find out. More information to investigate the export of these plastic waste. "The authorities of the two countries have shown cooperation on this issue."
On July 16, 2019, 83 General Containers weighing nearly 1,600 tons imported from the United States and Canada to Cambodia were searched by the General Department of Customs and Excise in cooperation with the relevant authorities.
According to the report of the General Department of Customs and Excise of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, these plastic waste goods were brought in several ships (27 times) and landed at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port. The first in September 2018 and the last in January 2019, a total of 83 containers of the same size 40 feet.
The company that is waiting to receive the plastic waste for recycling is named Jung Yuan Plastic Manifourer Ek. With a Cambodian boss named Suon Lok. But the companies that supply plastic waste to the company in the United States and Canada are still unknown.
According to Mr. Net Pheaktra, according to the inspection of the professional body, the imported plastic waste is packed or wrapped in large goods and thin plastic for packing food or fruit or wrapped in suitcases at the airport, which can not be used. But no stains were found. These plastic waste does not contain heavy metal compounds that exceed the standard can affect human health or lead to environmental damage.
He claimed that the Royal Government of Cambodia adheres to the strict position that the plastic waste, which is a prohibited product from entering Cambodia, will be sent back to its original source. Companies and those involved in the import of plastic waste face applicable laws and face severe penalties.
He said that the Royal Government of Cambodia will continue to implement strict legal measures against the smuggling of all kinds of prohibited goods. The Royal Government of Cambodia does not allow the import of plastic waste for recycling in Cambodia. Cambodia is not a dumping ground for outdated technology, and Cambodia has always opposed the import of plastic waste and motor oil for recycling in Cambodia.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, the Ministry of Environment, encourages the recycling of plastic waste as a raw material in Cambodia, because Cambodia has also been facing pollution by plastic waste, but does not allow the import of plastic waste from abroad. No processing in Cambodia.
Please note that in relation to the import of 83 containers of plastic waste to Cambodia, the Royal Government has decided to fine Chung Yuan Plastic Manufacturing Co., Ltd. The goods must be returned to the country of origin before August 24, 2019. At the same time, the Royal Government decided to fine the company in the amount of 1037.5 million Riels into the national budget.
According to the same announcement, in case the company does not comply with the above three conditions, the Royal Government will take legal action against the company as well. This rubbish is imported by Chung Yuan Plastic Management Co., Ltd. With a Cambodian boss named Suon Lok.
According to the equipment of the General Department of Customs and Excise and the laboratory equipment of the Ministry of Environment, the plastic waste does not contain any other harmful substances. Nearly 7,000 patients admitted to Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital this July, Kampong Cham provincial governor told doctors to try to provide better health services
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, told the doctors to continue to pay attention to provide better health services to the people.
The Provincial Governor instructed the doctors while accompanied by Dr. Kim Sour Phirun, Director of the Provincial Health Department to visit patients at the Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital on the afternoon of July 29, 2019.
According to Dr. Kim Sour Phirun, a total of 6,959 patients were admitted to Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital in July 2019.
Among the general patients admitted to the hospital were: tuberculosis, malaria, dengue fever, while the total number of major and minor surgery was 919.
