2,500 seedlings planted at Prasat Bakong District Hall, Siem Reap Province to promote environmental aesthetics
(Siem Reap): In order to improve the aesthetics of the environment and increase the forest cover, 2,500 saplings were planted by Prasat Bakong district authorities in the district hall as part of preventing anarchic activities in the forestry sector. And a strong sense of community for the benefit of the people who depend on non-timber forest products.
The planting ceremony was held on July 30, 2019 in the presence of Mr. Teap Bunchuy, Chairman of Prasat Bakong District Council, Mr. So Platon, Prasat District Governor and Mr. Sem Sok Khoy, General Director of Vyathapura Company. Develop a private company that has co-sponsored these saplings to plant a new garden in the district hall.
There are 2,500 trees that have been handed over to be planted at the district hall, including 2,000 rosewood trees and 500 flowering trees, such as Trabek Prey, Loeung Reach, Peacock and Rumduol.
In this ceremony, which also received 10 public lighting lamps (solar) sponsored by Youth Business Company through Mr. Phou Pheakdey, a representative of the company to distribute for installation in the 9 commune halls and 1 panel in District Hall compound.
The planting of trees now is to take care of the environment, inspire love of nature, especially to reduce the heat to the planet and enhance the beauty of the district hall to be attractive and to connect the district administration with businessmen, traders and people. Also, as the saying goes, "One person plants a tree for the balance of our national natural resource environment."
