(Turkey): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and Mr. Suleyman Soylu, Minister of Interior of the Republic of Turkey, on Tuesday, July 30, 2019. Sign an agreement on security cooperation between Cambodia and Turkey.
After signing the Security Cooperation Agreement, Suleyman Soylu, Minister of Interior of the Republic of Turkey, and Prince Sar Kheng addressed a ceremony attended by the signing ceremony. This importance.
He said that after the visit between the top leaders and the current visit of Prince Kralahom, the strengthening of cooperation and relations between the two countries will be strengthened in a meeting with Prince Sar Kheng on this occasion. Fruitful discussions and good results.
The Turkish Interior Minister stressed that in the meeting before the signing, the two sides discussed counter-terrorism work, including security cooperation, and agreed to further strengthen cooperation in these two areas. Strength and get better results.
Regarding the visit of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and the delegation of the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia on this occasion, he stated that it was time to celebrate the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries and also the first time of the visit. Of the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia and the signing of a security cooperation agreement between the two countries.
He then expressed his pleasure and deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior of Cambodia, for taking action against the Feto terrorist group in the past, that both sides will continue to work hard. More on this counter-terrorism work.
In addition to signing security agreements, the two sides also agreed to strengthen cooperation, exchange experiences in public order, safety and traffic management, and exchange experiences on strengthening partnerships between the Royal Government and Civil society organizations.
He also said that the two sides are also committed to promoting cooperation in the training of police, security officers, coast guard and the military police, and that in the spirit of the agreement on future security cooperation, both sides Two will promote police training of both countries.
In particular, at the bilateral meeting, the Minister of Interior of the Republic of Turkey also informed the ceremony that the two sides also discussed regional and global issues, including the exchange of views on terrorist networks and networks. The flow of migrants.
Afterwards, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked His Excellency the Minister of Interior of Turkey for inviting him and his delegation to visit on this occasion.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng considered this invitation as a confirmation of the good intentions of His Excellency the Minister and the Government of Turkey in promoting relations and cooperation between the two countries in general and in particular regarding security cooperation between the Ministries. Interior of both countries.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also expressed his full agreement with what the Turkish Minister of Interior said that what both sides received today was due to the pioneering efforts of the two countries' top leaders, His Excellency The President of Turkey and Samdech Techo Prime Minister of Cambodia.
On this occasion, Prince Kralahom praised the progress of the Republic of Turkey, despite the security issues and many other issues, but under the leadership of His Excellency the President and the active participation of His Excellency the Minister of Interior of Turkey. Still growing and hopeful.
Separately, Samdech also expressed confidence that in addition to the Royal Government, the relationship between the people of the two countries will be more developed in Turkey today, there are about 70 Cambodian students, including Cambodian Muslim students, and Samdech It is hoped that the number of students coming to study will increase.
Finally, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng expressed his support for the full statement of the Minister of Interior of Turkey regarding the discussions and agreements on security cooperation and stressed that both sides have shown willingness to implement. Yet practical to benefit each other.
It should be noted that the agreement on security cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Turkey, which the two sides signed today, is the result of an agreement between Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. And His Excellency Regip Thayipir, President of the Republic of Turkey, on the occasion of the Prince's visit to the Republic of Turkey at the end of October 2018.
