Minister of Agriculture: As of July, Cambodia exported more than 2 million tons of agricultural products
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on July 30, 2019, confirmed that as of July 2019, Cambodia has exported a total of more than 2.37 million tons of agricultural products.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Minister Veng Sakhon thanked the people and government of Malaysia for their good cooperation with Cambodia and for their continued support of Cambodia's agricultural products exported to the Malaysian market in the past. Come on.
Mr. Veng Sakhon also briefed the Ambassador on the progress of the agricultural sector under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, from a country that could not afford to supply food to its people to a country with a food surplus. Nearly 4 million tons of rice and a country that exports agricultural products to the world market.
Regarding agricultural exports, the Minister pointed out that as of July this year, Cambodia had exported a total of more than 2.37 million tons of agricultural products. Another major achievement that the Royal Government, recently headed by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, is the export of Cambodian yellow bananas directly to the Chinese market.
The Minister hopes and believes that through the Ambassador, trade cooperation on agricultural products and animal production between the two countries, especially Malaysian investors to invest in the processing of agricultural products in Cambodia and the export of agricultural products to the country. Malaysia will be effectively promoted and expanded to another level.
He also requested the Malaysian side to review the progress and promote the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Cambodia and the Ministry of Agriculture and Industry based on agro-industry of Malaysia.
The Ambassador praised the achievements as well as the progress made by the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Ministry in the past and present.
He fully agreed with the Minister's remarks regarding the work to strengthen and expand investment from Malaysia in agriculture and processing of agricultural products, stating that during September, some Malaysian investment companies will visit. Find out more about the potential of Cambodia's agricultural sector.
He added that the Malaysian side is pleased to increase the volume of agricultural trade between the two countries, as the Malaysian side has decided to increase rice imports from Cambodia and is very interested in other products such as pepper, tamarind and coconut oil.
The Ambassador also stated that during his tenure, he will do his best to promote, strengthen and expand cooperation between the two countries in the field of agriculture for the sustainable development for the benefit of both countries. Two.
