At least 52 people have been killed in clashes in a Brazilian prison after a group of inmates clashed, a BBC report says. Punishment fought fiercely for five hours.
Sixteen of the dead were beheaded, officials said at a news conference. Another report said parts of the prison had been set on fire. Two prison officials who were abducted by prisoners during the clashes have been released.
