(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree appointing and granting 106 additional advisors to the Ministry of Information, with the same rank from Director General to Secretary of State. This is according to the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News.
The newly appointed advisers to the Ministry of Information also include the five founders of the Federation of Cambodian Journalists: 1: Ms. Long Ratana, 2: Mr. Cheang Sokha, 3: Mr. Vong Sokheng, 4: Mr. Hem Bun Chuy and 5: Mr. Khieu Navy.
The following is the Royal Decree: Sanofi Cambodia gives love to the people of Cambodia by donating blood to the National Blood Transfusion Center
(Phnom Penh): Sanofi Cambodia on the morning of July 30, 2019, participated in activities to help society and give love to the people of Cambodia through the second blood donation in collaboration with the Center. Nation donates blood to raise awareness of the need for current blood at the office of Sanofi Cambodia.
Ms. Monsinee added: "We are very pleased that our staff has volunteered to donate blood, which is a gift of love to save lives. Moreover, this is also the spirit and charity and social activities, one of the many activities that Sanofi Cambodia always pays attention to and promotes good activities for the society.
Dr. Khay Sokheng, Mobile Team Leader of the National Blood Transfusion Center, said that the daily blood demand is more than 300 blocks. This is a serious need that the National Blood Transfusion Center is facing in seeking blood donations to meet this need.
Lately, the contribution of blood donations has increased significantly from general philanthropists and through companies as well as state institutions. However, with the increasing demand every day, therefore, blood donation is indeed limited to meet this growing demand, especially as technology advances, so does the demand for blood.
Dr. Khay Sokheng also appealed to the public who are 18 years old and weighing 45 kg or more to donate blood up to four times a year for men and three times for women. Men can donate every three months and women every four months. This difference is due to the biological characteristics between men and women.
The doctor also stressed that donating blood does not really affect health because donating 350 ml of blood, or about 5-6% of the whole body, contains about 50-60% plasma, which is converted from water. . Therefore, after donating blood, donors are required to drink plenty of water.
Between two and three hours later, it will replenish plasma. As for red blood cells, it will fill about 25 ml a day. So in about two to three weeks, the blood will return to normal. In medical techniques, blood loss of more than 30% requires patients to receive a blood transfusion, while donating 5% to 6% of blood does not really affect health.
Dr. Khay Sokheng also thanked the staff of Sanofi Cambodia for always supporting and actively contributing to the blood donation activities and also encouraged Sanofi Cambodia as well as many other companies to continue this social activity. As part of humanitarian activities, the Ministry handed over land titles to 176 families in Chit Borey district, Kratie province.
(Kratie): Mr. Sor Sovann, Secretary of State, Mr. Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, handed out 258 land ownership certificates to 176 concessionaires in Dar commune, Chit Borei district, Kratie province this morning. July 30, 2019 at the O'Kee Sen Chey community building.
Mr. Sor Sovann expressed his pleasure and congratulations to all the concessionaires who have received the Certificate of Identification of Real Estate Owners at this time. He said that after the people received social land from the Royal Government through the Land Allocation for Social Affairs and Economic Development Phase II (LASED II), people have land for housing and land for cultivation to improve livelihoods. Its and modify the new face.
At the same time, he said that obtaining land titles now, people will be safer to occupy and use the land received from the Royal Government as a legacy for posterity. Another point is that it becomes capital to provide a regular income through the cultivation and hatching of the people who are the concessionaires.
