(Phnom Penh): The Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) and the Department of Peacebuilding and Infrastructure Rehabilitation of JICA this morning, July 30, 2019, signed the minutes of the meeting between the Japanese Advisory Mission. And the Cambodian Mine Action Center on Japanese Technical Cooperation for Strengthening the Role of CMAC.
The signing ceremony was attended by Mr. Heng Ratana, Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) and Mr. SAKANE Koji, Director of the Department of Peacebuilding and Reconstruction of JICA, Tokyo, Japan. The ceremony was held at CMAC Command, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Heng Ratana stated that this technical cooperation project has a duration of 4 years (February 2020-February 2024). The main goal of this project is to strengthen the role of CMAC to participate in achieving the national plan. The Royal Government's Mine Action in Commitment to the Ottawa Convention in 2025, and in particular to strengthen the capacity and role of CMAC to continue its work after 2025, both in the country, in the region and in the international arena.
According to Heng Ratana, the Japanese government has decided to provide this project at the request of the Royal Government to support CMAC in what CMAC lacks, whether in terms of outreach or technical work.
