Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on people to eat pork as usual, do not worry too much about African swine fever (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Once again, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on July 30, 2019 It reiterated its call for people to eat pork sold on the market as usual, and called on people not to worry too much about African swine fever because the disease is not contagious.
Since the beginning of April, African swine fever has re-emerged in Cambodia, spreading to five provinces, including Ratanakkiri, Tbong Khmum, Svay Rieng, Takeo and Kandal, affecting about 3,000 pigs. The head was mutilated and killed.
However, the disease is not a risk to human health, but some people are still worried about eating dead pork.
As people have been panicking in recent weeks, pig farmers and pork sellers have complained about declining pork sales following the outbreak of African swine fever. But people suspend or reduce pork consumption.
