(Phnom Penh): So far, more than 3,000 private security agents have received training and retraining from the Department of Private Security Management of the General Commission of the National Police. This is according to Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department of Private Security Management on the morning of July 30, 2019.
At the opening ceremony of the 19th Private Security Agency Training Course, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey said that the private security sector is very important to contribute to maintaining security, public order and safety for the people. Therefore, the Ministry of Interior and the General The National Police Commission, which is staffed by the Department of Private Security Management, has opened a series of training courses.
According to Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey, from the first phase of the study until the 19th, for more than a year, the Department of Private Security Management has trained and trained more than 3,000 private security agents. And the specialized department will continue to provide continuous training to enhance the capacity of private security agencies.
He added that private security agencies not only have the role of protecting private property or private enterprises, but also have the duty to participate in protecting public property, social security and the lives of citizens, especially as The main support force to the competent authorities.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey added that security agencies also have the right to assist as a force to help arrest the perpetrators and must immediately report to the competent authorities to hand the perpetrators to the authorities for legal action and security agencies. Private guards at various entertainment venues must immediately report any incidents, especially drug offenses at guesthouses, nightclubs and karaoke.
The Private Security Management Department of the General Commission of the National Police, headed by Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, is committed to ensuring that all private security agencies in Cambodia have the capacity, knowledge and professionalism to contribute to security. Order and social security with the competent authorities.
