Vietnam seizes 125 kg worth of smuggled rhinoceros horns worth 4 million USD
Fifty-five rhinoceros horns are hidden in white lime. The illegal goods were found last Thursday.
According to authorities, the shipment was not taxed to avoid customs officials inspecting it as it was delivered to Hanoi International Airport.
Vietnam and China are often trading places for rhino horns.
Many Chinese believe that horns can be used to treat diseases, including cancer. But there is no evidence of the benefits for the drug from the horn.
Waste collected from Angkor area is composted, 80 tons every year, 160 tons more next year
(Siem Reap): The APSARA Authority has confirmed that some fresh and dried waste collected from some Angkor resorts is used as compost, with an annual production of 80 tons and an increase in production by 2020. 160 tons, which is also a continuation of the campaign against the use of plastic and enhance the beauty of Angkor.
Mr. Yit Chanda, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, said that in 2008, APSARA Authority established the Angkor Bridge Natural Agricultural Station located east of Angkor Wat on an area of more than 7 hectares, which is an active composting facility for supply. To the cultivation of agriculture in the Angkor resort.
Mr. Yit Chandarath said that APSARA Authority has also sent a team to regularly educate the local people about the negative effects of garbage in the Angkor resort by teaching them about clean villages, clean resorts, including the benefits of packaging and distribution. Store rubbish properly in designated areas.
APSARA Authority also publicly appealed to the people of all walks of life and national tourists to participate in preventing the use of plastic, packaging and proper storage of garbage in the designated places to avoid harm to the environment and enhance the beauty of Angkor. Beauty.
