During Sunday's eighth week of protests, Hong Kong police fired tear gas and rubber bullets to disperse a crowd trying to break into a Chinese government's office in Hong Kong. .
The protests were led by anti-government protesters in Hong Kong and pro-democracy activists opposed to the extradition of suspects to mainland China, as well as demanding the resignation of Hong Kong chief executive Carrie Lam.
Microfinance Association of Cambodia calls on the public to beware of cheating Phnom Penh business loans
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Microfinance Association issued a press release calling on the public to beware of cheating Phnom Penh Business Loan Co., Ltd., which disseminates false information. This is according to a press release obtained by Fresh News on July 29.
According to a press release from the Cambodian Microfinance Association, “Recently, Phnom Penh Business Loan Co., Ltd. published false information and used photos of the board members and the logo of the Cambodian Microfinance Association for the purpose of fraud and exaggeration. In fact, to attract public support on its Facebook page with some pictures and logos.
The Cambodian Microfinance Association states, “We have no relationship with Phnom Penh Business Loan Co., Ltd. Therefore, the public should consider and be very careful with the information published by this company to avoid any scams.
The Cambodian Microfinance Association strongly rejects the dissemination of false information using photos of the board members and the logo of Phnom Penh Business Loan Co., Ltd. At the same time, the association is preparing to take legal action for falsifying company information on the association in accordance with the legal procedures in force.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Microfinance Association, which represents the microfinance institutions that accept deposits, microfinance institutions and 96 financial leasing companies that are members of the association, have been providing legal financial services to about 2 million Cambodian families. In 25 capitals, provinces and cities of Cambodia.
