Last month, Japan tightened its exports of high-tech raw materials to South Korea. The move was seen by Seoul as retaliation for a South Korean court ruling over a case in which South Koreans were forced to work for a Japanese company during the Japanese colonial period.
The dispute between the two countries has prompted a strong boycott by South Koreans of Japanese products and services ranging from beer to clothing and travel in South Korea.
