Chinese navy announces military drill near Taiwan
BEIJING (Reuters) - The Chinese military will conduct a military exercise in waters near Taiwan this week, just days after warnings were issued, the Chinese Maritime Safety Agency said Monday. Use military force to invade the island if necessary. This was released by Reuters on Monday afternoon, July 29, 2019.
Last week, the Chinese Defense Ministry reiterated that Beijing would use military force to attack Taiwan if Taipei dared to declare independence or any foreign force, especially the United States, would try to break the border. This island is from mainland China. According to international law, Taiwan is only a Chinese province, as stated in the one-China policy, and the United States itself has long recognized it.
