Excerpts from relevant reports and articles published by international organizations, international institutions, leading banks and major Western media on China's economic development process and Chinese investment worldwide.
BEIJING (Reuters) - The following is an excerpt from a series of news articles and reports from major Western newspapers, major banks and the World Bank on China's economic development. From Chinese investment around the world and analysis of the future of the trade war between China and the United States:
1: China's economic growth continues to dominate
China's economic growth rate of 6.3% in the first half clearly indicates that China is still the largest source of growth in the world. As much as China's annual GDP growth is equal to Australia's full-year economy, the world does not need to worry about the onset of the crisis.
According to research by the Reserve Bank of Australia, in the 19th century, during the heyday of the United States, the economy experienced a three-year recession. Japan experienced high economic growth during the 1960s, but has been experiencing recession for more than 20 years since the early 1990s.
Reuters reports that with the subsequent adoption of previous supportive policies, China's economy is expected to achieve steady growth during the last half of the year. In particular, through the establishment of the "Belt and Road" cooperation, some of China's western provinces are becoming a leading platform for open policy, which can hopefully become a new force to boost China's economy. To the next day.
2: Economic reforms reduce China's level of dependence on world trade
According to a World Research Institute report by McKinsey, China is in the process of fully integrating into the world economy and has now become a potential trading power. In the world, which leads to increased global dependence on China.
China's economy is shifting to domestic demand as a driving force for the continuous growth of domestic spending capacity, making China even bigger in the context of "self-production and consumption". McKinsey's 2018 Global Consumer Confidence Data shows that 26% of Chinese consumers are currently in need of additional spending, but only 17% of the world's 10 largest economies.
At the same time, China will strengthen its own technical research and development, accelerate the localization of Chinese supply chain in the fields of solar (solar power systems), high-speed rail, electronic payment services, and the automobile industry, covering 90% to 100% of the domestic market. The "China Product 2025" plan will push China's other major technical sectors to achieve a domestic production rate of 40% to 90%.
3: China is highly in line with the world in the technical chain
The World Trade Organization, the World Bank, the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development and McKinsey have released separate and comprehensive research reports on the Chinese economy and world trade from 2000 to 2017. China accounts for 35% of the world's manufacturing sector.
4: China will finally win over trade war
5. China-Africa cooperation brings many benefits to Africa
Chinese enterprises provide free food and shelter, saving local workers more money. We cite Ethiopia as an example for locals who have to pay half of their salaries for food, which shows that the provision of food and accommodation from Chinese enterprises is a real big benefit. Kampong Cham Provincial Administration issues a press release on preventing and ensuring land encroachment in Phnom Thom area, Batheay district
