(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Tourism has decided to award certificates to 694 more tour guide trainees, including 50 from the 4th generation, 304 from the 25th generation and 340 from the 26th to apply for a license. Legal tour guide professional license.
The certification ceremony was held on July 29, 2019 in Siem Reap province, presided over by Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, with about 700 participants.
The above trainees went through a 6-month training course (4-month theoretical part and a 2-month research internship) and passed a regular evaluation test, which was also provided by the University of South East Asia (USEA) in Siem Reap. Cooperation in training is also highly valued.
The Secretary of State instructed the participants to further develop their skills and to apply for a tour guide license online or through the Department of Tourism in order to be able to practice their profession legally.
On the other hand, it is necessary to contribute to the promotion of national prestige, regardless of political affiliation, and to strictly adhere to the tourism law, sub-decree on tourism guides, and the code of conduct and professional ethics of tour guides set by the Ministry of Tourism.
He also instructed all the trainees who have just passed the exam to pay attention to study and respect the rules of the school well, in order to do so after completing the training, the trainees will have extensive knowledge, sufficient ability and real professional skills. Definitely able to work well in tourism.
Please be reminded that the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has the Ministry of Tourism as a professional staff, has given priority to skills training and job creation for Cambodian youth in response to the strong growth of national and international tourism.
China's crude oil imports from Iran fell by more than 60 percent from the beginning of the year to June due to US sanctions on Iran. National Bank of Cambodia explains international reserves to the public to avoid confusion!
(Phnom Penh): After examining some misunderstandings related to international reserves, an important indicator of the strength of the economy, the National Bank of Cambodia has further explained some international reserves to avoid any misunderstanding to the public. .
According to the National Bank of Cambodia, according to the International Monetary Fund (IMF), a country's international reserves refer to the internationally recognized assets that a country has and is controlled by the monetary authority for use in case of need, such as: financing. To the balance sheet, if necessary, exchange market intervention to manage exchange rate fluctuations and maintain confidence in the national currency and economy.
The National Bank of Cambodia points out that international reserves can take the form of gold and other IMF-recognized currencies such as the US dollar, the euro, the British pound, the Japanese yen and the Chinese yen. The IMF always recommends that member countries maintain adequate levels of international reserves. To set this level, the IMF always compares the size of international reserves to the number of months of imports of goods and services in the future.
For developing countries like Cambodia, the minimum adequacy level of international reserves should be three months of imports of goods and services in the future. The reason why the IMF prefers to compare international reserves to imports is because imports are a demand for foreign goods and services that a country needs to supply the economy adequately in addition to domestic production.
