The head of the Royal Government considers Kao Kim Hourn to be one of only three people qualified to run for the 2023 ASEAN Secretary-General when it comes to Cambodia, while the current ASEAN Secretary-General is Brunei's dignitary.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "His Excellency Kao Kim Hourn, the Deputy Prime Minister, I am planning to run for ASEAN Secretary-General in 2023, because there are three candidates for the ASEAN Secretary-General for Cambodia, which I can present. You have already given.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, to prepare a procedure to send Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, an expert on international affairs, to act as ASEAN Secretary-General.
This is the first time that Cambodia has had the opportunity to be the Secretary-General of ASEAN since Cambodia joined ASEAN in 1999. This is according to Mr. Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
Recall that ASEAN was formally established in 1967 and at that time ASEAN did not yet have a General Secretariat, and this Secretariat was only established in 1976. So far, there are 10 ASEAN members, including Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam.
