This Monday morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inspected the construction site of "Moradok Techo" Stadium
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, July 29, 2019, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen inspected the construction site of the “Techo Heritage” National Stadium and had a talk. With workers, leaders, sports officials and many other athletes.
In addition to inspecting and meeting with leaders, sports officials and athletes, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also presided over the installation of the last concrete seats, which is a symbol of the appearance of this large stadium.
Mr. Vath Chamroeun, Secretary General of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia (NOCC), said that the installation of the latest concrete seats is a symbol of the appearance of the stadium, which will show the greatness of the Emerald Techo National Stadium for sports. The 32nd SEA Games in 2023, which Cambodia will host for the first time, is a historic achievement under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
The Moradok Techo National Stadium is expected to cost between 100 million and 200 million US dollars, most of which will come from the Chinese government. Moradok Techo National Stadium is one of Cambodia's most modern national stadiums, built to host the 2023 SEA Games.
Currently, the construction of this stadium is in the second phase of construction, the construction of a large stadium used for football, rugby and athletics. The stadium is built on an area of more than 16 hectares and can accommodate up to 60,000 spectators.
The stadium also has 34 hotels, shops, clothing, sports equipment, sports equipment and products, children's playground, a number of gymnasiums under the main building, and the features of this stadium is There are many safe gates that can rescue 60,000 people in just 7 minutes.
The second phase of construction is also nearing completion, with completion scheduled for the end of 2020.
