Real estate experts share experiences on effective real estate investment
(Phnom Penh): Well-known real estate experts in Cambodia share their experiences on "effective real estate investment".
This program is organized by the Association of Appraisers and Real Estate Agents of Cambodia.
Mr. Man Chandy gave a presentation on how to use investment capital in the real estate sector, he mentioned some factors that entrepreneurs in this sector should do with how to use capital to be profitable and do business in the long run.
He added that investing in real estate for a profit is not easy. Types of investments should be divided into: focusing on investing in real estate as a home, start a small investment before working to increase, choose a house with a good neighbor as a house with a good location, choose a property that people Most want to live and have a lot of rental needs.
Mr. Sorn Sieb also presented the real estate appraisal before investing, he said that before investing should look at the location, size, depth, plot and shape of the land to make the investment run smoothly.
He added that the factors that we should evaluate before investing is to know the factors of resale and easy to profit.
Mr. Preap Kol showed how to build trust between real estate agents and investors to succeed in investing in big projects.
He said that building trust requires honesty, teamwork to increase trust for the other partner, respect for time, showing the juices of communication, respect for the other partner and so on.
Mr. Chrek Soknim also made a presentation on investing in real estate with high efficiency and high profit.
He said that in order to invest in real estate, you have to invest in looking at the road conditions, the location to suit the actual needs.
"For buying to live, you have to look at the taste of living, which means that some people like to live along the river, so as a seller, we should introduce the benefits in the river area," he said. Others like to live in civilized areas, so it is advisable to advise customers living in the city center.
