Suspect Arrested in Banlung Murder Case
(Ratanakkiri): After a thorough investigation into the murder case in Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province, the Banlung Municipal Armed Forces in cooperation with the Ratanakkiri Provincial Armed Forces this morning, July 28, 2019, arrested a young man. Sam Mako, 18 years old, lives in Lot village, Ting Chak commune, Bor Keo district.
This case of violence occurred on the night of July 23, 2019, when the suspect used a sword to cut the victim, Eng Ratha, causing his death on the spot at Ta Chuong, at the mouth of Boeung Kanseng Lake in Tes Anlong village, Boeung Kanseng commune. Banlung City, the suspect escaped.
Brigadier General Hay Vannara, Commander of the Banlung Municipal Gendarmerie, told Fresh News that after receiving the information that the suspect went into hiding in Lot village, Ting Chak commune, Bor Keo district, the military forces actually arrested him.
Currently, the suspect and the exhibits have been sent to the Ron Kiri Provincial Armed Forces Command to build a case to be sent to the provincial court to be punished according to the law.
