(Phnom Penh): Mr. Phay Siphan, Spokesman of the Royal Government of Cambodia, expressed his support for the activities of the Anti-Corruption Unit as well as the Natural Resources Crime Suppression and Prevention Committee, which has been active in cracking down on irregularities that damage the reputation. The Royal Government and the Pride of the Nation.
"The implementation of the ACU's anti-corruption measures is a clear message in response to the recommendations of the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, in the context of the five approaches," he said.
The Royal Government Spokesperson also reminded to punish any official who commits corruption for kidnapping. Collaborate with the ACU and the Commission for the Suppression and Prevention of Natural Resource Crimes.
"We all work together for the peace and prosperity of the nation through cooperation and implementation of all aspects of the Prime Minister's approach," he said.
Venezuela claims US spy plane violates airspace again
Venezuela has accused the United States of violating its airspace again, with similar incidents last week, with Washington blaming Caracas for sending planes. Fighters chase American planes unprofessional in the Caribbean. This is according to a quote from the Russian newspaper RT on Sunday afternoon, July 28, 2019.
Last week, a similar incident occurred. Venezuela then moved its Su-30 fighter jets to intercept the same US EP-3 fighter jets, while Washington blamed Venezuela's fighter jets for flying too close and pursuing its aircraft dangerously. But this time it is not clear whether Venezuela has moved more fighter jets.
The United States maintains that all of its aircraft are constantly operating in international airspace. But according to Caracas, since the beginning of 2019, US planes have violated at least 78 Venezuelan airspace so far.
Girl dies in Kampong Cham river while diving while unable to swim
(Kampong Cham): A 14-year-old teenage girl drowned while diving in the river to play with six other friends, even though she could not swim, causing grief to her family.
According to local authorities, this incident happened on the afternoon of July 27, 2019 in front of Wat Moni Rainsy in Orun village, Khpob Ta Ngoun commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province.
The victim is 14-year-old Phean Hangly, a resident of Dey Leu village, Peam Koh Sna commune, Stung Trang district. Before the incident, the victim girl and six other girl friends went to visit the river at the scene, but the girl could not swim, so she drowned.
Authorities confirmed that after examining the body, found that the girl really died from drowning and handed over the body to the family to take to the traditional ceremony.
Former student of Chea Sim High School, Takeo, 1986, commemorates teachers and inaugurates the statues of Jayavarman VII and King Kan
(Takeo): A group of alumni of Chea Sim Takeo High School in 1986 organized a memorial service for the teachers, the inauguration of the garden and the seating of the students, as well as the inauguration of the statue of King Jayavarman VII and the statue of King Kan (King Srey Chetha). In the garden of Chea Sim High School, Takeo.
Mr. Rin Ravi, representing all the students, said that 30 years ago, we, the children of farmers from 10 districts of Takeo province, more than 200 people came to study for the high school diploma exam by some students. Make stalls, some live in orphanages and stay in pagodas.
He said that with the willingness to be curious and with the efforts of education, guidance and teaching by teachers, has made all students successful until today.
Mr. Rin Ravi added that the group of alumni of Chea Sim High School in 1986 will continue to hold a memorial service for teachers and will also raise funds to help rebuild the school. In addition, this activity is also a good example for the next generation of students to emulate. Police to send Hang Pich to court this afternoon in case of encroachment on more than 3 hectares of Preah Tonle pond
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 28, 2019, the criminal police of the Por Senchey District Inspectorate will send a man named Hang Pich to court in connection with the case of erecting a pole to encroach on the Preah Tonle Wat Kork Panchan pond area of nearly 4 hectares.
During the interrogation, Mr. Hang Pich told the authorities that he followed the reliance of Mr. Heng Chesta, the owner of the newly opened Heng Chesta Company for more than 6 months, by sending 40,000 money from Mr. Heng Chesta through Wing. Pay for food, workers throw and plant poles at the location of the river pond only.
Mr. Hang Pich said that he had never known Mr. Heng Chesta before, met him by chance at a restaurant and had known each other for more than a month, but Mr. Heng Chesta Rely on him to bring money to pay for the food of the workers who are working on the post at the above location.
Mr. Hang Pich said that Mr. Heng Chesta sent money through Wing Value 3 times and received twice directly from Mr. Sok Sam Ath, 42 years old, a brigadier general in the bodyguard command unit, brought the money to him. To pay the workers two more times.
Another source leaked that after Mr. Hang Pich was arrested, some people intervened to take $ 4,000 to escape the release of Mr. Hang Pich, but this intervention was leaked according to the source. And.
It should be noted that the case of an unknown person using his children to erect a fence post to encircle the land of Wat Kork Panchan, with an area of nearly 4 hectares, worth nearly 20 million dollars, recently, now the authorities know the identity of the above person after Detained a man who went to participate in throwing the pole and standing guard the pole where they threw the pagoda land by order of their boss.
Recently, a group of nearly 10 people took a pole to encroach on the pond of Wat Kork Panchan, more than 3 hectares, located in Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, and set up a stand. The feet are there to protect the poles and the ground, which they claim to follow their master's orders.
After such a case, the villagers erupted in reaction, and on July 23, 2019, the authorities of Po Sen Chey district went down to remove the cement post, including detaining two people for questioning. An unrelated man was later released, detaining only one person, Hang Pich.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, sent a message of condolences to the family of Ms. Seng Siyut, Senator and Secretary of the Education, Youth, Sports, Fine Arts and Tourism Committee, who passed away at the age of 71 due to illness. .
