Cambodian-Thai medical team shows some symptoms and factors that cause 3 serious diseases!
(Phnom Penh): A team of doctors from Thailand and Cambodia have jointly identified a number of factors that cause people to develop three serious diseases, including: obstruction of the bile duct, pancreatitis and liver cancer.
Currently, these three diseases occur in many Cambodians due to their lack of awareness of prevention, prevention of these three diseases and lack of proper treatment. Therefore, Royal Phnom Penh Hospital in collaboration with Bangkok Hospital organized a workshop on "Bile obstruction, pancreatitis and gallbladder surgery and treatment of liver cancer" on 27 July. 2019.
The purpose of this workshop is to provide Cambodian people with a better understanding of how to prevent these diseases and how to treat them effectively, and to allow them to participate freely and for free.
According to the doctor, the measures to prevent this disease are: Frequent visits to the hospital for medical check-ups, avoid or stop smoking, alcohol or eating foods that cause a lot of fat.
"The disease is treated surgically or through piercings, which reduces the patient's pain and shortens hospital stays, and the success rate is higher," he said.
He said that for people with gallstones, if there is no pain or no health problems, there is no need for surgery, but to monitor the health.
Dr. Kham Sophea, a specialist in the digestive system, said that in order to avoid these diseases, people should find out more through the technology in mobile phones, search through the Internet by creating more self-awareness.
Doctors called on people to reduce alcohol consumption and smoking to prevent gallstones and pancreatitis. On the other hand, if people have symptoms such as: itching, itchy skin, yellow eyes and a little abdominal pain, please come to the hospital immediately for timely treatment.
Dr. Chea Chandy, a liver specialist, said that liver cancer is common in Cambodia and so far we do not have the right treatment. Liver cancer cannot be treated with radiation like other cancers.
The doctor said that the treatment of liver cancer by surgery and radiotherapy is the treatment with heat, which burns the cancer and makes the tumor and heal. Another type of treatment is vascular therapy.
"Especially for non-viral hepatitis, it is caused by alcohol consumption, which causes chronic hepatitis, this chronic inflammation that causes cancer, and the prevention is to prevent this chronic disease," he said. .
Samdech Heng Samrin Sends Condolences to the Family of Senate Senator Seng Siyut
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, on July 28, 2019, sent a message of condolences to the family of Mrs. Seng Siyut, a senator who passed away at the age of 71 due to a disease.
Samdech Heng Samrin stated that the death of Ms. Seng Siyut was the loss of an exemplary human resource who sacrificed her physical and mental strength to serve the country diligently and be loved by her relatives. Samdech, please pray for the soul of Mrs. Seng Siyut to be happy in eternal bliss, not to be wasted.
Please be informed that Ms. Seng Siyut passed away at the age of 71 due to illness at 10:30 am on Saturday, July 27, 2019. Her body was laid to rest at Wat Botum Vatey, Sangkat Chaktomuk, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh. Cremation ceremony will take place on Monday, July 29, 2019 at 08:30 in the morning at the field of Wat Botumvati.
The following is a message of condolence from Samdech Heng Samrin: Advisor to Samdech Heng Samrin encourages students to learn Chinese to help promote economic relations between Cambodia and China
(Kampong Cham): Advisor to Samdech Heng Samrin and Vice Chancellor of the University of Management and Economics (UME), Mr. Muon Veasna encouraged students to learn more Chinese in English to help promote social and economic relations between Cambodia and China. China is also the world's largest economy.
Mr. Muon Veasna said so in the seminar on the scholarship exam to study in China, held on the morning of July 28, 2019 at the University of Management and Economics, Kampong Cham.
He said that in the past, Cambodian students were only interested in learning English, but because of China's growing economy while Cambodia was peaceful and had good relations with China, students had to work hard to learn Chinese. More in English.
According to Muon Veasna, the world now uses more Chinese than English because there are more Chinese in the world and the world free market economy is led by the United States, China and other countries. Japan.
He said that according to economists, in the next 10 years, China could become the world's number one economic power.
Mr. Muon Veasna continued that only education is the way to lead people to success for a better life, and learning is never too late for those who want to have knowledge.
Two American youths arrested in Rome for stabbing Italian police officer
Two 19-year-old Americans have been arrested in Rome for the murder of an Italian police officer, Italian authorities have said. This is according to a quote from the Chinese newspaper CGTN on Sunday afternoon, July 28, 2019.
According to Italian police, after checking video, security cameras and the testimony of some witnesses, the two suspects were finally found and arrested in their hotel room during the night. Same Friday. However, US authorities have not yet commented on the arrest. Fisheries officials turn a blind eye to traders destroying fish stocks in Bassac River
(Kandal): Many residents of Kampong Pring village, Sitbo commune, Takhmao city, Kandal province, suspect that fisheries officials in this area may open their hands to the group of dragons, draggers and boats to destroy fish resources along the Bassac River. During the off-season.
These drag nigam or chaiya and yangkao groups are limited to towing boats from Kampong Pring ferry to Kbal Koh ferry. They dragged back and forth, but at that point, the water turned poisonous, there was no fish left for many years. This group acts both dry and rainy, never resting. According to sources from the people.
Sadly, the people have lost confidence in the fishery and are willing to close their eyes, sadly, the fish resources are destroyed from year to year. Director of Kandal Provincial Public Works Department calls on all truck operators and citizens to come in for a clean environment
(Kandal): Mr. Moeng Youleng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province, said that clean roads, clean villages, clean cities, only with the participation of all people.
He said this during the event, he took the officials of all public departments to clean the streets in Takhmao, with the participation of the directors of several departments in Kandal province on the morning of July 28, 2019.
As for the people in Takhmao City, the 6 Sangkats are clearing the roads in their respective Sangkats. He said that the clean-up of this road is to remind other people how to make the city a clean city, no garbage, no dirt, the city is an attractive city for tourists. Retrieved 3 rumduol in the future.
At the same time, he also educated and instructed the people who sell on the street, he called on people who are engaged in the business of transporting land, sand and other construction materials, especially the 9 sand depots in Takhmao City, please do not transport To be overweight and to pack properly according to technical standards, not to fall soil, sand on the road, and if they do not comply, the department will cooperate with the traffic police to fine according to the law.
He stated that he serves the people but does not serve individuals who destroy the environment and the beauty of the city.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith reacted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen sent his grandson to board the plane on Friday evening, while the Council of Ministers met on Friday morning, but the reporter shouted that just to give his grandson a meeting of the Council of Ministers.
Through his Facebook page on July 28, 2019, Mr. Khieu Kanharith also took to call a reporter of Radio Free Asia as a reporter in the mosquito net. He said that reporters in the mosquito net like this must try to find information, if there is no information must also compose information, unlike professional news.
The Minister of Information's reaction came after Radio Free Asia on July 27, 2019, reported that Samdech Techo Hun Sen on Friday evening, July 26, sent his eldest granddaughter back to study abroad. Willing to postpone the weekly cabinet meeting to a later date.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith stated: "Samdech Hun Sen sent his grandson to board the plane on Friday evening, when the Council of Ministers normally met on Friday morning, but reporters from inside the mosquito net shouted that only for the grandson to raise the committee meeting." Minister.
He continued, "Know how to shout like that? And there are always believers? On the other hand, not only every Friday, the cabinet must come to the meeting, if there is no work plan, it must ask for the approval of the whole government. "Journalists in the net must try to find information. If there is no information, they must also compose news, unlike professional journalists."
Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the evening of July 26, 2019 posted on his Facebook page about taking time to send his eldest granddaughter back to study abroad. Samdech Techo confirmed that the direct departure was due to Samdech Kittipritthbandit, the grandmother and Mrs. Hun Mana, who was a busy mother, so Samdech came to send directly.
