(Phnom Penh): Copyright is the owner's right to receive legal protection for his work, which is created by the intellectual and emotional nature of the author.
The Law on Copyright and Related Rights aims to ensure respect for copyright and related rights and to protect the cultural products of authors, performers, phonogram producers and broadcasters in order to ensure the order in which a legitimate business is conducted. Which are those cultural products to contribute to the development of the cultural sector.
What kind of works and rights of authors are protected?
The Legal Awareness Program, which is a collaboration between Fresh News and the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, brings the following topics related to "copyright" to the public:
In accordance with the Law on Copyright and Related Rights, it is stipulated that the work of the author is divided into two categories: original and sequel.
According to Article 3 of the Law on Copyright and related rights, works protected by this law are as follows:
2: Performance of the performer: a. Works of Cambodian performers b. The work of a non-Khmer performer, but the performance • took place in the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia • recorded as a phonogram under the protection of the law or • not yet recorded as a phonogram but Broadcast on television under the protection of the law.
3: Phonogram Note: a. The phonogram of the producer is of Khmer nationality. Phonogram recorded for the first time in the Kingdom of Cambodia. Fonogram recorded for the first time in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
4: Television broadcasts: a. Broadcasting of a broadcasting unit headquartered in the Kingdom of Cambodia. Broadcasting from broadcast media located in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
However, there are some works that do not allow protection through copyright, such as: the Constitution, laws, royal decrees, sub-decrees and official regulations, or proclamations, decisions, certificates, directives issued by state organizations or Make judgments or other court judgments, etc. For this type of work, any person has the right to copy to study and understand.
Next week, we will continue to elaborate, focusing on the scope of rights, conditions and procedures for legal protection of authors.
(Pailin): The Pailin Provincial Delegation led by Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by Mr. Cheng Nhan, Deputy Governor, and the leaders of provincial departments, units and professional institutions discussed with Chan Borei Province, Thailand to strengthen ties and Better cooperation between provinces bordering the two countries (Pailin + Chan Borey).
Mr. Phan Chanthul thanked the Chan Borei Provincial Administration for the warm welcome of the Pailin Provincial Delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss the cooperation on the border between the two countries in strengthening good relations and friendship. Together to strengthen cooperation in all fields, especially trade, industry and labor along the border between the Kingdom of Cambodia and Thailand to be even better.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul also requested the Thai side to continue to cooperate on a number of issues, such as: speeding up the construction of bridges across the border, the problem of illegal Cambodian migrant workers and cross-border crimes and agricultural exports. And cross-border trade between Chan Borei-Pailin Province, especially facilitating the export of mango, lentils and Pailin lentils to Thailand.
In response, Mr. Vithurat Srinam, Governor of Chan Borei Province, Kingdom of Thailand, promised to cooperate and resolve all requests of the Pailin Provincial Administration within the jurisdiction of the province, while he promised to bring all the requests. All of this is discussed with relevant officials and leaders, as well as the Royal Government of Thailand to find possibilities and solutions to enhance cooperation between the two countries.
On that occasion, Mr. Vithurat Srinam also commended the Pailin Provincial Administration for its past efforts to strengthen cooperation with the border provinces of the two countries in order to maintain security and order along the border and serve the interests of the people and the country. Both fairly and honestly.
It should be noted that the agricultural products of farmers in Pailin province, such as: potatoes, corn, mango, lentils and longan fruit, Pailin, etc., depend on the Thai market and there is always a problem with the price at the time of harvest, which is a concern of the provincial authorities. . North Korea releases Russian fishing vessel after nearly half a month detention
The Russian Embassy in North Korea issued a statement on Saturday, July 27, due to coordinated efforts by the Russian Foreign Ministry, the fishing vessel Xianghailin-8 was released after being stranded. North Korea arrested and detained Wonsan with 17 people on board on July 17.
(Phnom Penh): The golf tournament for the "Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh Award" 2019 officially opened on the morning of July 28, 2019 at the Grand Golf Course in Phnom Penh with the leadership of business officials And more than 200 national and international athletes participated.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and was attended by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense He is also the President of the Golf Federation of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Bora, Secretary General of the Federation, confirmed that this year's Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh Award was attended by 212 national and international business leaders and athletes. The tournament will run for one day only, and in the evening of the same day, the federation will hold a prize-giving ceremony at the Phnom Penh Grand Golf Course.
It should be noted that this event is organized every year to inspire golf activities and promote the development of the Olympic sport to grow in order to select athletes to participate in international competitions, especially travel. Towards the 32nd SEA Games in 2023, which Cambodia will host.
