Stung Treng Provincial Armed Forces Cracked Down on Two Tuk-Tuk Trucks in Sesan District and Burned It
(Stung Treng): The Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie, in cooperation with the Police, Forestry Administration and local authorities, cracked down on two tuk-tuks in Sesan district and burned them on the spot.
According to Fresh News, the operation was led by Brigadier General Ieng Vandy, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander, after receiving from General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie. Chairman of the National Committee for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes.
During the recent operation, the National Committee for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes has made a series of arrests, sent them to court for legal action, and confiscated the means of committing crimes and set them on fire. And the place as well. Kid Park Children's Entertainment Center officially opens its first branch at AEON Mall
The inauguration ceremony of Kid Park Kids Entertainment Center took place on July 27, 2019 at Aeon Mall Phnom Penh, 1st floor, with the participation of Mr. Meas Sopheak, Managing Director of Kids Park Kids Entertainment Center and management. And many employees as well.
Mr. Meas Sopheak, Managing Director, said, "Our children's entertainment center is focused on design and innovation in accordance with modern technology, modern technology and ensure high hygiene and safety. "Our children's recreation center has professional staff to provide professional service and go through proper training."
Kid Park Children's Entertainment Center is open from 9am to 10pm and welcomes children from 2 to 12 years old and 60cm to 145cm tall from Monday to Sunday. The children's entertainment center is also open for birthday parties.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the banking and financial sector continues to develop strongly and actively participates in promoting economic growth.
Mr. Chea Chanto made this statement on July 27, 2019 in the program to summarize the work results of the first half and the work direction for the second half of 2019 of the National Bank.
He added that in order to maintain strong financial stability, the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has continued to strengthen risk-based and prospective inspections, the introduction of macro and micro measures, consumer protection and financial awareness of the public.
He stressed that in order to support economic and financial growth, financial infrastructure has been gradually developed to be more efficient, especially the modernization of payment systems to improve security and reduce operating costs.
He said that the gross payment system (RTGS) is being developed to facilitate and reduce the risk of large interbank payments, especially payments in the financial markets.
The National Bank of Cambodia is developing a retail payment system via QR code and electronic payment system. With the benefit of financial technology, the National Bank of Cambodia has established an appropriate regulatory framework to regulate the use of financial technology to better support the financial environment and maintain financial stability.
He said that domestic and foreign money transfer transactions, check clearing and credit transfer orders of government institutions and banking and financial institutions were running smoothly and efficiently.
Minister of Agriculture instructs professional officers and agriculture departments in 24 provinces to regularly inspect farmers' growing conditions
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on July 27, 2019, instructed the officials and Departments of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in 24 provinces to inspect the cultivation status of farmers. Regularly provide support and need to find appropriate measures for farmers.
Such instructions were made when Mr. Veng Sakhon, accompanied by the Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province and his colleagues, inspected the situation of rice cultivation in the rainy season and talked and intervened to distribute Rumduol rice seeds to farmers in Namen Kheng village, Anhcheum commune. And Rieu village, Mong Rieu commune, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province on the afternoon of July 27, 2019.
According to Mr. Heng Piseth, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Tbong Khmum Province, as of today in Anhcheum commune due to lack of rain and lack of water source, the rain-fed rice crop of the farmers has withered and provided. Opportunity for weeds to attack severely affected and completely damaged 323 hectares of rain-fed rice crops of 810 families.
Mr. Heng Piseth's report added that in Rieu village, Mong Rieu commune, a similar situation affected and completely damaged more than 144 hectares of land of 237 farmers.
Considering that the rain has continued to fall at a good level and in order to improve the situation and alleviate the damage of the farmers, the Minister intervened with the General Department of Agriculture to transport 50 varieties of Romduol rice. Tons through the Cambodian food reserve system from Tuol Samrong rice seed farm in Battambang province for immediate distribution to farmers in both communes to help him to plant and harvest in the rainy season.
He also donated some diesel for pumping water in case of water source. In addition, the Minister also instructed the professional officers and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in the 24 provinces and cities to regularly inspect the farming conditions of farmers and to provide support and necessary measures to our farmers. Challenges, especially the drought.
Ms. Khieu Tep Rainsy Kanharith encourages all women to have hope, try to achieve their goals and do not be discouraged when the first failure
(Kampong Cham): Ms. Khieu Tep Rainsy Kanharith, Honorary President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development of the Ministry of Information, instructed all young women and men to have hope, try to achieve their goals and ask not to be broken. Despair when encountering failure for the first time.
This statement was made at a seminar on "Women in Hope" held at Chi Her High School, Chi Her Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province recently, chaired by Ms. Khieu Tep Rainsy Kanharith and Dr. Soeur Socheata, Undersecretary of State. Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
During the ceremony, Ms. Khieu Tep Rainsy Kanharith stated that it is true that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has worked day and night for the peace, development and education of the country. A priority area for growth, human resource development and the national economy.
She continued that in which the training of young women or women is really necessary and important for the country, because women are a strong driving force on the support of social stability, especially the Royal Government of Cambodia has significantly promoted and encouraged Women become leaders, smart decision makers in the service of the nation, the motherland and the people.
She said that the workshop of the Brilliant Women's Association under the theme of Women and Hope really shows that young people, especially women, can learn about the struggles, struggles in life to achieve a brighter life with the expected hope. Giving and providing opportunities and training for women means training to build human resources for oneself, society and family.
At the same time, Ms. Khieu Tep Rainsy Kanharith also instructed all young women to have hope, try to achieve their goals and ask not to be discouraged when the first failure. 1 and struggle until you get the next result and believe in yourself that you can do it all the time.
Ms. Khieu Tep Rainsy Kanharith emphasized that failure is the best life lesson for the future life of women and hope brings happiness in peace, progress that Cambodia has achieved.
According to Ms. Hang Chuon Narita, Vice President of the Association, the Association has already co-organized this program three times, including the first time in Kampong Chhnang, the second time in Kampong Speu and the third time in Kandal province effectively and effectively. Proud of receiving support and interest from students on the topic of sharing experiences, knowledge, skills, changing habits to become a successful youth for life in the future.
In particular, Dr. Soeur Socheata said that women in peace, progress, stability, Cambodian women have played a very important role for the development of all areas, especially in education, women in leadership in various institutions of the Royal Government.
She said that the workshop will be able to provide indispensable values for young people, especially for Jiher High School students, not only the courage, goodwill, determination of women in social work, study At school as well as in the family.
Dr. Soeur Socheata said that the education sector in Cambodia under the mechanism of education reform, with Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, has really responded to the training of youth resources as a successor. Bamboo is a successor with energy, determination and development.
She said that a country develops peace, national pride due to responsible training, equity, because national development work in all fields always has the active participation of young people, especially women.
On that occasion, Ms. Khieu Tep Rainsy Kanharith also handed over $ 1,000 to Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, to Chi Her High School to alleviate the school's shortage, while Ms. Chhay Chanrithy Solida also supported the program with 500 budget. US dollars as well. Not only that, the Charleston University Alumni Association of Cambodia has provided study materials to students who participated in this workshop program.
(Phnom Penh): Road and road infrastructure is one of the four priority tasks that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has set out in building and developing the country since its liberation from the Pol Pot genocidal regime. To this day.
Currently, many national roads have been improved and rebuilt, connecting Phnom Penh to the 24 provinces intertwined. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this week spent two nights and three days in the northwest and northeast of the country inspecting some of the major national roads that have been completed and are under construction, including National Road 55. National Road No. 5, National Road No. 58 and National Road No. 7.
Speaking to reporters during the inspection of the road construction, Mr. Sun Chanthol emphasized that roads and bridges are important economic vessels for Cambodia, and because of the value of these roads and bridges, the Royal Government of Cambodia led Samdech Techo worked hard to build this road and bridge.
The Minister of Public Works and Transport emphasized, "Roads are like our arteries, without which we can not survive. Therefore, this road is very important to participate in building our motherland, making the transportation of goods cheaper, saving time transporting both goods and tourists, our people. It is very important that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has given one of the four priorities in building the nation, roads, electricity, water, human resources.
Mr. Sun Chanthol affirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia will continue its efforts to build roads and bridges to attract investors and facilitate travel and transportation of goods.
In terms of road and bridge construction, most of the funding comes from friendly countries such as China, Japan, South Korea and development partners such as the World Bank and the Asian Development Bank. Borrowing money to build this road has always caused some Cambodians to express their concern that Cambodia is heavily indebted and others have said that the Royal Government is incapable of having a national budget to build roads.
Responding to these concerns and suggestions, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated that Cambodia does not have the budget to build roads. But the national budget is set aside to meet other needs, such as the provision of salaries for civil servants for development in the defense, education and health sectors.
Mr. Sun Chanthol further stated that this loan is clearly controlled by the Royal Government of Cambodia, not to lend more than 21 percent of Cambodia's gross domestic product.
Mr. Sun Chanthol stated, "We borrow money, but we protect the loan very well. The Ministry of Economy and Finance, he manages very well. Today, the loan rate on our GDP is only 21 percent." "If we divide the loan we borrow with our GDP, it is 21 percent, so many countries in the world that the loan rate compares to their GDP is 100 percent, 200 percent."
Mr. Sun Chanthol also compared the benefits between borrowing money from friendly countries and development partner organizations to build roads with not borrowing money to build roads and leave Cambodia's roads in a difficult situation.
Mr. Chanthol claimed that borrowing money to build roads and bridges was very profitable for the economy.
