Ms. Ngin Lina, Director General of the General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information of the Ministry of Environment, emphasized that this campaign is designed to encourage people everywhere, especially people living in urban areas to understand and participate in reducing the use of plastic bags and awareness. The impact of plastic waste aims to ensure the protection of public health, the environment and the beauty of the city.
Mr. Nak Neron, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, considered that today's event contributes to the dissemination of comprehensive knowledge to reduce plastic waste in Cambodia on a voluntary basis, as well as to encourage and encourage traders to stop providing plastic bags to contribute to improving livelihoods and reducing the impact. To the environment, welfare, people, hygiene, aesthetics of the city.
Please note that the amount of urban waste generated in Cambodia is more than 10,000 tons per day, people living in the capital and major cities are estimated to generate 1 kg of garbage per day and siblings. People living in rural areas generate about half a kilo of garbage a day. In total, a year, the amount of waste that Cambodia generates is about 4 million tons, of which 20% is plastic bag waste.
In order to successfully reduce the use of plastic bags, Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized that the participation of the people is very important and urged the people to implement the 3Rs to contribute to reducing the use of plastic bags. Recycle plastic bags or use plastic bag substitutes and recycle plastic bags.
