Senior officials of the National Bank of Cambodia urge people to be very careful with the lending company "Phnom Penh Credit" and ask the authorities to take legal action
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kith Sovannarith, Deputy Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, has warned the public to be wary of the online lending company "Phnom Penh Credit", which does not have a license and license from the National Bank of Cambodia. The company dares to advertise online lending in violation of the law.
Speaking to Fresh News on the morning of July 27, 2019, Mr. Kith Sovannarith stressed that "On behalf of the National Bank of Cambodia, I would like to ask the people to be careful about the Phnom Penh Credit Company, which operates a lending business or "Online loans without a license or permit from the National Bank of Cambodia."
He added that in addition, the company "Credit Phnom Penh" dare to use the image of the management of the National Bank and the Microfinance Association to deceive people.
"The National Bank of Cambodia does not support or license this Phnom Penh credit company and ask the authorities to take legal action against this company," he said.
