Today, traffic police inspected 10,409 motorcyclists, forcing 4,393 to wear helmets
(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police has launched a nationwide campaign to promote helmet wearing for a full month, and on July 27, 2019, the traffic police force in 22 capitals and provinces inspected a number of motorcyclists. Of the 10,409, 4,393 were forced to wear helmets, accounting for 42 percent. This is according to the report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department, which was obtained by Fresh News.
