(Kampong Thom): Mr. Thong Khon, Chairman of Baray and Taing Kork District Assistance Working Group, Kampong Thom Province, held a number of meetings to review the work that the leaders and party members of the above two districts have implemented in the past and set out the direction. Some new work for the leadership and party members to continue.
The meeting was held on July 27, 2019 at the Samdech Techo Hun Sen 5 Development Center in Baray District, which was attended by about 200 local CPP leaders and members.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot, President of the People's Party of Taing Kork District and Mr. Hak Mov Seng, Representative of the President of the People's Party of Baray District, reported on some of the work done by both parties in the past and the direction of implementation.
After listening to and evaluating some of the above work, Mr. Thong Khon set out some work directions for the leaders and party members to continue to pay attention, including:
* Continue to pay attention to the prevention and control of dengue fever in Baray and Taing Kork districts and to be vigilant against the disease "Pest African" pigs that may occur.
Strengthen the structure and organization of the Baray district party, Tang Kork district and the 18 commune parties of the two districts.
Strengthen the management and expansion of party members in both quantity and quality, especially focusing on the youth and continue to update party members to clearly manage party members and migrants.
* Continue to control public opinion, grasp the emotional, psychological, political politics of the local people and manage the activities of the former opposition group well.
* Efforts must be made to strengthen internal unity between the leaders and party members, and must continue to participate in activities to visit and support the people, especially the vulnerable, the elderly, the families of people affected by natural disasters - fires, etc.
At this point, Mr. Thong Khon praised the efforts of Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Mr. Oung Saroeun and his team, who often visit and bring donations to the victims often in the past.
* Must continue to gather and eat solidarity noodles with the people.
* Must continue to work to facilitate the cultivation of the people and the construction of necessary achievements at the local level, such as the restoration of canals, dams, irrigation systems, wells, roads, etc.
* Make it easier for people to live, have jobs, earn income and have a better life.
