(Kampong Thom): The construction of the sluice gate across Stung Stong, located in Bot Trang village, Msakrang commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province, is 95% completed, which has made the people along the river very happy after suffering Difficulties due to lack of water to use and grow crops in recent years.
In order to inspect, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on July 26, 2019, continued to inspect the water condition and construction of dams and sluice gates across Stung Stong directly. This activity was also accompanied by the Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Thom Province, as well as professional officers.
According to the report from the inspection team, the construction work of the above construction started from March 2019 until now, it has reached 95%.
In particular, the water level of the river is gradually improving with the subsequent rains.
Please be informed that Stung Stong receives water source from the upper part of the pool on September 30. When the above construction is completed, the water challenge in Stung Stong for daily use and people's cultivation will be solved.
On that occasion, the Minister further introduced the work to be completed to ensure the quality of long-term construction for now and in the future.
It should be reminded that during the dry season, facing difficulties in accessing water for the people living along the Stoung River, the Minister instructed the Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Water Resources to dig 16 ponds at the bottom of the river to solve the above challenges. To the people.
Lt. Gen. Run Rath Veasna: Tourist police must be competent enough to serve tourists
(Siem Reap): Lt. Gen. Run Rath Veasna, Director of the Tourism Police Department of the General Commission of the National Police, said on July 26, 2019 that all tourism police officers must be competent enough to serve tourists at their destinations. That it is standing on the defensive.
Lt. Gen. Run Rath Veasna's remarks were co-chaired by Lt. Gen. Muong Khim, Deputy Director of the Central Department of Judicial Police at the Closing Ceremony of the Second Intervention and Procedure Training Course for Judicial Police Officers at the Police Unit. Tourism in Siem Reap with about 70 police officers participating in this training.
Lt. Gen. Run Rath Veasna also highlighted that he will make every effort to ensure that all police officers must have more knowledge, because tourism police officers have been playing an important role in providing services to tourists, especially in By temples and major resorts in Cambodia.
The director of the department emphasized that it is very important for the tourism police to know foreign languages. Admittedly, the shape is a bit difficult because some police officers are so old that it is difficult to study.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Run Rath Veasna also instructed tourism police officers throughout the country to wear appropriate clothing, especially to abide by the set uniforms, to cut their hair short and to use good words, especially when there are tourists. Come and ask or help on something.
In addition, he expressed his sincere appreciation and encouragement to all tourism police forces who have worked hard to overcome all obstacles in fulfilling their duties to provide security and safety to national and international guests as well. Participate in strengthening and promoting the spirit of respect for the law.
Lt. Gen. Run Rath Veasna expressed his strong hope that all officers will use their wisdom and spirit to fulfill their duties and responsibilities with good cooperation and high sense of responsibility in maintaining order and safety for national and international tourists. Who came to visit in Cambodia.
