Minister of Commerce praises progress of Cambodia-Belarus bilateral cooperation (Video inside) (Siem Reap): Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak expressed his pride and appreciation for the results of economic and trade cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia And the Republic of Belarus that has played an important role in diversifying employment opportunities and economic growth in both countries.
The Minister made the remarks while presiding over the meeting with HE Gennady Svidersky, First Deputy Minister of the Ministry of Industry of Belarus at the opening ceremony of the third meeting of the Joint Committee on Trade and Cooperation. Cambodian Economy and Belarus held at the Sokha Siem Reap Convention and Conference Center on the morning of July 26, 2019.
In his welcoming remarks, Minister Pan Sosak briefed on the progress of Cambodia's economic growth and the Royal Government's investment facilitation efforts, which created opportunities for Belarusian investors, such as the successful case of the Belarus-Mekong tractor manufacturer. $ 4 million and has been distributing high quality tractors in the market and providing employment to many Cambodian workers.
He also encouraged senior officials of the two countries to continue discussions on agriculture, technology, industry, tourism, education and other fields, using skills and experience to develop a new action plan that identifies challenges to be strengthened and expanded. Bilateral economic and trade relations to further improve.
On that occasion, Mr. Jennady Schwartzky emphasized the commitment of the Belarusian government to continue to encourage investment in Cambodia in agriculture, industry, health and new technologies to create opportunities for the people and contribute to the development of Cambodia's economic growth with the Royal Government. Government.
In addition, the Deputy Minister of Belarus also promised to promote the transfer of knowledge and modern technology to reduce the skills gap and support the development of light and heavy industries in Cambodia.
Please be informed that the purpose of today's meeting is to monitor the progress of work under the framework of the 2014 agreement and find solutions to challenges to increase trade volume and strengthen economic cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Belarus. In-depth and comprehensive after the second committee meeting was held in June 2017 in Minsk, Republic of Belarus.
