(Stung Treng): Two Cambodian military officers standing guard at the O'Alay border area in Siem Bang district, Stung Treng province, were swept away by a tornado while on their way to treat malaria on July 24. 2019 ago.
The two of them went to seek treatment for malaria, but unfortunately, while driving a motorbike to the road between the bridge under construction at Oma, Street 101, Nhum Sou village, Thmor Keo commune, Siem Pang district, Stung Treng province, due to strong water flow. The road collapsed and the water swept away the two young fighters.
On the morning of July 26, 2019, the bodies of two military officers were found floating about 10 kilometers from the scene, just below Koh Tonsay, Siem Pang district.
The two unfortunate fighters were named Sok Sovandy and Pinidali. They served in the 3rd Squadron, Artillery Battalion, 1st Light Infantry Division, stationed in O'Alay. Both fighters are soldiers who just passed the military service exam in 2018.
The victim, Phin Dali, was the head of the intelligence team. He was born in Tani market, Phnom Kong commune, Angkor Chey district, Kampot province, and Sok Sovandy was born in Koh Takov village, Russey commune, Kampong Trach district, Kampot province.
