Director General of Taxation urges all tax branches throughout the capital to have a bank to facilitate taxpayers
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, urged all tax branches throughout the capital and province should have a bank in it to make it easier for those who To pay taxes, do not make it difficult for them to pay taxes for a long time, which is why they no longer want to cooperate as tax officials to pay taxes to the state.
Mr. Kong Vibol said this on the morning of July 26, 2019, when he presided over the inauguration ceremony of the auditorium of Meanchey Tax Branch.
Mr. Kong Vibol said, "Every tax branch in the capital and province should have a bank in it so that those who come to pay taxes easily when the tax is paid in the bank at once to make it easier. "People who come to pay taxes do not make it difficult for them to pay taxes for a long time, which makes them no longer want to cooperate as tax officials to pay taxes to the state."
At the same time, he encouraged all tax branches to make efforts to modernize their branches to make it more comfortable for both tax officials and taxpayers.
The General Department of Taxation also urges all tax officials to continue their efforts to collect taxes for the state in accordance with the plan as in previous years, and in Meanchey district has a lot of potential.
He also instructed the Chairman-Deputy Chairman of Meanchey District Tax Branch and all tax officials to continue to pay attention and work hard and provide good services to taxpayers in order to facilitate the effective payment of tax, accountability and Transparency and called on all officials to take care of all new equipment and office equipment and achievements for the benefit of long-term use.
