(Sihanoukville): The use of illegal fishing gear, encroachment on mangrove / flooded forests, land reclamation, and the removal of fishing grounds are serious acts of destruction leading to the destruction of natural resources and fish. To solve this problem, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, urged the relevant institutions to pay attention to the crackdown in time.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun introduced this on the occasion of releasing freshwater and juvenile fish into a natural lake in Prey Nob district on the morning of July 26, 2019.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun emphasized that through the National Fish Day on July 1, 2019, it will inspire people, civil servants, the Armed Forces and the private sector to participate in maintaining, protecting, conserving and increasing the stocks of natural fisheries resources to improve their livelihoods. Live of local people.
Mr. Nen Chamroeun, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Sihanouk Province, said that this National Fish Day, July 1, 2019, organized the release of 50,000 fish and 20 kilograms of fish to preserve the richness of the fish. More.
At the same time, Mr. Nen Chamroeun requested the fishermen not to use mosquito nets to catch fish or use electric tools, not to destroy the flooded forest, which is a fish sanctuary, and urged the people, local authorities, professional officials, development partners to participate. Preserve, protect and conserve all these natural fish resources to ensure sustainability and improve the livelihoods of local farmers.
It should be noted that every year, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, in cooperation with the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, holds a series of releases of fish fry and fish species in natural reservoirs in Sihanoukville.
