(Phnom Penh): Former Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister and Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong has confirmed that a report by the US Department of Defense and the publication of foreign newspapers alleging that Cambodia has authorized a Chinese military base at Sihanoukville's Ream Naval Base is A campaign against Cambodia to confuse the international community.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong said that according to the US Department of Defense's Indo-Pacific Strategic Report, it raised its concerns for fear of China seeking to build a military base in Cambodia. As a result of this report, its newspaper cited and published other foreign newspapers that countries have misunderstood Cambodia.
The former Cambodian diplomat added, "And I also told her that if there is a military base in Cambodia, it can not be hidden in Cambodia, everything is transparent, and this transparency is beyond Some other countries as well. "Therefore, Cambodia does not have any secret agreement to have a military base with China."
