(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has chosen to ride a bicycle to check the quality of the road under construction or completed before accepting from the company. Cycling to see the road has made some people express admiration, but some people see it as a thing to look good or to attract attention.
During a cycling inspection of National Road No. 7 in Tbong Khmum province on July 24, 2019, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol confirmed that the decision to choose this method of cycling to see the road is not to make it different or To draw that attention. But riding this bike made him check the quality of the road more clearly.
Despite public opinion, Mr. Sun Chanthol confirmed that he would continue to inspect the road by cycling or walking to get the company to pay attention to road construction and show the company that the Ministry is not indifferent. For checking the quality of the road they built.
On the occasion of inspecting the quality of the construction of National Road No. 7, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also confirmed the public opinion that during the construction of the road refused to inspect until the road was built. Mr. Sun Chanthol confirmed that the quality inspection of the road was carried out from the initial construction phase to the completion.
The Minister further stated that in order to ensure that the road is of good quality in accordance with this contract, he had to check and check in detail before signing the road from the company. The senior minister claimed that if the road was not built properly, it would not sign the agreement.
(Prey Veng): People who are members of the rice farming community in Prey Veng province agree to sell their rice to an international standard mill, which is recognized as safe, organic and organically produced for safe consumption. Health.
This agreement was confirmed through the contract signing ceremony between Prey Veng Provincial Agricultural Community and Chhun Thom Rice Mill based in Svay Antor District, Prey Veng Province, held at Prey Veng Provincial Hall on the evening of July 25, 2019 at Prey Veng Provincial Hall. .
Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, said that throughout Prey Veng province, 275 thousand hectares of rice production area, the annual rice yield is about 1.4 million tons. The average rice export is nearly 1 million tons.
Mr. Chhun Thom, the owner of the rice mill, promised to buy community rice from 10,000 tons at a price of 1,600 riel per kilogram, wet rice or more of the total rice yield of the community.
Please note that this program is supported by the Rural Development Bank, and in addition to buying rice in the province has a dryer.
