Phnom Penh International Airport CamControl Officer Inspects Goods at Century Plaza Market, But No Chemicals Found
(Phnom Penh): Camcontrol Phnom Penh International Airport Branch and its subordinates under the leadership of Mr. Khun Simon on July 26, 2019 cooperated with Trade Officers and Laboratory Officers to inspect goods at Century Plaza Market in Khan Por Sen Chey.
Mr. Te Ith Leang, Deputy Director of Camcontrol Phnom Penh International Airport Branch, said that the working group continued to inspect the quality and safety of goods, food and groceries at Sanjury Plaza Market, Po Sen Chey District. He said that the team conducted preliminary experiments on 11 food items, such as pickles of all kinds, vinegar, lemongrass, etc. to find banned chemicals that can affect the health of consumers.
As a result, the team did not find any goods or foodstuffs with banned chemicals and damaged or out of date. In addition, the working group explained to the traders to be aware and pay attention to the quality and safety of the food they sell and face the law.
According to the Deputy Director of Camcontrol Phnom Penh International Airport, the officials explained to the sellers and the people about the storage of packaged goods and the impact caused by defective goods.
