Senior Minister Kun Kim Conducts Disaster Preparedness and Dissemination Meeting in Pursat Province
(Pursat): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, chaired a meeting to review the work of the Pursat Provincial Committee for Disaster Management and disseminate preventive measures on the afternoon of July 25. And disaster response.
The meeting was held at Pursat Provincial Hall with the participation of Mr. Lam Heng Huot, Deputy Chairman of the NEC and Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province and government officials from relevant institutions, armed forces and partner organizations. And 291 municipal, district, commune and sangkat authorities throughout the province.
According to Mr. Mao Thunin's report, after the Royal Government built the third and fifth dams, the river flood can be reduced to some extent. The drought affected more than 46,000 hectares, but emergency services and recent rains did not cause any damage. In 2019, 3 districts experienced 12 strong winds, affecting 118 families, equivalent to 118 houses and 4 schools.
After delivering greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the members of the meeting as well as the people of Pursat province, Senior Minister Kun Kim introduced to the Provincial Disaster Management Committee and Relevant officials make a clear report on the impact and needs of the people to facilitate the ministries and institutions to take action to help the people.
