(Phnom Penh): "Cambodia wants more investment from China in the processing and packaging industry of agricultural products to diversify exports to international markets because we have a lot of unprocessed agricultural products such as mangoes in Kampong Speu, lentils in Pailin. And many other fruit trees. ” This was confirmed by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia to the Officer in charge of Economy and Trade at the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia.
During a meeting with a Chinese delegation led by Li An, Chinese Economic and Trade Advisor (out of term) at the Ministry on Wednesday, July 24, 2019, Pan Sosak briefed the Chinese side on the efforts of Ministry of Commerce to promote agricultural exports to the Chinese market by attending events, exhibitions and presentations at the Cambodian Business Center in the five capitals and provinces of the People's Republic of China.
The Minister requested the Chinese side to facilitate the export of Cambodian agricultural products and to mobilize Chinese companies with the right expertise to invest in Cambodia to further strengthen bilateral trade and investment relations. In addition, the Minister also promised to continue to cooperate with the Chinese side in the field of e-commerce (E-Commerce) to promote the sale and export of Cambodian products to regional and global markets.
In response, Mr. Li An and the delegation thanked the Minister for highlighting the good cooperation between the Ministry of Commerce and the People's Republic of China and the need for Cambodia to strengthen and expand bilateral economic and trade relations in line with the vision. Of the Heads of Government of both countries.
