Nong Heap Finance Microfinance Institution is a subsidiary and subsidiary of Nong Hep Bank of the Republic of Korea. Nong Hep is a bank established in 1961 with 100% Korean capital and is a specialized bank that manages both central and regional government deposits securely with an extensive branch network. Most across the country.
Nong Hep Finance received a license from the National Bank of Cambodia on August 08, 2018 to operate as a microfinance institution after Nong Hep Bank acquired a 100% stake in SAMIC Microfinance Institution Plc. Nong Hep Microfinance Institution currently operates in Phnom Penh and eight provinces, including Kandal, Kampong Speu, Takeo, Kampot, Kep, Sihanoukville, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom.
