16 farming communities in Prey Veng province sign agreement with rice millers on 718 hectares of rice seed production
(Prey Veng): Mr. Kao Thach, General Director of Rural Development Bank and his colleagues on the afternoon of July 25, 2019, attended the signing ceremony of the contract rice production agreement.
Between 16 farming communities in Prey Veng province and Chhun Thom rice mill on the production of 718 hectares of rice seeds, fodder and fragrant rice seeds.
Mr. Kao Thach congratulated the 16 communities and the Chhun Thom Rice Mill for achieving the signing of agricultural agreements under the contract to produce pure rice seeds for the production of rice for sale in the domestic and foreign markets. This ensures the sustainability of the farmers' rice seed market.
Mr. Kao Thach also reminded the farmers that in 2016, in some areas, your rice yield decreased due to weather and some other factors, which caused the price of rice to fall compared to other years. Previously.
He added that, however, the biggest problem that contributes to the decline in rice yields is that some farmers have grown unsightly varieties of rice, resulting in lower yields and poor yields, thus degrading traders. Price. Through this experience, we encourage farmers to grow rice using good quality rice varieties.
At the same time, Mr. Kao Thach strongly believes that through the agreement to supply rice seeds by setting a clear selling price from this Chhun Thom mill and making your production sustainable, in the coming season, farmers in Prey Veng will Pure rice varieties are good for cultivation.
In addition, the Rural Development Bank is ready to provide credit financing to support the farming community for this pure rice seed project with the most favorable interest rates. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Kao Thach.
Mr. Kao Thach confirmed that the Rural Development Bank has already opened its mobile office in Prey Veng, so the community can contact for information and get a loan from the Rural Development Bank's mobile office without going to Phnom Penh. No.
Mr. Kao Thach also requested the rice seed production community to produce high quality and clear standards, in which Mr. Kao Thach requested technical assistance from the Provincial Department of Agriculture to check the quality of rice seeds before supply. The market will continue to request support for this project from local, district and provincial authorities.
He is confident that today's agreement will lead to a professional change in rice cultivation, reduce production costs and increase yields in farmers' production chains.
It should also be noted that throughout Prey Veng province, there are 275,000 hectares of land for rice production and 280,000 hectares of land for both wet and dry rice production. The total rice yield is about 1,400,000 tons, the remaining amount of rice exceeds the demand in the province for export about 950,000 tons.
But in the past, farmers often faced market problems for selling their rice produce. The reason is that most of the rice varieties are not expensive in the market, making it difficult to make a profit or pay for production.
In particular, the situation of rice mills in Prey Veng province is mostly lacking working capital to collect rice from farmers during the harvest, which makes the mill owners can not store and dry for processing. Hold the market on time.
However, the implementation of contract rice production between the farming community and the millers is also difficult to implement because the mill owners do not have enough funds to pay the community on time, so farmers are forced to sell to exporters. Go abroad.
