Mr. Men Vibol continues to be the Chairman of Svay Rieng Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee for the 5th mandate
(Svay Rieng): In the meeting of the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Svay Rieng province this morning, July 25, 2019, Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng province, was elected as the chairman of the branch committee of the Cambodian Red Cross in Svay Rieng province for the fifth mandate. 2019-2015) to continue the leadership of the provincial Red Cross branch.
The organization of the conference for the fifth mandate was held at the meeting hall of Building "D", Svay Rieng Provincial Hall, with the participation of Mrs. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, Mrs. Duong Vanna and the Honorary Members. Technical Officer, Head Office, Executive Committee, Youth Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, a total of 213 people.
In this 5th mandate meeting, the Cambodian Red Cross, chaired by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, appointed Ms. Duong Vanna as the Honorary President of Mr. Chum Hat and 9 Honorary Vice Chairmen.
The main purpose of this conference is to listen to and edit and approve the report of work activities and financial report in the fourth mandate and the implementation plan for the fifth mandate (2019-2025), to elect the chairman of the branch committee of the fifth mandate and to announce the appointment decision. Honorary Vice President, Branch.
On that occasion, Mr. Men Vibol was firmly committed to adhering to the seven fundamental principles of the International Red Cross and Red Crescent Movement, including: humanity, impartiality, neutrality, independence, voluntary service, unity and universality. .
Mr. Men Vibol added that it is necessary to pay attention to the implementation of the guidelines of the Cambodian Red Cross in order to successfully fulfill its humanitarian duties, maintain unity within the Branch Committee and accept consultation with the Branch Honors Committee and unite to solve challenges by Samri. High responsibility.
Direct the branch executive team to perform the tasks in accordance with the strategy of the Cambodian Red Cross, which has four core areas, including: disaster management, health and community health care, promote the basic principles and humanitarian values of the movement.
* Develop institutions and develop resources, increase ideas to raise funds from philanthropists from all walks of life to serve the branch's humanitarian work, and take care to guide sub-branches to perform humanitarian duties well in line with the four core areas of the Cambodian Red Cross Strategy. .
* Focus on continuing to expand the Cambodian Red Cross volunteers at the local level and strengthen community health education activities.
* Pay attention to expand and strengthen the activities of the Cambodian Red Cross youth in educational institutions as a model in humanitarian work in educational institutions and society.
Takeo Provincial Court President and Prosecutor Urges Judges, Prosecutors and Clerks to expedite cases
(Takeo): In a meeting with judges, deputy prosecutors and clerks on July 25, 2019, Mr. Aak Phalla, President of the Provincial Court and Mr. Chiv Chandara, Prosecutor of the Takeo Provincial Court, urged lower officials All advice is to expedite the handling of the case as soon as possible.
Both Mr. Phalla and Mr. Chiv Chandara stated that Deputy Prosecutors, Clerks and subordinates must pay attention to all cases, especially cases involving detainees. Prompt, fair and transparent trial and early verdict.
The Takeo Provincial Prosecutor also requested that all judges, deputy prosecutors and clerks working in the field of justice work on the basis of professional ethics for the benefit of the unit, especially for the benefit of the general public. Justice and impartiality, that is, to avoid any acts that should not be done to offend the dignity of the unit, affect society and make people lose faith in the judiciary.
During the meeting, the prosecutor also decided to hand over the management and maintenance of the exhibits, which were previously administered by the prosecutor, to the administrative secretariat of the court.
On that occasion, Mr. Aak Phalla also announced the meeting on July 19, 2019 at the Ministry of Justice under the chairmanship of Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, Minister of Justice at a meeting to discuss with the President of the court and prosecutors across the country about the situation. Unaccounted for detainees and find solutions to speed up the trial of detainees.
