Insurance premium in Cambodia to reach $ 260 million by the end of this year
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Nguon Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, confirmed that the number of insurance company premiums in Cambodia is growing rapidly, with a total gross insurance premium of 35% on average per year for the last 5 years. The latter will increase to $ 196.4 million in 2018.
She added that the premium of Cambodian insurance companies is projected to reach $ 260 million by the end of this year.
This statement was made by the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy on the occasion of her participation in the "First Insurance Day" organized on July 25, 2019 under the participation of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Director General. The Prime Minister, the Minister of Economy and Finance, as well as many other distinguished guests.
Ms. Nguon Sokha continued, "With the growth of the insurance sector in Cambodia, there are 31 insurance companies, of which 13 are general insurance companies, 11 are life insurance companies and 7 are private insurance companies." "Small insurance companies."
She said that there are also 1 insurance company, 3 health operators, 3 insurance risk assessment companies, 16 insurance brokers and 22 insurance agents.
She also said that with the growth of the market in 2018, all insurance companies will create 3,000 full-time jobs and 9,000 part-time jobs.
"I am very pleased to see that the insurance industry has continued to grow proudly with strong momentum," said Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth.
"This is a testament to the clear distribution of the fruits of national economic growth with the development of the insurance sector," he said.
"The insurance sector is becoming another pillar of the non-banking financial sector, and this sector is driving growth in many other areas," he said. "Obviously, insurance premiums can be used as savings funds in the banking system or as capital markets and other investments."
At the same time, the insurance sector has contributed to building immunity to cope with disasters caused by disasters, especially natural disasters caused by climate change, which is becoming an important topic for the region and the world. Mr. Cambodia is a founding member of the Southeast Asia Disaster Management Project, which is supported by Japan and the World Bank.
