Pursat Provincial Governor Solves Environmental Problems at Duck and Pig Farms for Kandeang Residents
(Pursat): Pursat Provincial Governor, Mr. Mao Thunin, on July 24, 2019, successfully coordinated to solve the problem of 13 families living in Kampong Krasang Leu village, Kandeang commune, Kandeang district related to environmental problems with bad smell. From Ms. Ke Chanra's duck and pig farm, which affected the daily life of the people.
After mediation directly from the provincial governor, the farm owner agreed to the request of the people, requesting to postpone the sale of more than 1,000 ducks in the farm for a month and a half to avoid the smell. Stink affects neighbors.
In the case of the dispute over the smell of duck feces, it happened many years ago until the third power, but under the family and extrajudicial principles of Mao Thunin, the parties to the dispute Both sides agreed to end the long-running dispute and return the lawsuit from now on. In case of non-compliance with the contract to stop raising ducks in the disputed area, the farm owner must be punished according to the law.
On that occasion, Mr. Mao Thunin also distributed handkerchiefs to the people and teachers who participated in each received a sarong and instructed teachers, especially the principal of Hun Sen Oum Primary School. Eap would like to raise funds to fill the school yard, in which he also contributed to the filling of the land.
After the completion of the coordination, the provincial governor continued to lead the team to inspect the construction site of a stone bridge across a river connecting Boeung Kranh village, Svay Luong commune to Kandeang village, Kandeang commune at a cost of more than 80 million Riels. Come through the Solidarity Flower Festival of the Kandeang District Administration, the working group to help the district, commune and the people there.
(Phnom Penh): As of the third week of July 2019, a total of 33,000 cases of dengue fever, including 33 deaths, the number of dengue cases compared to the previous week has decreased by nearly 300 cases.
This was confirmed by the director of the Center for Malaria, Parasitology and Bacteriology, Dr. Huy Rekol, told Fresh News on July 25, 2019.
"As of week 28 (the third week of July), a total of 33,000 cases of dengue fever have been reported, with 33 deaths. Compared with the previous week, the number of dengue cases has dropped slightly by nearly 300 cases. The health of the people continues. ”
In addition, the doctor continued, "We continue to strengthen the action to eradicate the tiger mosquito larvae in the clear water by continuing to campaign to eliminate all clear water, especially all unused water. The main problem. "But we have already applied deworming and mosquito repellent."
