Lower Sesan 2 Hydropower: Leave a trail for fish to return home
(Phnom Penh): The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia on July 24, 2019 announced the importance of the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower under the title "Leave a road for fish to return home." The following is the full text posted by the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia:
In early April, at the Lower Sesan 2 Hydropower Station, located along the Sesan River in Stung Treng Province, Cambodia, a large dam with clear water looks very beautiful. To the right of the dam site, there is a tributary that flows along the steps of the secondary dam and flows into the forest as a passageway for fish to swim back and forth.
This lane was created in the manner of a natural waterway. Waterways for this fish are built through natural canals. Both sides are stock forests. During the period from April to August and from November to December each year, the fishing season travels from the lower reaches to the upper reaches of the river. At that time, there were many fish swimming back and forth.
Mr. Yeang San, Deputy Director of Lower Sesan 2 Hydropower Company, told reporters that during the construction of the Lower Sesan 2 Hydropower Station, we strive to implement both development and environmental protection projects and pay high attention to Protecting the environment and reducing the impact on the environment, as well as providing green energy to the people of Cambodia and the green impetus for the construction of "One Belt and One Road".
Speaking of the waterway for fish, Nong Chukwang, the manager of the waterway for fish, told reporters that the waterway for fish was built under natural waterway conditions and depending on the surrounding natural environment, it looks like a natural river. This river is the route given to the fish back home.
The waterway is 2,900 meters long from the lower part to the upper part along the river. The largest difference in height is 26.5 meters, the bottom of the river is 4-5 meters wide and digging ponds to provide space for fish to rest every 800 meters. Construction of the waterway for the fish began in April 2017 and was officially launched that year.
He added that after the waterway for this fish to be used officially, the inspectors have to inspect the fish port on a regular basis, to be inspected twice a month. In addition, we are looking for a team of fisheries management experts and detailed research studies.
