Senior Minister Kun Kim Chairs a Meeting on Disaster Management in Kampong Chhnang Province and Informs Officials to Prepare for Rescue
(Kampong Chhnang): General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions as the First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDD), this morning, July 25, 2019, chaired a review meeting. Examine the disaster management work of Kampong Chhnang province.
The meeting was also attended by Mr. Lam Heng Huot, Deputy Chairman of the NEC and Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province and officials from relevant departments, the Armed Forces, local authorities and development partners across the province, 500 people.
Chhour Chandoeun, provincial governor, said that in the first seven months of 2019, the province experienced 36 disasters, including one drought, 29 gusts of wind and six lightning strikes that killed five people. 6 people were injured.
The provincial governor added that the provincial disaster management committee, with the support of the National Committee for Disaster Management, philanthropists, as well as in cooperation with the provincial branch of the Red Cross and the Cambodian Red Cross, responded in a timely manner to the families of the victims.
After sending greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the ceremony, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised and highly appreciated the National Committee for Disaster Management and relevant officials at all levels. Pay attention to both physical and mental strength, cooperate well and respond in a timely manner to rescue people in the past in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
