(Mekong): The water level of the Mekong River during the beginning of the first flood season from June to July is at a record low, but this situation is confirmed by experts. That will improve by the end of July. This is according to the report of the Mekong River Commission (MRC) that was quoted recently.
In particular, the water level in the Mekong River area in Vientiane, this year, between June and July, is below the average level up to 0.70 meters, and it is also lower than the lowest level in the year record. 1992 up to 1.36 meters from June 16 to July 18, 2019.
Rainfall was light on the Mekong Basin earlier this year. In the upper reaches of the Lower Mekong Basin in the major Chiang Sen Dam area, rainfall was minimal during June compared to other areas in the lower Mekong. The average rainfall in June was only about 67% compared to the same period in June during the period 2018-2018.
According to the MRC report, which shows the shortage of water this year, EDC would like to take this opportunity to call on all citizens to save on daily electricity consumption, even if there is no power outage. In any case, please join together to help prevent power shortages at any time.
