US sends warships to Taiwan Strait after China warns of war
Washington: The United States has sent a warship to cross the Taiwan Strait again after Beijing warned of the possibility of war if Taipei declares independence. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, July 25, 2019.
The US military said in a statement that the USS Antietam crossed the Taiwan Strait on Wednesday. The statement said: "US warships have sailed across the Taiwan Strait to demonstrate their commitment to freedom and openness in the Indo-Pacific region ... and the United States will continue to fly and "Navigate wherever international law allows."
This is not the first time that a US warship has sailed across the Taiwan Strait, although this has always angered China. In fact, on Wednesday, China again warned that it would use military force to invade Taiwan if Taipei dared to declare independence or any outside force such as the United States wanted to separate Taiwan from mainland China.
